61. 　I pulled the bottle Wakata had given me out of my bag.
62. 　The amber liquid inside the bottle caught the setting sun.\nIt sparkled as if there were another sun inside the amber.
63. "Until that time... huh."
64. 　The seal had been broken, and just a tiny bit was gone from the bottle.
65. 　Just a taste...\nThat was all it seemed to be...
66. 　I passed by the side of the amphitheater and walked along the path of cherry trees.
67. 　From here to Yume-no-Ukisaka, the cherry forest continued.
68. 　In the western sky, without a single cloud, the "redness" of the sunset's afterglow still lingered.
69. 　Twilight.
70. 　The time everyone would recognize as beautiful.
71. 　But when just a little more time passes, it becomes the hour called magatoki.
72. 　Magatoki refers to oumagatoki -- the hour of meeting demons. Just hearing the name, even a modern person would feel a vague eeriness.
73. 　Once again, I held up the whiskey in my hand to the sky where red still lingered.
74. 　The sky being eroded by blue was all dyed amber.
75. 　Beyond that amber, I saw a shadow.
76. "Huh..."
77. 　Beyond the amber liquid, I saw a human figure.
