71. Like a pendulum clock set in motion, Rin rode the swing.
72. Happily, she accelerated into the night sky.
73. It felt like any moment now, she would launch off into the sky.

=== lines=138 stop_reason=end_turn in=5409 out=3745 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. "Kyah!"
2. "Wh-what the...?"
3. Early morning.\nA woman's scream and the tolling of a New Year's bell rang out.
4. No, of course a New Year's bell wouldn't ring on an early April morning.
5. The clangorous sound of something bell-like being struck, together with a woman's scream, jolted me awake.
6. "A scream? That voice was..."
7. I bolted out of my room.
8. The scream had come from Ai's room.\nAnd that voice had to be Ai's, too.
9. "Ai, you okay?! What just happened?"
10. "Ah, ah, ahh... I-I'm fine... ow..."
11. It really didn't look like she was fine.
12. "I'm coming in. All right?"
13. "Ah, w-wait..."
14. "Wh-what is... this situation..."
15. Ai was on top of her futon, teary-eyed, clutching her head.
16. That much was fine.
17. The problem was the metal washbasin lying beside her.
18. "L-like I said, I'm fine... Why did you have to open the door..."
19. "No, of course I'd open the door. There was a huge crash and a scream."
20. "There's nothing to worry about... ow..."
21. "'Nothing to worry about,' my ass -- you're totally on the verge of tears."
22. "Ahh, it's been a while, you see. I got a little too enthusiastic and made it too big."
23. "Made it too big, huh..."
24. The washbasin on the floor had a single large dent in it.\nAbout the size of Ai's head, in fact.
25. "Don't tell me... before I came here, this was how you'd been waking up?"
26. "Ahaha... There are times I wake up with a normal alarm, too. During the first few days after you got here, I was waking up properly with an alarm, wasn't I?"
27. "So this is your custom Ai-only alarm clock?"
28. Looking closer, there was a string tied to the washbasin, and a hook fixed into the ceiling.
29. Both sides of the alarm clock had packing tape stuck to them.
30. It was a simple enough contraption that one look was all it took to grasp the general idea.
31. Pressing the button on an alarm clock will silence it temporarily, sure -- but that doesn't shut the alarm off completely.
32. When people go to turn off an alarm, they'll usually pick the clock up without thinking.
33. Lift the clock, and the string held down by the packing tape comes free... and the washbasin suspended overhead crashes down onto Ai's head. That was the mechanism.
34. "You have to go that far just to get up?"
35. "Don't look at me with such pitying eyes!\nIt's going to make me sad!"
36. "I mean, don't tell me you were doing this the whole time before I got here? This?"
37. "The Natsume family are terrible at waking up, you see... And it'd be a real problem if I overslept."
38. "Even so..."
39. "I know what you're trying to say. But it's embarrassing to admit -- without a device like this, I really can't get up..."
40. I let out a deep sigh.
41. "There, you're making that face again!"
42. "Of course I'm making this face, you idiot!"
43. "Waah, don't call your teacher an idiot!\nA-and you shouldn't call someone who's doing her best an idiot either!"
44. "I know full well the Natsume clan is bad at waking up.\nBut at the very least, I'm one of the ones who wakes up easily."
45. "In fact, it looked like I was the only one who came running at your scream..."
46. "I'm sorry. Waking you up with a scream isn't much of a way to greet the morning... I'll do my best to absolutely not scream tomorrow..."
47. "You don't need to do your best at that."
48. "But if I don't try that hard, I can't wake up!"
49. "I'm telling you, you don't need to do any of this -- I'll wake you up."
50. "B-but that would be an imposition..."
51. "You said you wanted to welcome me like family. Was that a lie?"
52. "Wh-what, all of a sudden?! Of course it wasn't!"
53. "Then don't think of it as an imposition. From now on, waking you all up is my job."
54. "B-but then all the burden would fall on you, Naoya..."
55. "Dummy, food and lodging is more than enough. Besides, cooking for one isn't much fun, but cooking for a lot of people is worth the effort."
56. "Naoya..."
57. "Waah, why do you have to be such a well-put-together kid?! At least let your big sister do her part too!"
58. "What are you talking about..."
59. "You've been protecting this house all this time, Ai. That's plenty hard work already..."
60. "Now come on, hurry up and get dressed."
61. "And by the time we meet again, be back to your usual solid big-sister self, all right?"
62. "Thank you..."
63. "What are you saying, dummy."
64. Somehow feeling embarrassed, I fled Ai's room.
65. Thanks to Ai, I'd woken up a little earlier than usual.
66. Today I could take my time making breakfast.
67. "The rich aroma of coffee."
68. "The sound of an egg sizzling in oil."
69. "The scent of butter melting into toast."
70. "Hey! Don't do some incomprehensible narration next to the guy who's grilling dried horse mackerel and making miso soup with fried tofu!"
71. "Haaah..."
72. "Come on, hurry up or you'll be late."
73. "Okaaay..."
74. "I wonder if she really gets it..."
75. "I hope she hasn't drowned in the washbasin or anything..."
76. "Oh, smells good again today."
77. "Yeah. Dried horse mackerel and miso soup with fried tofu."
78. "Dried horse mackerel and fried-tofu miso soup -- now that's a Japanese breakfast."
79. "Oh? Shizuku, you finally awake?"
80. "Naoya... the food has changed..."
81. "It's different food..."
82. "It hasn't changed. The food is exactly the same."
83. "But just now it was toast and fried eggs..."
84. "That was an illusion your narration created."
85. "An illusion?"
86. "That's right, a phantom breakfast.\nEat up and get to school."
87. "Are you still half-asleep, Shizuku?"
88. "Maybe I am..."
89. "'Maybe I am' -- you look plenty awake to me."
90. "It's just, what's here doesn't look like an illusion."
91. "Yeah, this dried horse mackerel and fried-tofu miso soup, they don't look like illusions..."
92. "They're not illusions -- they're the real thing."
93. "Huh? But just now you said..."
94. "Sheesh, don't look at me with such an anxious face. What I called an illusion was the toast and fried eggs. The mackerel and miso soup are real."
95. Shizuku still looked puzzled, but she slowly began eating the mackerel.
96. "I don't really get it, but... this dried horse mackerel is delicious..."
97. "That's good to hear..."
98. Shizuku chewed away deliberately. Bones and all... crunch, crunch.\nI couldn't tell if the way she ate was elegant or just bold.
99. Since I'd woken up earlier than usual, naturally I ended up heading to school earlier too.
100. There was still time before class, so I made for the art room.
101. Confirming the door wasn't locked, I casually slid the somewhat sticky door aside.
102. The dim art room, still too early for most students to have arrived.\nA faintly stirring shadow caught my eye.
103. "Someone in here?"
104. In a slightly loud voice, I tossed the question toward the shadow.
105. After the dry sound of something scraping against the floor--\nA figure emerged.
106. "It's just me..."
107. "Ah, thought so -- Toritani."
108. "'Thought so'? What do you mean?"
109. "Ah, no, you're the only one who'd be here at this hour.\nYou're the serious type, after all."
110. "'Serious type'? What is that supposed to mean?"
111. Displeased with my answer, apparently, Toritani pursed her lips.
112. "You're not here to hang out at this hour, obviously.\nAnd you don't look like you came to paint, either."
113. "Besides, what you're holding is way too big to be a brush."
114. Toritani was holding a broom.\nNo matter who you asked, she didn't look like she'd come to paint.
115. "What a stupid joke...\nAnd on top of that, 'cleaning = serious'? I'm starting to realize just how low Kusanagi's bar for 'serious' is..."
116. "If it were only an occasional cleaning, sure.\nBut when you clean by yourself every morning, isn't that serious?\nAnd tidying up after everyone leaves in the afternoon, too."
117. "H-hey, what are you talking about?"
118. "About your daily routine."
119. "'Every morning'?! I don't do it on holidays or Sundays!\nA-and how do you even know about that?! You, who show up right before the bell every single day!"
120. "How do I know...?"
121. "'Every morning'?! What are you even basing that on?!"
122. Maybe it was something she didn't want brought up.\nHer voice rose louder than expected, her face bright red as she pressed me for answers.
123. "No, sorry, sorry. 'Every morning' was just off-the-cuff. It's not like I've been watching you or anything. But just because I'm always cutting it close doesn't mean I always arrive late, you know."
124. "Whenever I showed up early, I'd see you in the art room."
125. "That there were times you came to school early... I hadn't caught that. My mistake..."
126. "It's fine, isn't it? Why be so secretive? It's a good thing.\nIf it were me, I'd be bragging about it."
127. "You and I are fundamentally different in personality..."
128. "Personality, huh... I see."
129. "What? That's a loaded way of putting it."
130. "You've got quite the attachment to this club, don't you, Toritani."
131. "Attachment? Well, I'm the club president, so of course."
132. "It goes back before you became president. The cleaning, I mean -- I feel like you've been at it since your first day here..."
133. "Wh-- how do you even know about that?!"
134. "Because I saw you."
135. "H-how?! Back then, you and I hadn't even exchanged a single word! Why would you have been watching me as a first-year on day one?!"
136. "Well, I had a bit of interest in this art club, you see... So I came to scout it out right after enrolling."
137. "Yumihari was Kusanagi Ken'ichirou's alma mater, and its art club was pretty well known. Even though I'd quit painting, I was curious."
138. "So right after enrolling, I came to peek in on the art club. That day, too, was early in the morning."

