76. I see.
77. If Shizuku is living her life believing that, then I'm glad.
78. "I see."
79. "If Shizuku is living her life believing that, then I'm glad."
80. "Of course I believe it."
81. "I don't like people who state the obvious."
82. "You may be right."
83. Shizuku laughed.
84. "Take care on your way out."
85. Within a great span of time, many people cross paths.
86. What's preserved in an album isn't the only past there is.
87. There are countless pasts that leave no record.
88. Shizuku and I both know that well.
89. And so --
90. ...A sign had been put up.
91. Even though up until just recently, it had been completely vacant land...
92. All the sign said was: No Trespassing -- Authorized Personnel Only.
93. "So they really did sell it... this piece of land."
94. The empty lot had been enclosed by a simple fence.
95. Not enough to keep a person from passing through.
96. But soon a solid iron wall would go up here too, one that outsiders couldn't get past, and construction would begin.
97. "Memories that have to be erased..."
98. Just as there are memories that must be preserved,\nthere are memories that must be erased.
99. That much is only natural.
100. I climbed over the fence and stepped into the empty lot.
101. Nothing had changed since the thing that stood here six years ago was taken away.
102. Weeds had grown.
103. Here and there, what had once been garden plants remained, left carelessly behind.
104. "At the very least, this..."
105. I scattered cherry blossom petals over the land.
106. They were the ones that had been pressed inside that album.
107. Not all of them, but I wanted at least some part to be scattered over this land.
108. There was no real reason.
109. Probably just because that's what she would have done...
110. Even if it was nothing more than a fantasy of mine...
111. She would have done the same thing I did.
112. That must be why the petals of the Yume-no-Uki cherry had been pressed inside that album.
113. "At this point, there's no way for me to know what she was thinking back then, though..."
114. I left the empty lot behind.
115. I probably wouldn't stand here ever again.
116. I went out to Sakuragahara Station.
117. It wasn't as if I had any particular errand, but around Sakuragahara you could get most things without having to head all the way into the city center.
118. For anyone living around here, it was only natural to check the Sakuragahara area first when something caught your eye.
119. I bought some things I needed for the new room.
120. Most of what I needed was already covered by things from my apartment, but a few odds and ends came up -- bookends, a small desk lamp, that kind of thing...
121. At the apartment I had a large bookshelf, and a fine desk lamp too.
122. But in the room I was borrowing at the Natsume house, those things were actually too big to be practical.
123. "Oh, Kusanagi."
124. "Toritani, what are you doing? Here to buy art supplies?"
125. "Ahahaha... that's part of it, but today I'm here for something else."
126. "Something else?"
127. "I'm treating these two to a meal."
128. "These two?"
129. "Who? More importantly, do you ever actually treat anyone to a meal?"
130. "I do that sort of thing sometimes, you know... This one's Komaki, and this one's Kosachi."

=== lines=147 stop_reason=end_turn in=6972 out=4061 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
