121. "Tomorrow... at school... huh."
122. After parting with Akashi and the others, I walked along with Toritani for a little while.
123. Partly because I had nothing in particular to do... but really, I'd just been following her without much thought...
124. "I ended up somewhere with no real reason to be here..."
125. "What now?"
126. Well, the obvious thing was to head back to the Natsume house...
127. "Hinayumi Beach, huh... it's been a while."
128. In this town you could see the sea from anywhere.
129. A sea that was always visible.
130. Which was maybe exactly why I'd never bothered to come out to the shore itself...
131. "Why did I even end up at the beach..."
132. The sun sinking toward the horizon...
133. Well, I suppose these things happen from time to time...
134. Though this coastline was hardly what you'd call beautiful, even being generous.
135. Apparently this beach, with its underwhelming scenery, was an artificial one built about a decade ago by hauling in massive amounts of sand.
136. Not that it particularly mattered...
137. According to the old-timers around here, up until about the prewar era, the sea used to extend all the way to the area around Sakuragahara Station.
138. The cherry hill you could see from here... just below Yumihari Hill, the sea had once spread out.
139. Most of this town had originally been the sea, most likely...
140. Maybe that was why...
141. That beach I'd walked along with my mother felt as if it had been so beautiful.
142. The sand pure white... the sea blue...
143. That's the memory I have.
144. Maybe that was around the time this artificial beach was being built...
145. Or else...
146. Maybe I've reshaped every memory of my mother into something beautiful...
147. The scenery of Hinayumi Beach as I walked along it now hardly deserved the word "beautiful."

=== lines=56 stop_reason=end_turn in=3015 out=1347 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. 　Muddied sand.
2. 　Muddied sea.
3. 　On the dimly darkening shore, filthy foam had collected.
4. 　I kept walking along this artificial coast.
5. 　Further on lay Hinayumi Coast Park, up on a rise.
6. 　The place with the cherry grove where Kusanagi Ken'ichirou had been cremated.
7. 　I climbed the steps from the sand.
8. 　From Hinayumi Coast Park up on the rise, you could take in the whole Hinayumi shore at a glance.
9. 　The sea that had looked so ugly when I was walking right beside it now, seen from this height and dyed by the setting sun, was terribly beautiful.
10. 　Some things only look beautiful once you're far away from them.
11. [Naoya] "As you'd expect... even the cherry blossoms are about to fall."
12. 　I walked into the grounds.
13. 　Cherry trees on the verge of scattering stood in rows.
14. 　Pressing on through the park, one came upon the cherry grove.
15. 　Climb further beyond that, and there was the municipal crematorium.
16. 　I walked steadily on along that road.
17. 　For an instant, I thought perhaps something had once again been\nspirited away into the dream that the cherry trees dreamed--
18. 　The great wind died in a moment.
19. 　The rustling of the trees vanished.
20. 　It was the very opposite of that twilight Yume-no-Ukisaka.
21. 　But this was not that cherry forest.
22. 　Just a municipal park where Kusanagi Ken'ichirou happened to have been cremated.
23. 　There was no mystery here.
24. 　And yet......
25. 　The cherry grove, and Ai.
26. 　Her figure gazing at the scattering blossoms.
27. 　Already out of reach, far away,
28. 　Cherry petals swallowed into the distance beyond.
29. 　Dancing up into an eternal sky.
30. [Ai] "K-Kusanagi?"
31. [Naoya] "Ai."
32. [Ai] "Wh-what are you doing in a place like this?"
33. [Naoya] "No... I just happened to end up here... What about you?"
34. [Ai] "I -- I..."
35. 　For some reason Ai's eyes were bright red.
36. [Ai] "Just... I was out on my bike, and the sunset was beautiful, so..."
37. [Naoya] "The sunset, huh..."
38. [Ai] "To run into each other in a place like this... what a coincidence..."
39. [Ai] "The cherry blossoms in this grove will be gone by today, too... so maybe it's not just a coincidence after all..."
40. [Ai] "No, it's nothing... nothing at all..."
41. [Naoya] "Somehow..."
42. [Naoya] "It feels like a lie that the funeral was only just the other day."
43. [Ai] "Yeah... it does. Like it's a story from a very distant past."
44. [Naoya] "Yeah, that's how it feels..."
45. [Ai] "You're right... the cherry blossoms fall... and spring ends, too..."
46. [Naoya] "The end of spring, huh..."
