55. 　And rain moistens the air......
56. 　And summer comes.

=== lines=145 stop_reason=end_turn in=4849 out=3240 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. Beneath the summer sky.
2. It didn't matter how small.\n
3. I picked whatever patch of shade I could find and lay down.
4. But the summer sun is merciless.\n
5. The already meager shade shrank faster and faster as the sun climbed toward its zenith, stealing it away.
6. The inner courtyard I'd wandered into.\n
7. The wind off the sea slipped just so between the buildings, forming a natural sort of air conditioning.
8. A wind off the sea.\n
9. Put that way alone, it sounds terribly poetic.
10. But wind funneled through buildings is really just what people call a "building wind," and in truth there's not a shred of poetry to it.
11. And yet it's precisely because this building wind lacks all poetry that it feels so cool.
12. Beneath the unrelenting summer sun.\n
13. I lay down in that little scrap of shade.
14. I'd made up my mind to nap for about an hour.\n
15. That was the extent of today's schedule.
16. As I stretched out, something odd caught my eye.
17. "That's..."
18. A man glaring at the wall of the chapel.
19. An outrageous man wearing a stifling black coat in the dead of summer.
20. Of all the sweltering things to intrude on my view... a nuisance of the highest order.
21. "What is that guy... even doing..."
22. Glaring at the chapel under the blazing sun.\n
23. A normal person would drop from heatstroke on the spot.
24. Whether it's willpower or just habit, I couldn't say...\n
25. Well, he's a man who pours his energy in all the wrong directions.
26. "What could he be staring at so intently..."
27. Nothing good ever comes of it when that guy takes something seriously.\nHis "serious" is more dangerous than anyone else's.
28. "Good grief, scheming again, are you.\n
29. That man never learns his lesson..."
30. How many times has he been suspended, how many times nearly expelled... a truly outrageous man.
31. "An outrageous man, huh..."
32. There are only two kinds of outrageous men.
33. Because, well...\n
34. it would be more than anyone could bear if outrageousness came in every flavor imaginable.
35. The wall he stared at caught the sunlight harshly, reflecting it back in white.\n
36. As if it were some enormous canvas soaking in the summer light.
37. No matter how long I waited, the man didn't move.
38. Seriously, isn't he going to keel over? I wondered,\n
39. but there was no need to worry about him.\n
40. He had the vitality of a cockroach. He wasn't about to die from anything like that.
41. "Hnnh..."
42. Sleep came for me the moment I lay down.\n
43. For now, I closed my eyes.
44. I woke to the sound of cicadas.
45. How long had I slept?\n
46. Not that long, I imagined...
47. In any case, the man was gone.
48. "So he went home, huh..."
49. Well, of course. What was he even doing at school during summer break?\n
50. He couldn't have had any particular business there...
51. "What a man of leisure..."
52. Not that I could talk... In truth, I had, however reluctantly, a proper reason to come to school.
53. Otherwise, I wouldn't set foot in a place like this.\n
54. Summer vacation was too precious to waste at school.
55. I looked up at the sky again.
56. For some reason a shadow blocked it out.
57. "A shadow?\n
58. No, this is... a parasol?"
59. I traced my gaze to the fence, where a parasol had been wedged in.
60. And there, on the far side, stood Hikawa in a straw hat.
61. Or rather... a straw hat?
62. "Hikawa?"
63. "It's hot, isn't it? Really, really hot...\n
64. It makes one keenly impressed that summer is almost upon us..."
65. "Why are you here..."
66. "Well, you know how it is.\n
67. Your kouhai little sister is always right there in your heart."
68. "I wasn't asking about your delusional fantasies."
69. "Delusional fantasies, is it...\n
70. 'Delusional Fantasy Kouhai Little Sister'... sounds like the makings of a new drama series."
71. "Yeah, in your head it can start as many times as you like.\n
72. Just don't let it out of your head. It's tiresome..."
73. "Yes, yes, I understand. But really, Senpai is always so harsh with Hikawa."
74. "Because from way back, none of what you say has ever made sense to me."
75. "'From way back' is awfully cruel.\n
76. Well, Rina has always been eccentric, yes, but she's never been incomprehensible."
77. "So you're aware you're eccentric..."
78. "Eccentric... well, yes, I'm aware.\n
79. But if anything, wouldn't it be more of a chuunibyou thing?\n
80. Like, the Night of the ZYPRESSEN..."
81. The Night of the ZYPRESSEN...\nAt those words I recalled the trees standing in the night like black flames.
82. "So? What's the eccentric one up to?\n
83. Wearing a straw hat under a blazing sun."
84. "Senpai was drying out by the water's edge, so I decided to observe from beside you."
85. "...You're not making sense.\n
86. What water's edge, for one.\n
87. I'm sleeping in the courtyard, aren't I?"
88. "As ever, Senpai has zero sense of location.\n
89. Right beside where you're sleeping is the pool, isn't it.\n
90. That's why we're talking through this chain-link fence."
91. "The pool?\n
92. Ah, come to think of it..."
93. I'd thought I was napping in the back courtyard, but come to think of it, right beside the back courtyard was the pool.
94. Sure enough, I could see the pool beyond the fence...\n
95. It seems the human mind has this way of blotting out completely whatever doesn't interest it.
96. I'd forgotten all about it.
97. Through the fence, I could just barely see Hikawa's back and her straw hat.\n
98. And an opened parasol had been hooked onto the fence.
99. I was lying within the shade of that parasol.
100. So this was why I'd been able to nap so comfortably in the shade, unbaked by direct sunlight...
101. "The parasol. Shouldn't you be holding it yourself?"
102. "No, Rina has her straw hat."
103. "Then why did you bring the parasol?"
104. "I thought I might use it, but it seems I don't need it, so there it sits."
105. Even as petite as Hikawa was, no straw hat could shield her whole body under the summer sun...
106. Before that, if she wasn't going to use it, there was no reason to leave it open like that...
107. "It's hot."
108. "It really is. Hot enough that a person sleeping out in the sun could turn into dried fish before he knows it."
109. "People don't dry up that easily..."
110. "Oh, but they do. Heatstroke is a frightening thing.\n
111. It comes on all at once, you know..."
112. "So they say..."
113. "It's true...\n
114. Even if you think you're fine, you can black out suddenly.\n
115. You have to be careful."
116. "You're well informed."
117. "Rina has low physical stats, so I've had a few experiences with it."
118. "Especially someone sleeping under a sun like this with drool running down his face -- that's dangerous..."
119. "I'm fine..."
120. "You're not fine. And to begin with, you shouldn't go carelessly baring such a defenseless face in front of other people."
121. "It's my face, isn't it..."
122. "That isn't something for Senpai to decide."
123. "Why not..."
124. "A sleeping face is the privilege of only those permitted to see it. It won't do for it to be released to the general public so casually."
125. "I have no idea what you're on about..."
126. "'Hast thou ever gazed upon the sleeping face of a friend? In an effort to know his true countenance? What, indeed, is the face of a friend one sees day by day? And wert thou not astonished at the visage of that friend?'"
127. "There you go quoting weird stuff again.\n
128. And you sure know some odd lines."
129. "Fufufu, as expected of Kusanagi-senpai. You always know the source of a phrase that tickles the chuunibyou heart."
130. "Don't call one of history's great figures a chuuni..."
131. "In any case, being able to see Senpai's sleeping face is the little sister's privilege..."
132. "What is that supposed to mean..."
133. "It just is.\n
134. Though, well, that privilege won't last forever, I suppose..."
135. "But until the very last moment, until I can no longer do it, please humor me in this little farce... ehehe."
136. Hikawa said this, for some reason, with a smile.
137. "Never mind that -- you should be using the parasol yourself..."
138. "Rina is fine. I'm the straw-hat little sister."
139. "...Look, you just said it yourself. Heatstroke comes on suddenly without warning, right...?"
140. "And you've had it before, haven't you?"
141. "Besides, Hikawa, you're--"
142. "...Hm?"
143. "Could you be quiet for a moment?"
144. "Huh? Ah, sure..."
145. A figure appeared beside Hikawa.

=== lines=144 stop_reason=end_turn in=6727 out=3866 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. That was...
2. "Rina... that's my line. What are you doing talking to yourself?"
3. "Ohh, this? Yumi, can't you tell just by looking?"
4. "No... I have no idea."
5. "Fishing, as you can see."
6. "But this is a pool."
7. "Yep. It's a pool, all right."
8. "Can you catch anything?"
9. "Weeell, that's what I'm investigating."
10. "Is it fun?"
11. "Yeah, quietly fun."
12. "It looks boring, though."
13. "What's this? Picking a fight, Yumi? Is it that time of the month?"
14. Kawachino's silhouette gave a tiny nod.
