54. [Makoto] "That kind of orthodox approach won't get him to slip up, though.\n
55. [Makoto] I'm pretty sure he knew he was being followed, too..."
56. [Naoya] "He's got sharp instincts. That guy...\n
57. [Naoya] Animal-like, or something..."
58. [Makoto] "Akashi-senpai has been investigating that church for quite a while.\n
59. [Makoto] Remember the balloon story that came up earlier?"
60. [Naoya] "Yeah, that one about flying into the sky with a sex doll balloon?"
61. [Makoto] "The sex doll was just decoration. It's classic senpai -- a bit of showy flair to distract from his 'real purpose.' The real purpose was to fly through the sky by balloon."
62. [Naoya] "What, was he actually trying to cross the Pacific by balloon like that balloon man?"
63. [Makoto] "Of course not. That flight was to observe the church as a whole -- especially the upper structure, which is hard to see from below."
64. [Naoya] "Observe?"
65. [Makoto] "He botched the landing and broke a bone, but they say he stayed airborne for quite some time. He was apparently floating for about an hour."
66. [Naoya] "He was up there that long?"
67. [Makoto] "That's why it became such a huge fuss. If it had only been a few minutes, no one would have even spotted him. Sounds like he really hung on up there in the sky."
