87. [Makoto] "'No, it's not that I have anything I can say for certain... more importantly, you still suspect Akashi is plotting something?'\n
88. [Makoto] Honestly, listen to yourself... you've mostly worked it out already, haven't you?"
89. [Naoya] "No, at that point I really had nothing to go on for a definite conclusion. It was truly just a vague hunch..."
90. [Makoto] "It's the same for me now. I still have nothing that would let me say for sure...\n
91. [Makoto] Only..."
92. [Makoto] "No, never mind..."
93. [Makoto] "Anyway, this isn't the time for pointless chatter. Three days from now is the camp, after all."
94. [Naoya] "Seems that way..."
95. [Makoto] "Aren't you coming?"
96. [Naoya] "Kawachino would hate that, wouldn't she?"
97. [Makoto] "That's not true. Yumi actually rather likes you, believe it or not."
98. [Naoya] "Kawachino? No, that can't be right."
99. [Naoya] "Well, I suppose so. From where you're standing, it can't be helped that you'd see it that way."
100. [Makoto] "But Yumi does want everyone to go together.\n
101. [Makoto] The whole art club. You, Kei, Akashi-senpai of course, and even Thomas -- she wants us all to go to the camp together."
102. [Naoya] "All of us? No, seriously, no way. She absolutely can't stand Thomas, for one."
103. [Makoto] "You've got no eye for people at all. That girl actually cares a lot about the club.\n
104. [Makoto] She understands well that it's all of us together that makes the Yumihari art club."
