143. [NARRATION] In other words, all I could see was an utterly ordinary landscape...
144. [Naoya] "What was he looking at... that man..."

=== lines=141 stop_reason=end_turn in=6121 out=3442 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. Akashi Wataru.
2. My association with him began when I entered this school......
3. a full two years and more of acquaintance now.
4. "An alien, huh......"
5. A genius whose thinking always went sideways of what you'd predict.
6. He hadn't been made head of Yumihari's art club for nothing.
7. His irregular circuitry of thought -- everything about him looked like nonsense, and yet inside him it was all strung together on a single thread.
8. He saw connections that ordinary people couldn't see, and conversely failed to see the connections that ordinary people did.
9. Different from that world-class genius of a painter, Kusanagi Ken'ichirou.
10. And different from Natsume Kei, blessed with absolute artistic aptitude......
11. If anything, in terms of raw artistic talent, he was inferior to them.
12. But Akashi had a gift of a different kind.
13. "Honestly...... when I entered Yumihari Academy, I was floored......"
14. Up until then, the geniuses I had known in my life were the two named Kusanagi Ken'ichirou and Natsume Kei.
15. Even those two alone were staggering to me.
16. To think there were people like that in the world......
17. And yet, at Yumihari Academy...
18. the density of talent in and around its art club was abnormal.
19. Why had this crowd all gathered here?
20. "For talent to be packed together in such a narrow space......"
21. Was that what people meant by this school's history, its tradition?
22. No, even across its long history, there could hardly have been an era with a concentration this high......
23. "I guess that's just how it is......"
24. When you read the autobiographies of great figures, you often find that, for some reason, talented people cluster around other talented people.
25. And on top of that, they get clumped together in the same region during the same period.
26. Whether that's coincidence or necessity, I don't know......
27. "Even so......"
28. I can't trace his thinking at all.
29. "No, the materials are all here."
30. "Probably, most of the materials are in place."
31. But I can't catch up with his thoughts......
32. "Damn geniuses......"
33. I stared out in the same direction Akashi had been staring.
34. What he saw out there, I hadn't the faintest idea.
35. If I kept at this, the sun would set.
36. Once night came, I wouldn't be able to see anything.
37. I tried to search for something, but couldn't find it.
38. Standing alone, various thoughts float up in my mind and vanish again.
39. "So Akashi's taking a leave of absence......"
40. I'd been sure he was being held back a year.
41. And in truth, he was always skipping class......
42. reasons for being held back seemed endless.
43. "But that wasn't the case.
44. It was just as he said once......"
45. "He was waiting...... he really was putting it off for the sake of something......"
46. "With that guy, I can never tell what's serious and what's a joke......"
47. "What was he waiting for?"
48. He was waiting until summer......
49. That much I can guess to some extent.
50. Indoor slippers, easy to melt down.
51. Even heated on a stove, in midwinter they'd harden right up again.
52. Working in the peak of summer would be far more efficient.
53. That's probably what the industrial fan is for, too.
54. Melt the rubber, dry it out quickly, and fix it onto that enormous canvas.
55. That's why he was waiting for summer.
56. But is that all there is to it?
57. If that were the only reason, he'd already had plenty of chances to actually go through with it.
58. Today too was hot......
59. Just this month there have been any number of days over 30 degrees.
60. There must have been days that topped 35, too......
61. He wasn't just waiting for summer.
62. Most likely, he was aiming at a specific day, some particular day in summer......
63. "He's waiting. What is this particular day?"
64. "Peeping, are we?"
65. "Oh, it's you......"
66. [Kosachi] "You've been showing up at the church a lot lately. Is Komaki your target?
67. If so, you're wasting your time. That girl wouldn't give you the time of day."
68. "No, she actually keeps me company in conversation pretty well, or so it feels......"
69. [Kosachi] "Hmph, I wonder why Komaki even bothers exchanging words with someone like you......"
70. "That's a harsh thing to say......"
71. [Kosachi] "You resemble him, somehow...... that's why I don't like you."
72. "Who?"
73. [Kosachi] "Wataru and you. You and my brother -- there's something similar about the two of you......"
74. "No, seriously, spare me that.
75. Being told I'm like him -- what kind of punishment game is that?"
76. [Kosachi] "You're alike...... the two of you."
77. "That's cruel......"
78. [Kosachi] "Wataru came by again today."
79. [Kosachi] "He hardly ever came to the church before...... honestly, what on earth is he thinking......"
80. "Meaning, even you have no idea what Akashi's thinking?"
81. [Kosachi] "Obviously. How would I ever know what that man's thinking? He's always sideways of anything you'd predict."
82. So even his sister can't read Akashi's actions, huh......
83. "You just said Akashi almost never came to the church before.
84. When did he start visiting it so often?"
85. [Kosachi] "Beats me...... I really don't know.
86. Ah, but before we started here, apparently, back when Wataru was in his first year, he used to come see this church a lot -- so I heard."
87. "Heard? From who?"
88. [Kosachi] "The Father."
89. "Ah, the Father who's not here right now."
90. [Kosachi] "It's not that he's not here. He's just on leave."
91. "Ah, so I've heard. And you're all working hard to bring him back, apparently."
92. [Kosachi] "Of course. The Father will definitely get better and come back."
93. I see -- she really does care about the Father, this one.
94. Or rather, these sisters do......
95. "Do you like the Father?"
96. [Kosachi] "Obviously."
97. "Well, sure. Otherwise you wouldn't be doing something as bothersome as being a sister."
98. [Kosachi] "To someone with no faith like you it may seem like a bother, but this has its own kind of fulfillment."
99. "Is that how it is, I wonder......"
100. [Kosachi] "You see, Komaki was helped by the Father. It's a story from long ago......"
101. "Helped?"
102. [Kosachi] "Yes, when we were children...... Well, thinking back on it now, it may seem trivial, and if I told everyone they might laugh......
103. But Komaki, and I too, were saved by the Father's words."
104. Something that seems trivial in hindsight......
105. So as a child, she'd been saved mentally by the priest here......
106. But needing to be saved mentally by a priest as a kid...... what kind of troubles was she carrying as a little kid?
107. [Kosachi] "So, you know, maybe I'm not really so devout after all -- maybe I just love the Father who saved Komaki......"
108. "What's the connection between Akashi and the Father?"
109. [Kosachi] "Well, there isn't much of one, is there? Though I don't really know......"
110. "No connection with the Father......"
111. "That doesn't quite seem to be the case."
112. [Kosachi] "Komaki."
113. [Komaki] "I could hear the sound of a lively conversation, so I couldn't help coming over."
114. [Kosachi] "It, it wasn't anything lively!"
115. "Is there a connection between the Father and Akashi?"
116. [Komaki] "Yes. Before we entered the school -- right when my brother was in his first year -- he apparently spoke often with the Father."
117. [Kosachi] "Huh? The Father and Wataru? What would they even talk about? A conversation wouldn't hold together between those two, would it?"
118. [Komaki] "It seems to have been about architecture. My brother, believe it or not, has knowledge of architectural matters, and apparently he often spoke with the Father about it."
119. "About architecture......"
120. "Ah, no, never mind. Go on."
121. [Komaki] "Apparently the architectural style of this church is exceedingly interesting, and their conversations really took off from there."
122. "Well, it is an extremely unusual architectural style......"
123. [Komaki] "Who originally designed it and when, when the interior was renovated, who did it -- all sorts of things like that, I hear they talked about."
124. [Kosachi] "I see. So that's why he was coming to the church so often in his first year."
125. [Komaki] "Yes, and I hear that at the time the Father gave him various things as well."
126. "Various things?"
127. [Komaki] "I don't really know either...... but I remember he was terribly excited about it back then. It's rare for my brother to show that kind of joy......"
128. "It's not rare for him to get excited. He'll go wild over a single rice cracker."
129. [Kosachi] "That, well, not really. At home Wataru doesn't get carried away the way he does outside."
130. [Komaki] "He isn't unfriendly or anything, but he does always seem to be lost in thought. Especially lately."
131. [Kosachi] "It'd be one thing if his thoughts were lofty, but they're mostly worthless...... honestly, why does he play the fool with such a straight face......"
132. In that respect, maybe I'm in no position to talk......
133. "So then, Akashi heard various things from the Father and received something from him?"
134. [Komaki] "Yes, something like plans, or blueprints...... I don't know the details......"
135. "Plans? Blueprints?"
136. [Komaki] "Yes, I wasn't actually shown them properly. I just remember my brother getting excited over them......"
137. Plans......
138. Blueprints......
139. Plans and blueprints that would delight that guy......
140. "Come to think of it, Komaki said something."
141. [Komaki] "About what?"

