31. And in the first place, why isn't Wakata-sensei here?"
32. "That man is not a morning person.\n
33. I doubt he'd answer his phone on a day off like this."
34. "That good-for-nothing..."
35. Only Akashi being hauled away...\n
36. things wouldn't turn out that conveniently.
37. Every single person present was called into a separate classroom and subjected to a barrage of questions that felt like an interrogation.
38. The interrogations seemed like they'd drag on a long while, but they ended abruptly.
39. Sparked by a single remark of mine.
40. "Just what were you thinking?!"
41. "Even if I told you what I was thinking, I don't think you'd get it."
42. "'You'?! Bastard, who do you think you're talking to -- a teacher!"
43. "Who knows. All I know is you're clueless enough to look at that and feel nothing..."
44. "You brat! To a teacher, no less! D-don't think you'll get off scot-free!"
45. "Scot-free? Are you stupid? Does that look free to you?\n
46. In market value, it's worth several million. No -- these days it could easily go for tens of millions."
47. "Wh-what are you talking about?"
48. "You'll show this to the top man at this school, won't you?\n
49. Tell him it's Kusanagi Ken'ichirou's final work..."
50. As I said this, I set that stack of blueprints and designs down on the desk.
51. "What the hell are you? Listen here!"
52. "Guhf."
53. "What's with that attitude of yours, you..."
54. "A-Ai..."
55. "Not 'Ai.' Natsume-sensei. How many times do I have to tell you before you get it?\n
56. This idiot..."
57. "Natsume-sensei."
58. "Please leave the rest to me. I'll keep this one quiet...\n
59. And please handle those documents Kusanagi gave you with care.\n
60. In monetary terms, they're worth several million yen."
61. "Several million? Not you too, Natsume-sensei, spouting such nonsense...\n
62. There's no way scraps of paper like these are worth that much."
63. "For now, please deliver them to the headmaster.\n
64. I've already contacted her, and she should be arriving at the school shortly,\n
65. and please don't forget to tell her these are 'Kusanagi Ken'ichirou's final work.'"
66. "Kusanagi Ken'ichirou's final work, you say..."
67. "I leave it to you, then."
68. "U-um, Natsume-sensei..."
69. "I leave it to you."
70. Ai declared it with a somewhat overbearing tone.
71. "To think that even facing a work like that, all he could think about was how to punish his students...\n
72. Just how withered can a person's sensibilities get... moron."
73. "Guff."
74. "You're the moron! What idiotic thing are you saying now?!\n
75. Do you even understand what you've done?!"
76. "I understand...\n
77. Of course I did it knowing full well..."
78. "You really understand?\n
79. What you did was trespassing, property destruction -- a full-fledged crime."
80. "Yeah, I know. I did it all knowing that."
81. "Hah... I see.\n
82. So that attitude of yours is a bluff, then?"
83. It wasn't just me -- every one of us did it prepared to be expelled.
84. There wasn't a single one of us who didn't understand what we were doing... probably... (Thomas is questionable, though).
85. "But it's a necessary bluff.\n
86. If I flinched and acted suspicious here, no one would believe that thing has any value."
