115. "Time?"
116. I looked at Toritani.
117. Toritani was floating on the water, looking up at the sky.
118. "Isn't it about time?"
119. "You should float on the water like me and look at the sky."
120. "Float on the water... and look at the sky?"
121. As instructed, I too floated on the water.\n
122. My eyes gradually adjusted to the darkness.
123. And then...
124. "Wow..."
125. "Ah, amazing."
126. "I see... you were waiting for our eyes to adjust to the dark..."
127. Floating on the water and looking up at the sky, though we hadn't noticed at all until then, it was filled with a sky brimming with stars.
128. "Since we're at it, I thought stargazing would be nice too...\n
129. Well, it's probably nothing compared to Rin-chan's countryside."
130. "That's not true. Being able to see this many stars is amazing."
131. I see, so this is why she had the lights turned off on purpose...
132. Even as compensation for the church renovation, isn't this too extravagant?
133. Stargazing in a pitch-dark pool.\n
134. Is it really okay for a school to let its students indulge in such luxury?
135. "So that's why I had the lights turned down, so we could stargaze while in the pool. Well, the fireworks will be easier to see this way too."
136. "Whew, thanks to that I'm stuck working overtime."
137. "Ai-sensei, why don't you get in too?"
138. "I'm your supervisor. If something happened in the dark, it'd be a big deal.\n
139. I'll keep watch from a spot where I can see clearly."
140. "Still, you could've worn a swimsuit, couldn't you?"
141. "Toritani... are you picking a fight with me?\n
142. Do you think someone like me owns such a thing?"
143. "But you only told us yesterday."
144. "Toritani, I'll say it again.\n
145. Do you think a single teacher supporting her siblings could scrounge up something like that on such short notice?"
146. "...Ahaha.\n
147. Sorry..."

=== lines=67 stop_reason=end_turn in=3238 out=1310 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. "Aren't Rurio-chan and Suzuna-chan getting in?"
2. "It's deep!"
3. "It seems to be a bit too deep for us..."
4. "Oh, right, come to think of it, the children's pool is a little shallow."
5. "Even so, we can see them so clearly."
6. "Well, stargazing is something you do while lying down, after all.\n
7. So the idea of watching them while floating in a pool isn't half bad... though I've never heard of it."
8. "You're right..."
9. Everyone looked up at the sky.
10. When everyone fell silent,\n
11. all that reached my ears was the sound of the water.
12. "It's quiet..."
13. "Yumihari Academy is pretty deep in the mountains, after all..."
14. "More on top of a hill than in the mountains. There are even apartment buildings nearby, technically..."
15. "But we're tucked away here... so the sounds really don't carry."
16. "It's a good thing tonight is a new moon... makes the stars stand out even more."
17. "Ah, right, when the moon is more waned, there's less light, so the stars show up better..."
18. "It's not something you get to experience often, so you'd better savor it. It's pretty rare."
19. "Yeah. Summer break's almost over, too..."
20. And for us in particular, this was our last summer break.
21. "It really is ending, huh..."
22. "It's just our summer... that's ending."
23. "Yeah... our summer is coming to an end..."
24. "Amazing..."
25. "Wow."
26. Fireworks went up.
27. And then more, one after another.
28. The stars that had been shining in the darkness vanished in an instant, as if startled by the sound of the fireworks and fleeing.
29. Fireworks blazing in the sky, seen from a pitch-dark pool.
30. They lit up the sky dazzlingly, faded, and were launched again.
31. Before long, no one spoke a word.
32. In the darkness, all that existed were the sounds and lights of the fireworks going up.
33. Everything else was drowned out.
34. Fireworks announcing the end of a midsummer's night.
35. It felt as though they might go on forever...
36. "Because what's ending is our summer..."
37. "Our finale isn't here."
38. Toritani murmured that as she watched the fireworks.
39. No, that wasn't it.
40. To put it more precisely, she was looking farther than the fireworks.
41. She was gazing beyond the end of summer.
42. Ah, I see... I thought.
43. The reason she had studied without fail ever since her first year.
44. The reason she was trying to keep me company as I studied.
45. It could only be that one thing.
46. "So you really... are seriously aiming for it..."
47. "Of course I am. This is my last chance."
48. "Why are you so fixated on doing it while you're still at Yumihari?\n
49. Not even pros can win that prize. You really think mere students like us can pull it off?"
50. "It's because I think we can that I'm doing it..."
51. Fireworks went up.
52. Their light illuminated Toritani's face.
53. Her gaze was full of strength.
54. "But for now..."
55. "We should make the most of our last summer, huh..."
56. There's no such thing as forever.
57. As a matter of course, there's a beginning and there's an end.
58. No matter how brilliantly its contents shine, no matter how beautiful they are... it ends.
59. The fireworks end too.
60. Just a few more shots.
61. Just a few more minutes.
62. Even the fireworks powerfully dyeing the sky
63. faded away into the silent heavens.
64. So, just for now...
65. Without thinking about the end, simply, honestly,\n
66. we enjoyed the fireworks.
67. At the end of summer...

