=== lines=143 stop_reason=end_turn in=5300 out=3570 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. After my schoolwork wound down, I set about cleaning up from dinner.
2. I'd left everything to soak for a few hours, but even so, tonight's dishes were a bit of a chore.
3. "I went a little overboard..."
4. Well, we did go all the way out to shop, so I suppose it's only natural I got carried away with the cooking too.
5. Meals with a crowd are fun.
6. And summer brings plenty of vegetables in season.\n
7. Naturally, in summer, vegetable prices drop.
8. When things are cheap, you can make dishes a bit more lavish than usual.
9. For fish at this time of year, I'd recommend flying fish -- cheap and delicious.
10. They're commonly called "hon-tobi" -- a term for flying fish caught from summer through early autumn.
11. Flying fish caught in spring are called "haru-tobi," while those caught in summer earn the name "hon-tobi" -- the "real" flying fish. As the name suggests, summer flying fish are something special.
12. Flying fish are low in oil and mild in flavor, but they make truly excellent tempura.
13. They're a pain to fillet because of all the fine bones, so it's a relief to find them already prepared as sashimi...
14. All you have to do is cut them into bite-sized pieces and coat them in batter.
15. That aside, summer is also the season for whiting.\n
16. Whiting is another fish perfectly suited to tempura.
17. Tempura made with seasonal ingredients is delicious and fun to prepare, but the cleanup is a pain, as always.
18. "Fried food really is a nightmare to clean up after."
19. Once I'd finished washing everything, I took some barley tea from the fridge and settled down in the tea room.
20. Pouring the tea into a glass, I opened the newspaper that lay nearby.
21. "Another tax hike? Is it really okay to raise taxes at a time like this?\n
22. Spare me from any more economic downturn, please."
23. At the very least, I'd like the economy to have picked up by the time I hit the job market.
