75. [Makoto] "Honestly, always causing trouble..."
76. [NARRATION] 　Unable to help myself, I pressed in on Toritani as she made a face like she'd had enough.
77. [Makoto] "Wait -- too close! Way too close!"
78. [Naoya] "But come on, you being Toko-san of 'The Moon Rabbit'?\n
79. [Naoya] There's no way that's not amazing. They were selling your stuff in a department store!"
80. [Makoto] "Getting sold in a department store isn't that big a deal...\n
81. [Makoto] The event coordinator's just going by their own taste, and they reach out to small studios too..."
82. [Naoya] "Is that how it works? No, but still, it's amazing.\n
83. [Naoya] Your pieces get carried by pretty famous sites,\n
84. [Naoya] and they're so popular they sell out immediately."
85. [Naoya] "This is way past the level of 'selling stuff on a handicraft site.'\n
86. [Naoya] That's not what you told me yesterday, is it!?"
87. [Makoto] "In the beginning, I really was selling through a handicraft site.\n
88. [Makoto] I wasn't lying... I wasn't... I just wasn't telling the whole truth..."
89. [Naoya] "And there's an official site, too... and it gets updated...\n
90. [Naoya] I've been camping on that thing to try and buy stuff, you know..."
91. [NARRATION] 　Suddenly, I hung my head.
92. [Makoto] "Wh -- what, why did you go all deflated all of a sudden..."
93. [Naoya] "No, hold on... are you really, really her?\n
94. [Naoya] Are you really Toko-san?"
95. [Makoto] "...Sorry to disappoint you. She's not the mature, dignified, composed person you imagined."
96. [Naoya] "No, please, forget I ever said that..."
97. [NARRATION] 　Before I knew it, I was holding my head in my hands.
98. [Makoto] "H-hey, what? Seeing you like this is way too rare,\n
99. [Makoto] I don't know how to deal with it, so quit doing that."
100. [Naoya] "No, but I gushed about Toko-san right in front of you...\n
101. [Naoya] And yesterday I said your pottery was pretty good, too..."
102. [Naoya] "This is too embarrassing..."
103. [Makoto] "Ah, no, well... don't worry about that...\n
104. [Makoto] I missed my chance to say something, or rather, I couldn't bring myself to say it. That was my fault."
105. [Makoto] "You have good intuition, Kusanagi -- you pick up on the tiniest changes right away.\n
106. [Makoto] But even though I was obviously flustered, you acted like you didn't notice at all, and I started to wonder if maybe you were just messing with me..."
107. [Makoto] "Ah, but then again, you can be strangely dense in weird places, too..."
108. [Naoya] "No, I was just too locked in on my assumptions. I never dreamed that a professional potter working that publicly could be right there next to me..."
109. [Makoto] "That's what I keep telling you, it's not that public.\n
110. [Makoto] And calling me a 'professional potter' is an exaggeration too..."
111. [Makoto] "Honestly, I just started it thinking it might help a little with tuition and living expenses.\n
112. [Makoto] That's all it was..."
113. [Naoya] "No, no, no. You're insanely popular, you know?\n
114. [Naoya] Search for the brand or the name and it turns up right away."
115. [Makoto] "It's fine, I don't need to... I'm not really interested..."
116. [Naoya] "You really didn't know?"
117. [Makoto] "Nope. Even the fact that people call my stuff 'Toko white'\n
118. [Makoto] I only heard from you just now..."
119. [Naoya] "Ah, then that piece the coffee jelly came in the other day --\n
120. [Naoya] was that actually one of 'The Moon Rabbit's, too?"
121. [Makoto] "Hmm... strictly speaking, no.\n
122. [Makoto] That was really early work, from back when I was selling on the handicraft site."
123. [Makoto] "At first, I was going to sell under the name pica-pica. Pica-pica means magpie. So I was planning to just call myself something like Sagiko, offhand."
124. [Makoto] "When I showed the master the piece and told him that,\n
125. [Makoto] he told me I should go with rabbit instead..."
126. [Makoto] "I should've caught on right then, but..."
127. [Naoya] "Caught on?"
128. [Makoto] "Sorry, just talking to myself. Both the name 'The Moon Rabbit'\n
129. [Makoto] and the name Toko -- the master's the one who came up with them."
130. [Makoto] "Do you know the foreword on 'The Moon Rabbit' site?"
131. [Naoya] "Yeah, I remember it well."
132. [Makoto] "Right. That was because that name was too cute and embarrassing on its own,\n
133. [Makoto] so I gave it a meaning to sort of dress it up... well,\n
134. [Makoto] I didn't just slap something on carelessly, though."
135. [Naoya] "So yesterday's packing work -- was that maybe not the pieces sold at Chimera, but..."
136. [Makoto] "Yes, they were mine.\n
137. [Makoto] The number of pieces the master sends is small; those are only sold in the shop."
138. [Naoya] "Now that you mention it, they were all wrapped up in packing material so I couldn't see the pieces inside,\n
139. [Naoya] and you did the paperwork downstairs... in other words, you made sure I couldn't see them."
140. [Makoto] "That's right. Sorry for tricking you."
141. [Naoya] "No, that's fine."

=== lines=26 stop_reason=end_turn in=2351 out=637 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
