20. "You haven't left. You're pretty far from Sakuragahara, sure, but you're still inside Yumihari City.\n
21. From where you are, rather than heading back to Sakuragahara, I think it'd be faster to head straight for Utagi Town."
22. "Utagi Town? Isn't that one station away from Sakuragahara?"
23. "Yes, that's right. But you've already walked more than that distance, so going back would be quite a hassle. It'd be better to walk from Utagi straight to Natsume-kun's house in Kootoha."
24. "Well, since you're giving me directions off a map, I suppose you're entirely right.\n
25. Got it, I'll head for Natsume's place. So, which way should I go?"
26. "Go straight down the road you're walking on now. That'll bring you out onto the main strip."
27. "Main strip? Is there something like that around here?"
28. "Yes, there's a district with bars, so once you've walked that far, call me again. I'll have things ready by then."
29. "Ready?"
30. I didn't really understand, but for now I did as Rin said and started walking with the highway on my right.
31. "Ha, ha, ha..."
32. "R-Rin... you..."
33. "I-I made it in time... haa, haa, haa..."
34. "You came all the way out here?"
35. "Ah, but I took my bike. Since it was by bike, it was quick."
36. Rin laughed as she wiped away her sweat.\n
37. There was no way that looked like "quick"...
38. "Ah, here, please take this."
39. So saying, Rin handed me a hand towel.\n
40. I took it.
41. "I figured you'd be tired from walking so long, so I soaked it in ice water and wrung it out. Was it maybe too cold?"
42. "No, I was just startled by how cold it felt the moment I touched it.\n
43. I've been walking under the blazing sun this whole time, so it's a huge help."
44. "That's good. If you'll pardon me, I'll..."
45. So saying, Rin wiped her sweat with a dry towel.
46. She must have sped over here on her bike in the middle of summer.\n
47. She was drenched in sweat.
48. "Ahaha, sorry. I'm all sweaty... do I smell?"
49. "As if you would..."
50. "I'm sweating quite a bit, aren't I. Nao-kun, if you keep walking around in weather like this, you'll get heatstroke."
51. "The one I'm worried about is the girl who sped over here by bike in this weather just so I wouldn't have to wait."
52. "I-I didn't really speed over that hard."
53. "Oh? You weren't standing on the pedals?"
54. "W-Well, I was standing on the pedals, but..."
55. "Thought so. Geez, if a girl in a skirt stands on the pedals, her panties'll show."
56. "Th-They will not! I'm not that clueless!"
57. Unusually, Rin raised her voice.
58. "The back of the skirt is longer, and... and I was careful not to let it flip up..."
59. "It was a joke. A joke."
60. "Was it? Now that you say it outright, I'm getting embarrassed."
61. "But it's not like your panties were actually showing, right?"
62. "Of course not!"
63. "It's just, I really was standing on the pedals in this skirt, so...\n
64. I thought maybe it was a little unladylike."
65. "It's not like you were born before the war -- something like that isn't unladylike at all.\n
66. More importantly, you must be exhausted, right?"
67. "No, not at all."
68. Liar.
69. "So, are you okay, Kusanagi-kun? No heatstroke or anything? You don't feel sick?"
70. "I've told you plenty of times, I'm perfectly fine. I'm much more worried about you and the groceries."
71. "Ah, the groceries. That's right, you were on your way back from the supermarket."
