123. Watching her laugh like that, she really seems like an ordinary girl.
124. It surprised me when she suddenly said "I really like you," but...
125. Even her expression at that moment had seemed like that of a completely ordinary girl.
126. Yet her joints were spherical.
127. Which meant she was not ordinary.
128. Shizuku's interest in 'The Footprints of the Sakura' was also bothering me.
129. I looked at Shizuku.
130. "Just as Naoya has been keeping things hidden from Rin, I too have been keeping various things concealed."
131. "Yes -- if speaking of them would bring Naoya harm, then I have no intention of telling you anything.\nHowever..."
132. "Perhaps I could tell you everything.\nAbout Rin and me... and about Sui..."
133. "If only I could be certain that nothing would happen, I don't think there'd be any need to hide it."
134. "I see, so there's a chance something might happen..."
135. "No, at present that possibility is quite low.\nUnless something serious -- something truly enormous -- occurs, Sui and I appear to be stable as things are..."
136. "Stable, huh..."
137. "Shizuku, does that...\nno, does it have something to do with Kuzu's power?"
138. "Kuzu, is it... Yes. Hearing that name somehow feels nostalgic."
139. "Really? It wasn't all that long ago, was it?"
140. "No, I would like to savor that taste again after so long..."
141. "What? What taste, after so long?"
142. "No, no, it's nothing. Well then, shall we head home?"
143. Dinner finished, I returned to my room.
144. There, for some reason, a magazine lay tossed on the floor.
145. When I opened it up, it seemed to be a special issue on Shizuku.

=== lines=142 stop_reason=end_turn in=6073 out=4041 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. [Naoya] "Why is something like this... wait, this is Shizuku, isn't it!"
2. [NARRATION] 　I scanned the hallway, scanned the window, but there was no sign of her.
3. [Naoya] "I thought Shizuku was watching me again..."
4. [NARRATION] 　For the moment, I flipped through the pages.
5. [NARRATION] 　Since it was a new magazine, naturally there were gravure photos of Shizuku I'd never seen before.
6. [NARRATION] 　In the magazine, Shizuku was smiling.
7. [Naoya] "Actually, that's an expression I don't see much..."
8. [NARRATION] 　Shizuku's expressions are sparse.
9. [NARRATION] 　Even so, she's become considerably more expressive than before.
10. [Naoya] "I wonder about that..."
11. [NARRATION] 　Shizuku is living as an ordinary girl.
12. [NARRATION] 　Everything is over now, so she's able to live under her true name.
13. [Naoya] "Come to think of it... she said her heart was something like a copy..."
14. [NARRATION] 　A certain genius artist.
15. [NARRATION] 　That person created her heart.
16. [NARRATION] 　And that genius, in turn, having gained her as an audience, came to know what human art is.
17. [NARRATION] 　That's what I've been told...
18. [Naoya] "It's still hard to believe, though..."
19. [Naoya] "A heart, huh..."
20. [NARRATION] 　I stared at Shizuku's photo.
21. [NARRATION] 　Come to think of it, when she first ate my cooking, Shizuku had cried.
22. [NARRATION] 　I hadn't expected that kind of reaction.
23. [Naoya] "Come to think of it, I never asked her why she cried..."
24. [NARRATION] 　No, that would've been tactless.
25. [NARRATION] 　Various things happened, and she ate my cooking.\nThen she cried.
26. [NARRATION] 　That alone should be enough...
27. [NARRATION] 　The Shizuku in the gravure is smiling.
28. [Naoya] "She really does have well-formed features..."
29. [NARRATION] 　I'd thought she was cute for a while now, but to think she'd go pro.
30. [Naoya] "Thinking about it now, maybe I let something precious slip away..."
31. [NARRATION] 　No, no, that's not the kind of thing I should say, even as a joke.
32. [NARRATION] 　I kept turning pages.
33. [Naoya] "This..."
34. [NARRATION] 　There were photos tucked inside.
35. [Naoya] "A swimsuit..."
36. [NARRATION] 　Several of them.
37. [NARRATION] 　Without flipping through, I called out loud on the spot.
38. [Naoya] "Shizuku, you're there, aren't you?"
39. [NARRATION] 　No answer.
40. [Naoya] "You're not there?"
41. [Naoya] "Even if you're not, I'm not going to look at the photos you planted."
42. [Naoya] "Geez... why would you pull something like this now..."
43. [NARRATION] 　Just then, Shizuku appeared from the window.
44. [Naoya] "You were in a place like that..."
45. [Shizuku] "Yes, I was in a place like that."
46. [Naoya] "You'll get bitten by mosquitoes hanging around outside."
47. [Shizuku] "I've already been bitten to pieces..."
48. [Naoya] "Ahh, jeez, just come inside for now."
49. [NARRATION] 　Shizuku came to my room through the back door.
50. [Naoya] "What did you want?"
51. [Shizuku] "I took some photos, and I really wanted Naoya to see them..."
52. [Naoya] "Are you an idiot? Of course I'm not going to look."
53. [Shizuku] "Watching Naoya since I came to the Natsume house, I thought maybe... but the reaction is the same as before."
54. [Naoya] "Obviously."
55. [Shizuku] "But it can't be helped, I suppose.\nAfter all, I've already been rejected by Naoya..."
56. [Naoya] "Huh? Why is it set up like I rejected you? That doesn't even make sense."
57. [Shizuku] "More importantly, something's been bothering me..."
58. [NARRATION] 　Shizuku's expression grew heavy.
59. [Shizuku] "You do regret it, don't you?"
60. [Naoya] "Regret what?"
61. [Shizuku] "You let slip that you'd 'let something precious slip away'..."
62. [Naoya] "Y-you're wrong, that's not it."
63. [Naoya] "I don't regret renouncing the inheritance at all."
64. [Shizuku] "Is that so...? I heard from Kei-niisan that Naoya regretted renouncing the inheritance..."
65. [Naoya] "Well, with that much money, sure, I do think it's a bit of a waste."
66. [Shizuku] "Th-then--"
67. [Naoya] "But listen. If I hadn't renounced the inheritance, and because of that Shizuku hadn't been in this house, I would have regretted it incomparably more."
68. [Naoya] "No, 'regret' wouldn't even be a strong enough word.\nI would have hated myself. No question about it."
69. [Shizuku] "Even so... I'm sad."
70. [Naoya] "No, no, there's no reason for you to be sad."
71. [Naoya] "Besides. Even when I say I regret it, it's really just a tiny bit.\nIt was easy money to begin with, and the amount was so absurd it didn't feel real."
72. [Naoya] "I don't regret it. Not one bit."
73. [Shizuku] "But in front of Kei-niisan and Ai-neesan..."
74. [Naoya] "I told Ai and Kei about the inheritance renunciation because it would've come out eventually. I couldn't keep it secret."
75. [Naoya] "So if I didn't pretend to regret it, it'd seem strange. There's no way you'd renounce an inheritance without a reason."
76. [Naoya] "If they suspected anything, they'd start prying, which would be a pain.\nThat incident is something only we need to know about."
77. [Naoya] "So it's just an act."
78. [Naoya] "'I renounced the inheritance to look cool!' If I look really regretful about it, then it's such a stupid reason nobody's going to press me further, right?"
79. [Naoya] "That's all it is."
80. [Shizuku] "Naoya really is... too kind..."
81. [Naoya] "That's not it. Besides, if you're going to talk like that, it was Kusanagi Ken'ichirou who gathered that money."
82. [Shizuku] "Forgeries..."
83. [Naoya] "E-even so, that was only possible because Kusanagi Ken'ichirou existed.\nHis achievement was the greater one."
84. [Naoya] "And, well, there wasn't a written will, but that was my old man's unspoken will.\nHe knew my personality well. It was a will just like him."
85. [Naoya] "'Carry on what I couldn't accomplish.'"
86. [Naoya] "That was his unspoken will."
87. [Naoya] "Though when I say 'will,' it was actually while he was still alive..."
88. [Naoya] "Either way, I, as his son, carried out everything he left undone, exactly as his will dictated. That's all."
89. [Naoya] "So if you're going to thank someone, thank my old man."
90. [Shizuku] "I am grateful to Ken'ichirou."
91. [Shizuku] "But I'm even more grateful to Naoya."
92. [Naoya] "Why me? Like I said before, I'm actually grateful for that incident."
93. [Naoya] "He called my work his epitaph."
94. [Naoya] "I'm grateful I was able to create a work like that..."
95. [Naoya] "So don't worry about it."
96. [Shizuku] "That's impossible... you did so much for me and I haven't been able to give anything back..."
97. [Naoya] "You did eat my cooking, didn't you?"
98. [Shizuku] "That doesn't even count as thanks."
99. [Naoya] "I'm saying it's fine, so it's fine."
100. [Shizuku] "But, but, if you say that, I don't know where to direct my feelings."
101. [Naoya] "Your feelings...? Come on, being that grateful just makes it awkward for me..."
102. [Shizuku] "No. It's not gratitude. I -- I--"
103. [NARRATION] 　There Shizuku's words broke off.
104. [Naoya] "You what? What is it?"
105. [Shizuku] "I -- I think I've said it before."
106. [Shizuku] "It's obvious. My feelings--"
107. [Naoya] "Your feelings? Really?"
108. [Shizuku] "Th-that's right..."
109. [Naoya] "Your feelings... what are they?"
110. [Shizuku] "Nnh--"
111. [NARRATION] 　Suddenly Shizuku's face turned red.
112. [NARRATION] 　This girl -- her face goes red while her expression stays blank.
113. [NARRATION] 　For some reason I braced myself.
114. [NARRATION] 　Because she also looked like she'd gone bright red with anger...
115. [Shizuku] "M-my feelings--"
116. [Shizuku] "Nnnh--"
117. [NARRATION] 　So red it showed on her face.
118. [Shizuku] "Uu... it used to be easier than this..."
119. [Shizuku] "Uu -- it's Naoya's fault too for not listening properly."
120. [Naoya] "Listening to what!"
121. [Shizuku] "Well, isn't it fine?\nCome, let's go to bed."
122. [Naoya] "Ah, yeah..."
123. [Shizuku] "I-I'm going to bed now."
124. [Naoya] "Right. I've got the bath running.\nTake one before you sleep."
125. [Shizuku] "Well then, Naoya."
126. [NARRATION] 　For some reason, Shizuku left my room as if fleeing.
127. [NARRATION] 　Come to think of it, I never did explain what I meant by "precious"...
128. [NARRATION] 　Well, it's not something I need to explain...
129. [NARRATION] 　But how do I really feel, actually?
130. [Naoya] "Back then, we'd just met, and we didn't know anything about each other..."
131. [Naoya] "But now, I know her well..."
132. [NARRATION] 　That's why I've ended up thinking, belatedly, that it was a waste.
133. [Naoya] "I mean, she's such a cute girl..."
134. [Naoya] "Well, no use crying over spilt milk..."
135. [NARRATION] 　I studied while waiting for Shizuku to finish her bath, then took my own bath and went to bed.
136. [NARRATION] 　In my sleep, I heard someone's voice.
137. [NARRATION] 　This voice... I feel like it isn't the first time...
138. [NARRATION] 　Faintly...
139. [NARRATION] 　Why have I forgotten about it until now...
140. [NARRATION] 　That's right.
141. [NARRATION] 　When I wake up after this kind of sensation, my head is always oddly clear, all the dregs of the dream washed away... that sort of feeling.
142. [NARRATION] 　That's why I never used to remember.

=== lines=128 stop_reason=end_turn in=5427 out=2947 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. "This isn't it..."
2. 　I sprang out of the futon at once.
3. "Kh... haaa..."
4. 　Shizuku was collapsed right in front of me.
5. "Sh-Shizuku!?"
6. 　When I shifted my gaze, I saw that bowl rolling on the floor.
7. 　Water was spilling out of it.
8. "Sh-Shizuku! You, you--"
9. "Kh... I-I'm fine..."
10. "There's no way you're fine. Why would you do something like this!\nYou don't have any reason to do this kind of thing anymore, do you?"
11. "I-I'm sorry... it's just..."
12. "For now, I'll go get some water."
13. "I-I brought water with me, properly..."
14. 　A plastic bottle was rolling beside Shizuku.
15. "Just in case..."
16. "Just in case nothing -- for you to do dream-drinking now, of all times!"
17. "I-I'm sorry..."
18. 　I picked up the bottle.\nThe seal hadn't been broken.
19. 　In other words, she hadn't drunk any yet.
20. "Shizuku, first, drink some water."
21. "Y-yeah..."
22. 　Her lips trembling, Shizuku couldn't manage to drink from the bottle.
23. "Drink, Shizuku."
24. "Nn... my mouth is shaking, I can't..."
25. 　Shizuku's color grew even worse.
26. 　There wasn't a moment to lose.
27. 　I took the water into my own mouth.
28. "Nn..."
29. "...gulp... gulp..."
30. 　I fed the water to Shizuku, mouth to mouth.
31. "Kfuh..."
32. "Shizuku, are you all right?"
33. "Th-this time, I was conscious..."
34. "You did the same for me before...\nBut that time, I wasn't conscious..."
35. "Yeah, that time you were out of it, so I panicked pretty badly."
36. "Back then, I was so full of regret. Why did something like that have to happen when I wasn't conscious for it..."
37. "Haha, come on. So you weren't joking when you told me afterward to do it one more time?"
38. "It wasn't a joke...\nI felt like I'd really been cheated out of something..."
39. "What are you talking about. Forcing water down you when you're suffering from the side effects of dream-drinking -- that's emergency first aid..."
40. "Perhaps it is, but... kh..."
41. "Are you still hurting?"
42. "Of course you are."
43. "It doesn't hurt at all... nnh..."
44. "How is that not hurting. Your breathing is ragged, your face is bright red, your heart's pounding."
45. "That's... that isn't pain."
46. "For that matter, why did you do dream-drinking at all? There's no need for you to be Hakuki anymore, is there?"
47. "You're right, but... I suppose I couldn't forget it..."
48. "The joy of sharing Naoya's heart..."
49. "When I was Hakuki... drinking Naoya's dreams was a joy..."
50. "But you were the one saying that what you were drinking from me were all wet dreams."
51. "It's true that they were mostly wet dreams, but there's no such thing as a purely lewd dream...\nInside Naoya's wet dreams, there was always love as well..."
52. "Since I was someone who couldn't receive your affection...\nbeing able to borrow it even just in dreams -- back then, that was my only reward..."
53. "What is that supposed to mean..."
54. "I loved Naoya... from before we ever met... and then, after we met, I came to love you more and more..."
55. "But I -- from the very start, Naoya never really cared about me..."
56. "Idiot. How do you get that I never cared about you?"
57. "I did all sorts of things, didn't I..."
58. "All sorts of things...?"
59. "I looked things up on my phone and tried all kinds of dirty things."
60. "That was to obtain wet dreams, right?"
61. "That was just an excuse..."
62. "I simply love Naoya..."
63. "I'm sorry... I know it must be a nuisance."
64. "But I couldn't erase the feeling itself..."
65. "This time too, I've caused you all this trouble...\nI'm sorry. Naoya..."
66. "I, I, really -- there's nothing I can give back, and yet\nI just keep causing Naoya trouble..."
67. 　Tears began to overflow from Shizuku's eyes.
68. "All I really want is to make Naoya happy...\nbut I'm an idiot, I don't even know how to make you happy..."
69. "I just keep being a burden.\nI can't give anything back to you..."
70. "I-idiot..."
71. 　I pulled the crying Shizuku into my arms.
72. "See, doing things like that, that make me happy...\nNaoya, you're too kind..."
73. "It's only ever me..."
74. "Idiot, it's not only you."
75. "Besides, the reason I just held you wasn't because it would make you happy..."
76. "Honestly, what a moment you pick to confess."
77. "I thought I'd been confessing to you all along..."
78. "It only ever sounded like you were joking."
79. "Perhaps so... now that I think of it, I feel the same way..."
80. "Ahh, geez, I don't know..."
81. "I'm sorry, are you angry?"
82. "Of course I'm angry."
83. "I'm sorry."
84. "I am angry. Because, you see..."
85. "I always thought that when I confessed to someone, I'd definitely do it myself, first."
86. "And that it would be, without fail, just once in my life."
87. "I'd made up my mind and lived by that."
88. "That sounds just like you..."
89. "You know the Kusanagi clan, so you understand.\nOur bloodline is single-minded in love."
90. "Which is why someone like me isn't needed, is that it."
91. "As if that could possibly be true..."
92. 　I held Shizuku tightly.
93. "You and I -- it's not like we just happened to meet each other recently.\nThat's not what we are..."
94. "At least, for me, that's how it is...\nI owe Kusanagi Naoya a debt I couldn't repay in a whole lifetime."
95. "But as Shizuku, it's only been a short while since we met..."
96. "Even as Shizuku, we've been together nearly half a year now.\nThough the time hasn't been as intense as it was back then..."
97. "Yes -- back then, the time truly was intense.\nI was very happy..."
98. "So I wanted to return that happiness to the Naoya who gave it to me...\nbut I couldn't do anything..."
99. "That's not true..."
100. "No, I think that a debt like this can only be repaid with money, or something like it."
101. "That's why I started working."
102. "I did lots of CMs and variety shows, things that would make money..."
103. "I was good at emptying my heart... so acting comes fairly easy to me."
104. "What the hell...\nDon't tell me you became an actress in order to pay me back?"
105. "It's not a matter of 'in order to.'\nFor me, that's the whole of the rest of my life."
106. "Someday, I want to give everything back to Naoya."
107. "Idiot..."
108. "What do you mean, idiot -- I'm doing my very best in my own way!"
109. "There's no way I could accept that kind of money..."
110. "I'll force you to accept it."
111. "I absolutely won't."
112. "Then--!"
113. "Then?"
114. "Then what am I supposed to do with these feelings of mine!"
115. "From the person I love most, I've only ever received help. I can't do anything at all for the person I love."
116. "What am I supposed to do with feelings like that!"
117. 　After a brief silence, I opened my mouth.
118. "Then, how about this?"
119. "It's something you're trying to repay over the course of a whole lifetime, right?\nIn that case..."
120. "Give me the thing that's most precious to you."
121. "The thing most precious to me?"
122. "Yeah. If you give me that, it'll be enough."
123. "What is the thing most precious to me?"
124. "It's what Kusanagi Ken'ichirou, Natsume Ai, Natsume Kei, and Misakura Rin gave you."
125. "And, of course, what I gave you as well..."
126. 　I drew Shizuku's face close to mine.
127. "Your heart..."
128. 　Our lips met.

=== lines=142 stop_reason=end_turn in=5463 out=3748 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. Me and Shizuku.
2. It's late to say it now, but that day--
3. Where we met was not Yume-no-Ukisaka, with the cherry blossoms falling.
4. That was a reunion.
5. Or perhaps my first meeting with Natsume Shizuku.
6. Something like that.
7. Her name was "Shizuku."
8. Write it in hiragana and you get "shizuku."
9. Reverse that and you get "kuzushi."
10. But there was one character in it she hated.
11. It was "shi."
12. "Shi" calls to mind "shi"--death.
13. At that time, what she least wanted to acknowledge was the death of a certain man.
14. That man had treasured Shizuku.
15. No, he had always treasured not only Shizuku but every one of the Natsume family.
16. Shizuku could not accept the death of a man like that.
17. So she stripped the "shi" from "kuzushi."
18. Kuzu.
19. At first she called herself Kusanagi Kuzu.
20. What I'm about to tell is the somewhat long story of Kuzu and me, back then.
21. But this story is very, very important.
22. "A splendid derangement of epitaphs."
23. That's what he used to say.
24. "A Nice Derangement of Epitaphs."
25. Yes--this is the story of a certain artist's epitaph.
26. A wonderful, wonderful derangement.
27. The derangement of an epitaph.
28. A tale of the past.
29. It was a certain winter's day.
30. The day after Kusanagi Ken'ichirou returned to Japan and was rushed into hospital.
31. I was standing in his hospital room.
32. "Yo, son. You doing all right?"
33. "Yeah, maybe I am. At least better than you are."
34. "Calling your own father 'you' like that. What a hopeless brat I raised."
35. "Well, that's what happens when you abandon your kid."
36. "Abandonment? What are you talking about. It was a top-class elite education, wasn't it?"
37. "When it comes to painting, sure. Everything else was left to rot."
38. "I taught you everything else properly too. 'Learn by watching my back!'--like that."
39. "The only thing I learned is that your back is hunched."
40. "That's not good. Watch your posture."
41. "Right. I'll be careful not to end up hunched over like you. So? What did you call me here for?"
42. "Ah, that. I don't have long left."
43. "I figured as much..."
44. "You noticed?"
45. "Your hatred of hospitals was legendary."
46. "So when you suddenly come home and check yourself in for the long haul, it doesn't exactly sound like good news..."
47. "I see. Well, that means my parenting wasn't wrong after all?"
48. "What? You were training me to sense my parent's death or something?"
49. "No one does that."
50. "I meant that you can properly take it when your one and only blood kin leaves this world."
51. "I loved my mother. Honestly, your death isn't that much of a shock."
52. "Ouch."
53. "Besides, I've been watching how you work all along. You weren't asking for a long life, were you?"
54. "Ah--about that. It's a delicate matter. I'd figured on living another few years. Maybe another ten."
55. "Then you should have gone in for a check-up."
56. "If I went in for a check-up I'd end up sick, wouldn't I."
57. "That's not how it works. What kind of grasp of the world do you have?"
58. "It's a real thing. Quantum mechanics, was it? Nothing is fixed until you observe it, or something. In other words, if you don't get checked, whether you're sick or not is only a probability."
59. "Are you an idiot. Don't just make things up."
60. "It's not made up. I am an idiot, after all."
61. "You, an idiot..."
62. I let my gaze wander around the hospital room.
63. As always, mountains of books.
64. "You brought a load of insanely difficult books all the way to the hospital, huh. What's this one by your pillow? Philosophy? Math?"
65. "No idea. It's too hard, I can't follow it."
66. "Reading even in the hospital, huh."
67. "What? You've got that 'and you don't even have long to live' look on your face."
68. "That's not what I meant..."
69. "Ah, but I'm properly reading books about the afterlife too, you know."
70. "What do you mean, books about the afterlife--like 'The World You Don't Know' or something?"
71. "A little different. I'm reading the Lotus Sutra and such."
72. "The Lotus Sutra?"
73. "Yeah. I want one of those, too--'a green paper reduced-mandala about the size of a postcard folded in four,' that lets you go anywhere on 'this imperfect Fourth-Dimensional Fantasy Galactic Railroad.'"
74. "The hell was that... Anyway, in 'Night on the Galactic Railroad' the paper Giovanni hands to the conductor is only described as 'a green paper about the size of a postcard folded in four.' Where do you get 'reduced-mandala' from?"
75. "Oh? You picked up on 'Night on the Galactic Railroad' being the source from just that?"
76. "'Galactic Railroad' only means either the pachinko machine or the story."
77. "Still, impressive. Remembering every word of your dad's favorite story--that's something."
78. "It's not every word. The ticket scene is just striking, so I remembered it."
79. "Still, why the Lotus Sutra?"
80. "Well, it's not exactly out of nowhere, but when you're told your days are numbered, you've got to memorize a sutra or two, right?"
81. "As they say, 'the nenbutsu is your fare.'"
82. "What's with that gloomy face--you're going to drag me down too."
83. "Not my problem. I only came because you called me. More importantly, what's this about? You didn't drag me out here for stupid chatter, did you?"
84. "Of course not. I called you for something more important."
85. "Here. All of this goes to you."
86. Ken'ichirou tossed something at me.
87. "What is this... A bankbook?"
88. "Your inheritance."
89. "Are you stupid? An inheritance--you're not even dead yet."
90. "Apparently gifts before death get taxed less."
91. "No, no, that's for gradual gifting over ten or twenty years. Hand over a lump like this and they'll take a ridiculous tax off the top."
92. "You're pretty well-informed for a kid."
93. "This is the second time I've received inheritance tax paperwork... All I ever accumulate is lousy experience."
94. "Yeah, well, I don't get gift tax rules. The upper limits change all the time depending on when."
95. I took the bankbook that had been tossed at me.
96. "So, how much is in--"
97. "Wait, what?! This amount! You're off by a digit! It's over eight hundred million! Nearly nine hundred million yen!"
98. "It's all yours. Take it home."
99. "W-what's this supposed to mean?"
100. "You went to America and never came home all that time because you had a purpose, and you were saving up money for it. Right?"
101. "It doesn't add up. This is money you were saving with a purpose."
102. "Well, roughly."
