30. "A work...... how'd you figure that out?"
31. "Was I wrong? It was just a feeling......"
32. "No, you're pretty much on the mark."
33. "I love Ken'ichirou's work.\nAnd Naoya's too......"
34. "My work? You wouldn't know anything about it, would you?"
35. "Mm-mm. I used to live in Japan too. I know Naoya's last work."
36. "My last work?"
37. "Yeah, it's a wonderful painting. 'Sakura Day Rhapsody.' If it were now, I think I could understand the meaning of that painting even better."
38. "'If it were now' -- what's that supposed to mean?"
39. "Nothing. Never mind. For now, let's go home."
40. "Well then, dinner is over."
41. "You didn't eat any of it, though."
42. "Right. So now I'll procure tonight's main course."
43. "...... What's that supposed to mean?"
44. "So then, Naoya, what sort of thing shall we do tonight to work up your libido?"
45. "You idiot, how many times do I have to tell you we don't need to do anything like that!"
46. "In other words, Naoya, you won't even give me my dinner."
47. "Hey, I let you have my dreams, but why does it have to be a wet dream? Any old dream would do, right?"
48. "Meals ought to be tasty!"
49. "Since when are wet dreams tasty?!"
50. "It's not that they're delicious, but wet dreams are the easiest to swallow."
51. "Why the hell are wet dreams the easiest to swallow......"
52. "To be precise, wet dreams aren't the easiest. Better still would be for Naoya to have a happy dream -- those would be easier to swallow."
53. "Then give me one of those, dammit."
54. "Until Kuzu swallows it, I can't tell what kind of dream it is.\nIn other words, I don't know what sort of dream it is until I've swallowed it."
55. "If I were to swallow a nightmare, in my current state I'd likely be in a very dangerous condition."
56. "It's not that I've completely lost my heart. Well, from Naoya's point of view I may seem short on expression, but even so, Kuzu does have feelings."
57. "That much I sort of get. You just don't show it on your face -- you've got emotions all right."
58. "Your face went red the other day."
59. "Ah, ah, that -- that was, right, when we were talking about wet dreams, wasn't it?\nOf course I'd blush......"
60. "How come?"
61. "Sh-shame play, is it!? \nW-well, if that gets Naoya excited, then I suppose it's fine......"
62. "How does this turn into shame play?"
63. "W-well, think about it.\nA wet dream so intense that Naoya has to masturbate to it. \nAnd I take all of that in."
64. "Huh? Th-that means?"
65. "I-I wasn't masturbating, all right......! It's purely in the sense of a libido great enough to make Naoya masturbate."
66. "Oh, that's what you meant......"
67. "It is, after all, the energy that keeps me alive, so it would be a waste to have it dissipated that way."
68. "Th-though, that it feels incredibly good is...... certain."
69. Uncharacteristically, Kuzu answered haltingly, her face bright red.
70. Th-this is......
71. "Well then, about how much has that filled me up?"
72. "That was an act?! Don't just snap back to business as usual!"
73. "It isn't......"
74. "If I don't say something like that, Kuzu gets embarrassed too, when things are embarrassing...... I-I mean, even I do, you know...... uh......"
75. "Eh? So then--"
76. "How was that just now?"
77. "That's an act again?!"
78. "You may take it however you wish. As far as I'm concerned, so long as Naoya has proper wet dreams, that's fine."
79. "You succubus!"
80. "Succubus...... succubus......"
81. "You look everything up on your phone, huh......"
82. "My Japanese isn't very good......"
83. That night, unusually for me, I had a dream.
84. Meeting Nakamura Shouichi had probably left a bad taste.
85. I dreamed of the past -- of my mother being taken away by Nakamura Shouichi.
86. Which was, naturally, a nightmare.
87. My heart felt like it was being torn apart with grief.
88. There was the sound of someone collapsing at my bedside.
89. I sat up at once.
90. None of my usual morning drowsiness.\nWhich meant......
91. Before my eyes, Kuzu had fallen.
92. "Kuzu!"
93. Even calling her name got no response.\nShe seemed to be unconscious.
94. I lifted her into my arms.
95. "Kuzu! Are you all right!"
96. I held Kuzu in my arms.
97. She was faintly breathing.
98. "Damn it, did you swallow the nightmare......"
99. Kuzu's lips moved faintly.
100. "What is it? Kuzu?"
101. No voice came out.
102. I hurriedly filled a cup with water and brought it to Kuzu's mouth.
103. "Haa, haa......"
104. All she managed was a labored sound of breath; she wouldn't drink.
105. "Damn it, sorry, Kuzu!"
106. I took the water into my own mouth.\nAnd then......
107. I passed it, mouth to mouth, into Kuzu's.
108. Bad dreams dissolve in ordinary water. That's what my old man had said.
109. Making an unconscious person drink water is dangerous, but this is the way to handle a dream-swallower's attack.
110. I took a second mouthful.\nAt that moment--
111. "What was that just now?"
112. "That was definitely Rin......"
113. The figure was my childhood friend, Misakura Rin.
114. Long ago, I had cut ties with her.\nWhy would her young image flash back to me at a moment like this?
115. "No, this memory......"
116. "Ke-hoh, ke-hoh."
117. Kuzu coughed.\nHad water gotten into her windpipe?
118. I tended to her.
119. "I have no excuse."
120. "That's my line. I promised the old man, and yet I put you in danger."
121. "No. I only had to spit it out right away.\nIt's my fault for not spitting it out."
122. "That's not true."
123. "But, thank you."
124. "You've saved me again. I'm always being saved."
125. "I don't know about the old man, but I don't think that's true for me."
126. "It very much is true! \nHow can I ever repay you now? I can't think of a way!"
127. "Like I keep telling you, it's fine......"
128. "Uu......, how can I ever repay you......"
129. "Naoya? W-would you make me your sex slave?"
130. "Wh-what are you suddenly blurting out?!"
131. "I see...... So no matter what, you won't let me pay with my body."
132. "Then, would it be money?"
133. "Money? Ah, that's fine. I've got a huge inheritance, so money isn't a problem."
134. "Really?"
135. "Liar......"
136. "Naoya, you're kind. Really, just as I heard."
137. "Just as you heard? Huh? Don't tell me the old man said something like that?"
138. "No. Ken'ichirou only ever says, Naoya's an idiot, he's an idiot. It's sad how he took after me and turned into an idiot. He should've taken after Mizuna instead, oh, awful, awful. I don't need a son like that. That's all he says."
139. "That guy -- I'll kill him!"
140. "But if being an idiot like Ken'ichirou means anything, it means you're kind."
141. "No, it doesn't. That guy really is an idiot."
142. "Father and son say the same things about each other."
143. "Well, he is an idiot. His behavior is all over the place, and he only says stupid stuff."
144. "Ah, you really do say the same thing."
145. "So that's the sort of thing he was saying! I'm really going to kill him!"
146. "In any case, that Naoya is kind is something I heard from a distant friend.\nShe called you an artist of the Sakura......"

