33. [Naoya] "You'd know, wouldn't you, learned Friedman? About the 'Nine Aspects of Death.'"
34. [Friedman] "-- !? The 'Nine Aspects of Death'......"
35. [Akashi] "W-what's this 'kusouzu' thing?"
36. [Friedman] "Heh heh heh, I see -- indeed, a convincing concept."
37. Friedman, who rarely laughs, gives a small laugh.
38. [Naoya] "How about it? As a curator at the Moore Foundation?"
39. [Friedman] "More than sufficient. As long as it clears the technical bar as a forgery, no problems."
40. [Naoya] "Glad to hear it. Hearing that from a pro is reassuring."
