137. [Naoya] "Now then, in that spirit -- after looking at a photograph of the first piece, 'The Reclining Sakura,' take a look at this."
138. [Naoya] "This is the Seven Aspects, part two: 'The Sakura of Esou.'"
139. I remove the veil covering the canvas.
140. [Naoya] "For the second, I made it a sakura whose image is that of decay progressed, of skin festered, split, and flesh laid bare......"
