14. [Friedman] "Yes. You've already used a week. You're seriously behind schedule."
15. [Naoya] "I'll pull all-nighters."
16. [Friedman] "Won't the quality suffer from no sleep?"
17. [Naoya] "Well, I've spent all this time not painting. If I channel it all into these two weeks, it should be fine."
18. [Friedman] "Hmph. Why on earth you ever broke your brush is truly beyond me."
19. [Friedman] "Exactly as I said. You took up the brush to help someone out, and yet...... to think you could paint this provocatively."
20. [Friedman] "It's a painting where the painter's fighting spirit is laid bare."
21. [Naoya] "Really? Well, that's good. Without passion, a painting can't strike anyone's heart."
22. [Friedman] "Hmph. You two really are alike.\nThe way you can put on such a dissembling attitude......"
23. [Naoya] "Come on, only two weeks left. Until the negotiations with the Nakamura family, I'll give it everything I've got."
