25. [Akashi] "I'll give it my all, too!"
26. [NARRATION] Day after day, I kept painting.
27. [NARRATION] The stray thoughts that welled up each time I took up the brush.
28. [NARRATION] All those stray thoughts, from a certain point on, faded away with the passing of the days.
29. [NARRATION] Each stroke of the brush honed everything sharper.\nA sensation as though every wasted thing were being erased from my mind.
30. [NARRATION] My body becoming the brush, my heart becoming the canvas.\nAnd everything becoming one.
31. [NARRATION] The brush is flowing.
