30. "We're both idiots."
31. "What, only just noticed? Idiots, huge idiots, hopeless idiots."
32. "That's why we teamed up, right?"
33. "No mistake there."
34. "Next time we meet will be after winter break."
35. "Yep, that's right. Third term."
36. "See ya then, Akashi."
37. "Yeah, well then, comrades of Yamamotoyama!\nFarewell!"
38. And with that, Akashi vanished.
39. Comrades of Yamamotoyama, he says...... I'm the only one here......
40. After that, my old man lived on for about three months.
41. He was pretty spirited right up until the day he died.
42. His will was:
43. Tell everyone that my life was an unhappy one,\nso there is no need to worry.
44. Bless me in my death! See me off with smiles!
45. -- some ridiculous thing along those lines.
46. Well, I think it was a fitting end for him.
47. The beginning of April.
48. We finished his funeral.
49. In a forest where cherry blossoms bloomed, he became bones.
50. No -- rather, because he was a man who had painted so extraordinary a cherry blossom, it was only right that he turn to ash beneath the most ordinary cherry blossoms of all.
51. I did wonder if it was a childish sort of revenge, but even so, I felt it was the greatest respect I could pay him.
52. A genius, of all people, ought to sleep in commonplace earth.
53. The day of the cherry blossom funeral.\nNo tears came.
54. I greeted that day with an unbelievable flatness.
55. It was because I didn't love him all that much...... I'd like to say, but...... that's a huge lie.
56. In truth, the day he called my work an 'epitaph'.
57. The day he affixed his seal to my hexaptych.
58. On those days I had wept my eyes out.
59. So the hexaptych is an epitaph, huh......\nA fitting way for him to put it.
60. But I do think my work was saved by that.
61. What is made, one hopes, will be saved.
62. Most makers would think that way, I suppose.
63. In that sense, I think I was a blessed painter.
64. That must be why I was able to see my old man off in the ordinary way beneath that cherry forest......
65. Parting with the last blood relative of the Kusanagi family......
66. The cherry blossoms of that day were very beautiful.
67. Anyway, about the matter of the inheritance......
68. It took place a few days after the transaction with the Nakamura family was concluded.
69. I, the sole blood relative, had said I wouldn't accept any of the inheritance of a world-class artist......
70. Naturally, Friedman was there.
71. Here, of course, the setup was that Friedman and I had never met before.
72. Even in a place like this, the two of us were putting on a farce.
73. Well, of course it would be that way......
74. But it's only by renouncing the inheritance that Kuzu can be saved.
75. It's a bit late to be saying it, but that's how it is.
76. Friedman said this with a thin smile.
77. Hey, wait a second, you!
78. You're the one who said you'd confirm three times, damn it!
79. "Is there something?"
80. "No, nothing...... I was just admiring how there really are people who won't keep a promise no matter what......"
81. "I'm a rationalist, you see. I reconsidered and decided that one confirmation was quite enough. Or would you prefer we continue the farce as planned?"
82. "No, nothing, it's just, as a Japanese, I do like to savor the lingering aftertaste of things."
83. "Is that so. If you want so badly to steep yourself in the aftertaste, why don't you finish signing and get out of this room posthaste?"
84. "Ah, don't mind if I do......"
85. Marty Friedman.
86. A foreign devil like him could never understand the beautiful Japanese sense of manners.\nYou lump of rationalism!
87. I finished writing my signature.
88. "Ah, that's right. In terms of your relationship with Kusanagi Ken'ichirou, I may indeed have no reason to be involved with you......"
89. "Nah nah, I'm never going to have anything to do with you again."
90. "I'll show up any number of times, wherever there's money to be made."
91. "No thank you. You economic animal!"
92. "That's a slur against Japanese people, isn't it."
93. "But it suits you especially well."
94. "I see, well, I'll take that as a compliment......"
95. "I'll never team up with you again, you moron."
96. I hurled my parting shot and walked out of the room.
97. In this way, I refused the whole inheritance.
98. Akashi wasn't able to receive his success fee either.
99. The only one who profited was Friedman, who had pocketed an outrageous middleman's margin when the genuine Nakamura family paintings were sold......
100. No, that's not quite right.
101. The only one who ended up losing out was Akashi......
102. "I'm home."
103. "Naoya, welcome back."
104. Kuzu came to greet me.
105. "Kuzu, could you sit down for a minute?"
106. Whereupon Kuzu sat down formally right there in the entryway.
107. "No no, not here. Let's go to the living room."
108. "Really? I thought you wanted a fellatio from this position."
109. "Why the hell would I demand some depraved play the moment I get back?"
110. "It's been a while since you were home...... I figured all that time staying over, Naoya's must have built up quite a bit of pent-up lust."
111. "I don't have that kind of energy. I was pretty much sleepless the whole time. Besides, you kept coming to drink my dreams, didn't you......"
112. "Yeah, that's true, but......"
113. "Anyway, let's go to the living room. We can't have a proper talk here."
114. I led Kuzu to the living room.
115. "Kuzu."
116. Kuzu was sitting primly on the sofa.
117. "It's all over."
118. "It's all over?"
119. "Yeah. The Nakamura family won't come after you anymore."
120. "Eh? How?"
121. "Well, I sorted out my old man's inheritance and scraped the money together, that kind of feel? At any rate, I was able to secure your freedom."
122. "This is the written pledge."
123. I handed a single sheet of paper to Kuzu.
124. It was something we'd obtained from them at the sales contract with the Nakamura family.
125. Written on it was a promise that from now on they would never lay a hand on her.
126. The name on it wasn't 'Kuzu'...... well, that's how it is, I suppose.\nIt was the name she had been hiding all this time. I did my best not to look at it.
127. "B-but even Ken'ichirou's entire fortune wasn't going to be enough......"
128. "No no, it actually did prove to be enough, which is why this pledge is here in my hand. You're free now."
129. "I'm free......"

