16. [Kuzu] "The one who really has to be grateful is you, Naoya?"
17. [Naoya] "Yeah, that's right. Because you gave me the opportunity.\nIf this whole affair hadn't happened, I wouldn't have been able to create that piece."
18. [Naoya] "The Splendid Confusion of an Epitaph, huh......"
19. [Naoya] "Because I got to paint a work like that as my last one......"
20. [Naoya] "In that sense, I suppose I owe thanks even to that hateful Nakamura Shouichi, and of course to Akashi, and to that shit Friedman......"
21. [Naoya] "Because they gave me a moment like that......"
22. [NARRATION] I dedicated 'Sakura Day Rhapsody' to my late mother.
23. [NARRATION] The 'Seven Aspects of the Sakura, six works' I had built up as forgeries.\nThese, my father called 'my epitaph'.
24. [NARRATION] I gained, through creation, a sense of fulfillment I had never felt before.
25. [NARRATION] A moment like that.
26. [NARRATION] There will be no other.
27. [Naoya] "So you see, the one who needs to be grateful is me."
28. [Naoya] "Because you gave me that supreme time with my old man......"
29. [Naoya] "That's something nothing else could replace......"
30. [Naoya] "You understand, don't you? Kuzu?"
31. [NARRATION] So saying, I placed a hand on Kuzu's shoulder.
32. [NARRATION] Tears were spilling one after another from Kuzu's eyes.
33. [NARRATION] Ah, yeah, of course......
34. [NARRATION] Because Kuzu, too, had loved that man......\nJust like I had......
35. [Naoya] "Oh, that's right...... there's this too, I want to give it to you."
36. [NARRATION] I handed Kuzu an old-fashioned paulownia box.
