40. [Ai] "So...... when I learned the truth, I felt my own powerlessness keenly......"
41. [Ai] "'Are the Kusanagi going to save us again?' -- that's what I thought."
42. [Naoya] "You say 'the Kusanagi,' but we're relatives to the Natsume, aren't we?"
43. [Ai] "Yes, because Grandmother Kotoko arranged it that way......"
44. [Ai] "A few weeks after I saw those paintings, Shizuku came back to this house."
45. [Ai] "I was told she was now a free woman."
46. [Ai] "And Shizuku, too, was crying, bitterly......"
47. [Naoya] "Crying? Her?"
48. [Ai] "Yes, she was crying.\nShe's a girl without much emotional range, but even so, when she's sad, the tears come."
49. [Ai] "We're always the ones being protected......"
50. [Naoya] "That's not true, Ai."
51. [Naoya] "You protected me too."
52. [Naoya] "I was just a kid when I came back to the country for my sick mother."
53. [Naoya] "But even so, I was just a powerless kid. There wasn't much I could do."
54. [Naoya] "For Mother's sake, you often came to our apartment."
55. [Ai] "Of course I did. Mizuna-san was my one and only sister.\nWhat kind of little sister wouldn't look after her......"
56. [Naoya] "Even so, I was saved by you."
57. [Ai] "You were? If you can say that, then nothing makes me happier.\nBecause I always thought I couldn't do anything for you......"
58. [Naoya] "That's not true at all."
59. [Ai] "It is true. So please, rely on me more.\nI'm powerless, yes, but I still want to be of use to you."
60. [Ai] "Too much has happened lately......\nKen'ichirou-san..... Shizuku..... and Misakura......"
61. [Naoya] "Misakura?"
62. [Ai] "You've been hiding it, haven't you? About Misakura?"
63. [Naoya] "You know about Rin?"
64. [Ai] "How could I not? She was Shizuku's first friend."
65. [Naoya] "Really? But you never gave any sign of knowing Rin at all."
66. [Ai] "With Misakura, there's a truth that you, and Shizuku, are trying to hide from her. So I thought pretending not to know was best."
67. [Ai] "If I knew about Misakura, all sorts of cracks would show."
68. [Naoya] "So that's how it was......"
69. [Ai] "You've already heard about Rin from Shizuku, haven't you?"
70. [Naoya] "Yeah, though not all of it......"
71. [Ai] "I see...... You should hear about that incident directly from Shizuku's own mouth.\nAnd you have to hear it."
72. [Naoya] "If I can hear it, then by all means......"
73. [Ai] "So Naoya and Shizuku are going to be together...... I ought to be angry, but the gladness is greater than any of it."
74. [Ai] "Shizuku, come in."
75. Shizuku, who had been in the corridor, is called in.
76. [Ai] "Shizuku, cherish Naoya. He's the one you fell in love with, but he's also a benefactor of the Natsume family."
77. [Shizuku] "I know."
78. [Ai] "Good. That's enough, then."
79. [Ai] "This talk is over."
80. [Ai] "Shizuku, about that incident...... explain it to him yourself, properly."
81. Shizuku gives a firm nod.
82. [Naoya] "I really thought Ai was going to hit me......"
83. [Shizuku] "Ai-neesan wouldn't do that."
84. [Naoya] "No, she actually has hit me before."
85. [Shizuku] "When?"
86. [Naoya] "Early one morning, when you'd fallen asleep in the kitchen and I had no choice but to carry you to your room. She saw me coming out of your room and took it for some kind of night crawl."
87. [Shizuku] "If we weren't properly going out, Ai-neesan might do something like that."
88. [Shizuku] "But now Naoya has reported to Nee-san properly.\nSo Nee-san wouldn't do that."
89. [Naoya] "Is that how it works......"
90. [Shizuku] "Mm..... more importantly......"
91. Shizuku looks out at the garden from the door.
92. [Shizuku] "This time it's my turn."
93. [Naoya] "Your turn? For what?"
94. [Shizuku] "Mm, I'm going to tell Naoya......"
95. [Naoya] "You'll tell me?"
96. [Shizuku] "Mm, what happened between Rin and me......"
97. [Naoya] "Ah, that......"
98. [Naoya] "That, huh......"
99. Scratching my head, I too look out at the garden.
100. [Naoya] "What happened between Rin and Shizuku......"
101. It is a hidden past.
102. Just as I did with Rin,\nShizuku and my father, too, kept a certain truth silent.
103. Because it was a truth that didn't need to be told.
104. But now that Shizuku and I are going to be together, it isn't right to keep secrets.
105. Especially when it involves Kusanagi Ken'ichirou. And Misakura Rin. And, to add to that, the Natsume family -- then surely I have to know.
106. [Naoya] "Somehow, right after finishing up with Ai...... it feels a bit anticlimactic, but......"
107. [Shizuku] "Should I have drawn it out a little more?"
108. [Naoya] "No, nothing like that."
109. [Naoya] "When you were Kuzu, I learned the truth. Ever since then, it's been on my mind."
110. [Naoya] "So knowing I'll get to hear it just like that -- it does feel a little anticlimactic."
111. [Naoya] "Even so, as Ai said, I want to hear it from your own mouth."
112. [Naoya] "This is definitely the right timing...... conversely, if you dragged it out, I'd be at a loss."
113. [Shizuku] "I want Naoya to know, too.\nThe story of Rin's and my past......"
114. [Shizuku] "It might get a little long."
115. [Shizuku] "In my memories with Rin, Ken'ichirou-san was always there......"
116. [Naoya] "Because she was my father's apprentice, after all......"
117. [Shizuku] "Mm. But besides that -- Ai-neesan, Grandmother Natsume, Nakamura Saki-san...... and Sui."
118. [Naoya] "Nakamura Saki? ...? Um...... who?"
119. [Shizuku] "Right now, she's Toritani Saki-san."
120. [Naoya] "Th-that's the principal of Yumihari?\nYou know the principal?"
121. [Shizuku] "Only a little...... but the impression is deep......"
122. [Shizuku] "It'll be long. Is that all right?"
123. Shizuku begins slowly to speak.\nThe story of two young girls......
124. Of how, in the past, the two of them met in this place, and how they parted......
125. This is a story from more than ten years ago.
126. I had been abandoned by my parent, and taken in by the Natsume family.
127. No -- I don't even know whether I was abandoned.\nPerhaps my mother thought that being in the Natsume house was what would protect me.
128. After all, I don't even remember my mother's face.
129. I came to the Natsume house not long after I was born.
130. And, as with all the others -- I too was Nakamura Shouichi's mistress's daughter.
131. Whether even as an infant I already showed some sliver of Hakuki's ability, or whether I didn't -- even that I don't know.

=== lines=139 stop_reason=end_turn in=7112 out=4796 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. But the one who arranged all of it, they say, was Grandmother Natsume Kotoko, who was still alive at the time.
2. I spent three years in this house with Grandmother Kotoko, and I remember her well.
3. Back in those days, I think, I had a heart just like anyone else -- I was an ordinary child.
4. In the memories of that time, I laughed, and I cried.
5. [Kotoko] "What is it, Shizuku? Are you crying?"
6. Grandmother Kotoko sat down beside me as I was crying.
7. [Kotoko] "What's the matter? Are you missing your mother?"
8. [Shizuku] "No. I don't know anything about my mother, so there's nothing to miss......"
9. [Kotoko] "Then why are you crying all alone?"
10. [Shizuku] "I don't know...... I just ate my meal, and the tears came."
11. [Kotoko] "Ate your meal, and the tears came, hm...... I see."
12. [Kotoko] "Well now...... Perhaps, since you are so sensitive, the act of eating is, for you, the same as the act of eating a living thing's heart......"
13. [Kotoko] "No...... but that isn't it, is it."
14. [Kotoko] "Perhaps a meal that someone else has made carries that much feeling in it......"
15. [Kotoko] "Tears come at happy times too, you know."
16. [Kotoko] "If there is love in a meal, then there is heart in it.\nWell, we say 'put your heart into it,' after all."
17. [Kotoko] "And you, Shizuku, can feel that......"
18. [Shizuku] "The heart...... put into a meal?"
19. [Kotoko] "Yes, and that kindness is what brings the tears......"
20. [Kotoko] "You are that sort of gentle child."
21. [Shizuku] "I...... am a gentle child?"
22. [Kotoko] "Yes, that you are."
23. [Kotoko] "But perhaps, from now on, there will be people who won't treat you as such a gentle child. Who will treat you like a mere object."
24. [Kotoko] "But you must not forget. You are more sensitive to the heart than anyone, and because you are sensitive, you have a special power."
25. [Kotoko] "You must never, ever think of yourself as a heartless doll."
26. [Shizuku] "The heart? What is the heart, Grandmother Kotoko?"
27. [Kotoko] "What is the heart? Now that is a difficult question......\nCome to think of it, Mizuna used to ponder such difficult things too......"
28. [Kotoko] "Well, I have no learning. Difficult things are beyond me, but......"
29. [Kotoko] "The heart, I think, is what one feels there."
30. [Shizuku] "What one feels there?"
31. [Kotoko] "Yes. So a meal, too, has a heart in it.\nIf you feel that a heart has been put into it......"
32. [Shizuku] "A meal has a heart, too?"
33. [Kotoko] "It isn't that everything has one.\nBut if you feel a heart there, then there is a heart there."
34. [Kotoko] "There, and also within yourself."
35. [Shizuku] "The heart is in all sorts of places?"
36. [Kotoko] "That's right. The people of old thought so."
37. [Shizuku] "The people of old?"
38. [Kotoko] "Yes. The people of old were wise -- they felt a heart in the trees and stones and rivers, too. The heart, they knew, belongs not to humans alone."
39. [Kotoko] "That, I believe, is a truly right way of seeing the world. I do......"
40. [Shizuku] "Say, say, then where is your heart, Grandmother Kotoko?"
41. [Kotoko] "Why, it is inside you, Shizuku."
42. [Shizuku] "I-inside me? Eh? Then...... where is my heart?"
43. [Kotoko] "Your heart is inside me, Shizuku.\nAnd of course, it is inside you, too."
44. [Kotoko] "So don't worry -- inside you, there are ever so many hearts packed away."
45. Grandmother Kotoko smiled gently.
46. [Kotoko] "Even after I am gone, my heart will still be there inside you, Shizuku."
47. [Shizuku] "I don't want you to go away, Grandmother Kotoko."
48. [Kotoko] "Would you say so? But people must part someday.\nThat is why you must cherish the heart of each person......"
49. [Shizuku] "Even so, I don't want you to go away, Grandmother Kotoko."
50. [Kotoko] "It will be all right. I won't go away so easily -- don't worry."
51. I loved Grandmother Kotoko dearly.
52. More than anyone else.
53. And so, on the day she died --
54. Just like that,\nI lost my heart.
55. I could not keep what Grandmother Kotoko had told me.
56. She had told me, so many times, that I had a heart.\nAnd yet, when she was gone, I let my own heart go.
57. I could not even inherit Grandmother Kotoko's heart......
58. Because I was a weak child...... by losing my heart, I ran away from that fact, I think.
59. From then on, there was no laughter, no tears in me.
60. Until then, the world had been filled with hearts.
61. And all of that was lost.
62. I became Hakuki.
63. [Ken'ichirou] "Shizuku? Is it all right?"
64. [Shizuku] "Nod......"
65. [Ken'ichirou] "Expressionless as ever, aren't you......"
66. That day, as always, Ken'ichirou had come by the Natsume estate.
67. Around this time, my mother -- Mizuna-san -- had been diagnosed with her illness, and Ken'ichirou had returned to Japan for a while.
68. [Ai] "Ken'ichirou. Hot tea, that all right?"
69. [Ken'ichirou] "Yeah, don't bother yourself......"
70. [Ai] "You may be fine with that, but doesn't the little guest over there need something?"
71. [Ken'ichirou] "Ah, right. I was late with the introduction."
72. Behind Ken'ichirou, a small tuft of soft hair swayed.\nThe girl bowed her head and introduced herself.
73. [Rin] "Nice to meet you. My name is Rin."
74. [Ai] "Ah, nice to meet you. I'm Natsume Ai.\nI'm the eldest of this house, and its head as well."
75. [Ai] "Well, no wonder you look like that.\nUntil last year, it wasn't a child like me but a proper grown-up who kept this house......"
76. [Ken'ichirou] "Come to think of it, the first anniversary's coming up soon...... even that old woman could die, huh. Still hard to believe."
77. [Ai] "Ken'ichirou, what a way to put it!"
78. [Ken'ichirou] "It's a fair way to put it! That old woman may have been kind to you lot, but to me she was a demon of a woman."
