16. [Sui] "Something to tell me?"
17. [Shizuku] "Mm. Sui, may I tell Naoya about your past with me?"
18. [Sui] "Why now? It's not as though we've been keeping it a secret..."
19. [Shizuku] "Actually, isn't even your own memory of it kind of fuzzy, Sui?"
20. [Sui] "That's true. Well, part of me came into being again from the petal of the thousand-year cherry that was pressed inside Rin's album, when it was scattered on that piece of land..."
21. [Naoya] "Huh? You mean you appeared because that album petal got scattered there?"
22. [Sui] "Well, more or less."
23. [Sui] "How about we talk while we walk? I'll tell you those parts too."
24. [Shizuku] "Yes, let's. My story with Sui..."
25. [Naoya] "Walk where?"
26. [Sui] "To the other thousand-year cherry, of course."
27. [NARRATION] With that, the two of them began walking toward the school building.
28. [NARRATION] Slowly, telling the old tale as they went...
29. [NARRATION] I have almost no memory of our life in New York.
30. [NARRATION] Without any sway of emotion, everything looks like a flat landscape.\nWhen a person has no heart, the power of memory doesn't develop.
31. [NARRATION] So I have hardly any memories of that cityscape.
32. [NARRATION] On Manhattan Island, old giant buildings in Gothic Revival or Art Deco styles, the kind you don't see in Tokyo, stood side by side with brand-new glass-walled towers.
33. [NARRATION] Even that much I only learned later.
34. [NARRATION] We lived in Chelsea.
35. [NARRATION] Our home was in an atelier set among the warehouses along the Hudson River.
36. [NARRATION] Many artists lived there, and in fact all sorts of people came and went through that atelier.
37. [NARRATION] And in the middle of it all, I always sat alone, motionless as an object.
38. [NARRATION] That day too, as always, I was on the sofa at the edge of the warehouse.
39. [Ken'ichirou] "Hm, hmm?"
40. [Ken'ichirou] "No, it's just... I thought I heard a voice."
41. [Shizuku] "There's no one here but me..."
42. [Ken'ichirou] "Well, yeah, but..."
43. [NARRATION] Ken'ichirou-san stared at the space beside the sofa I was sitting on.
44. [Ken'ichirou] "Isn't there someone there?"
45. [Shizuku] "As you can see..."
46. [Ken'ichirou] "As I can see, huh..."
47. [Shizuku] "Do you see something?"
48. [Ken'ichirou] "No, nothing."
49. [Shizuku] "Then that's your answer..."
50. [NARRATION] Ken'ichirou-san tilted his head and walked off toward the atelier.
51. [Sui] "What was that? Staring at people like that..."
52. [Shizuku] "It's all right... he can stare all he likes, since he can't see anything..."
53. [Sui] "I suppose so. Still, to think he can't see someone as pretty as me -- Ken'ichirou-san must have absolute holes for eyes."
54. [Shizuku] "I don't think it's that his eyes are blind, though..."
55. [NARRATION] Rin's feelings were too strong to remain contained within my body.
56. [NARRATION] Little by little, they took on a form.
57. [NARRATION] And became a presence that only I could see.
58. [Ken'ichirou] "Who are you talking to?"
59. [Shizuku] "No one. Just to myself..."
60. [Ken'ichirou] "...Hmm."
61. [NARRATION] I became friends with this presence that only I could see.\nBut one day, Ken'ichirou-san said:
62. [Ken'ichirou] "There's someone there, isn't there?"
63. [Shizuku] "Someone like who?"
64. [Ken'ichirou] "I don't know. But the feeling of it... yeah.\nThat's it. It's like Rin."
65. [Shizuku] "Rin is in Japan."
66. [Ken'ichirou] "Yeah, so it probably isn't Rin."
67. [Shizuku] "Then there's no one there..."
68. [Ken'ichirou] "I wonder. Lately, though, I feel like the 'Hakuki-ness' has slowly been leaving you too, Shizuku."
69. [Shizuku] "Hakuki-ness?"
70. [Ken'ichirou] "Yeah. You still don't open up to me, of course, but... you seem like you're having fun."
71. [Shizuku] "Having fun?"
72. [Ken'ichirou] "Yeah, even though your face is as blank as ever..."
73. [Shizuku] "Blank... but having fun..."
74. [Ken'ichirou] "I wonder what'll come of it."
75. [Ken'ichirou] "That thing you swallowed, Shizuku."
76. [Ken'ichirou] "The thing you swallowed. It was something incredible.\nLike drawing being out of nothing. That kind of thing."
77. [Ken'ichirou] "If it has that much power to take shape... how long can it really stay contained inside you?"
78. [Shizuku] "Ken'ichirou-san..."
79. [Ken'ichirou] "What's this one's name?"
80. [Shizuku] "Name? I don't really know...\nOh, she says 'Sui.'"
81. [Ken'ichirou] "Sui... I see. Same name as that person, huh..."
82. [Shizuku] "Same as whose name?"
83. [Ken'ichirou] "Ah, nothing, never mind."
84. [Ken'ichirou] "Sui, you must get lonely with just Shizuku, right? Feel free to talk to me too, no need to hold back."
85. [Shizuku] "You can see her too, Ken'ichirou-san?"
86. [Ken'ichirou] "As if. I can't see or hear a thing."
87. [Ken'ichirou] "But look. Shizuku, you must be lonely on your own, and Sui, you must be lonely on your own too, right? I've got lots of friends over here, but the two of you don't have many."
88. [Ken'ichirou] "So let me be part of your circle."
89. [Ken'ichirou] "How about it, Sui?"
90. [NARRATION] From then on, Ken'ichirou-san treated the invisible Sui as if she were an actual person there.
91. [NARRATION] When we ate out, it was never a table for two, always for three.\nHe'd have them prepare a meal for Sui too.
92. [NARRATION] Ken'ichirou-san would toss conversation not only to me but to the empty seat as well.
93. [NARRATION] He was having conversations with a Sui he wasn't supposed to be able to see.
94. [NARRATION] Conversations that shouldn't have connected at all somehow became, before we knew it, proper conversations.
95. [NARRATION] I asked Ken'ichirou-san once.
96. [Shizuku] "Ken'ichirou-san, can you actually see Sui?"
97. [Ken'ichirou] "Nope, can't see her."
98. [Shizuku] "But you're always having proper conversations with her."
99. [Ken'ichirou] "Yeah, I wonder. Maybe when it comes to painting, the conversation actually connects."
100. [Shizuku] "When it comes to painting?"
101. [Ken'ichirou] "I can just kind of tell -- like, 'this one would gripe about this part,' or 'she'd approve of this bit.' Right, Sui?"
102. [Sui] "Indeed. Ken'ichirou-san's paintings have plenty of problems, but when it comes to painting, I suppose we're on the same wavelength."
103. [Ken'ichirou] "Hey, you just said my paintings had problems, didn't you?"
104. [Sui] "It can't be helped. To a genius like me, Ken'ichirou-san's paintings are still nowhere near enough."
105. [Ken'ichirou] "Is that so? I bet if you actually tried painting, you'd turn out something pretty pathetic. Critiquing and actually painting are worlds apart."
106. [Sui] "Hmph, what a cheap taunt. Well, when I return to my true body, I'll show you the gap in talent between us."
107. [Ken'ichirou] "That day's never coming."
108. [Sui] "Well, I'll admit, that one, 'The Reclining Sakura' -- I acknowledge that much. If it were up against something I painted on an off day, when I thought 'not bad for a day I'm not on form,' I might just lose to it."
109. [Ken'ichirou] "I don't get half of what you just said..."
110. [Shizuku] "See... you two really are having a conversation..."
111. [Ken'ichirou] "Like I keep saying, I can't hear her. It's just a feeling."
112. [Sui] "Well, Ken'ichirou-san has excellent artistic intuition. I suppose it just gets across somehow."
113. [NARRATION] From the outside, it looked like a man talking loudly to himself.
114. [NARRATION] Not just in the atelier -- restaurants, shopping, galleries, wherever he took us, he spoke to Sui as well.
115. [NARRATION] Together with me, the child dragged along like a stepchild, the world dismissed Ken'ichirou-san's behavior as the "eccentricity" of a genius.
116. [NARRATION] And it was true -- to anyone who couldn't sense Sui's presence, what Ken'ichirou-san did was pure eccentricity.
117. [NARRATION] But Ken'ichirou didn't care how the world saw him.
118. [Naoya] "I see... so Sui was Rin's talent itself..."
119. [Sui] "Was I? If I were talent itself, I don't think I'd have taken on this kind of form."
120. [Sui] "I really do think it's more that I've been dragged along by Rin's emotions."
121. [Sui] "In fact, when Rin returned to this town, her pull on me was strong enough that my very existence got reset."
122. [Naoya] "Your existence got reset?"
123. [Shizuku] "I think Sui's existence stands on the balance between Rin and me."
124. [Shizuku] "When we were in New York, Rin was so far away that my influence was stronger, but once Rin and I started spending time together in this town, that balance shifted greatly."
125. [Shizuku] "I think the very fact that Rin has lost her memories has affected Sui's existence as well."
126. [Shizuku] "That's why when Sui appeared again here, she'd lost all her memories up to that point."
127. [Sui] "Yes. The feeling that Shizuku and I were friends remained, but... my memories were just gone, cleanly."
128. [Shizuku] "So if Rin and Sui had had more direct contact, Rin might have started searching for the memories she'd lost along with Sui..."
129. [Naoya] "I see... then it's a good thing Rin and Sui haven't had much contact."
130. [Shizuku] "Is that what you really think, Naoya?"
131. [Naoya] "Well, yeah -- those are memories that have to stay hidden from Rin.\nAt least, that's how I understand it..."
132. [NARRATION] Shizuku gave a noncommittal reply.
133. [Naoya] "What is it? Do you think Rin would've been better off getting her memories back, Shizuku?"
134. [Shizuku] "No. I don't know... I don't know, but..."
135. [Shizuku] "If that had happened, I think you would probably have walked alongside Rin..."
136. [Naoya] "Walked alongside her?"
137. [Shizuku] "I mean you wouldn't have been here at my side."
138. [Naoya] "Why would it come to that? I like you, Shizuku. I love you."
139. [Shizuku] "Mm, I know that."
140. [Shizuku] "So I think that just now was a little too tactless of me..."
141. [NARRATION] We took a slight detour and came out beside the church.
142. [Shizuku] "So this is where we come out..."

=== lines=142 stop_reason=end_turn in=6880 out=4564 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. [Naoya] "Yumihari's grounds are all winding, so if you cut through the woods instead of the paths, you end up on campus.\nWell, it was a bit of a detour, though..."
2. [Sui] "In any case, what Shizuku just told you is the sum total of my secret."
3. [Sui] "And, well, it seems that thanks to this painting, I've been able to make contact with more people..."
4. [Naoya] "'The Footprints of the Sakura,' huh..."
5. [Shizuku] "Whether they saw it on TV, or saw it in person... anyone who saw this thousand-year cherry painted by the art club members could perceive Sui..."
6. [Naoya] "So that's why back then... the clerk at the swimsuit shop couldn't see Sui..."
7. [Shizuku] "Right. That clerk probably hadn't seen this work on TV, either."
8. [Sui] "But in the end, it's only a thousand-year cherry painted on a wall...\nIt's not the kind of thing Rin would have painted..."
