=== lines=50 stop_reason=end_turn in=2891 out=1239 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. "Why are you thanking me?"
2. "Well, but..."
3. "Idiot. Everything I did, I did because I wanted to..."
4. "I only ever do what I want to do."
5. "So no matter how difficult it might be, I see it through..."
6. "Because it's what I wanted to do, after all."
7. "No matter what happens, I have to see it through..."
8. Shizuku wiped her tears away.
9. Wh-whoa, she's really clinging tight to my arm...
10. "Still! Naoya, you're way too good at too many things!"
11. "What are you talking about. I'm no good at all."
12. "You are not no good!"
13. "Back then, I never thought you'd say you'd paint the thousand-year cherry..."
14. "Well, of course I'd paint it..."
15. "Otherwise, I wouldn't know what I've been keeping my brush in reserve for..."
16. "Keeping your brush in reserve?"
17. "That's right. It's not that I broke my brush.\nI've been keeping it in reserve so I can pick it up whenever I want to paint..."
18. "It's not as if the right hand is the only thing you paint with..."
19. "It isn't the right arm that gives birth to a painting."
20. "Talent isn't what gives birth to a work."
21. "The wish to paint -- that conviction is what gives birth to a work."
22. "So, whenever it happens, I'll start painting again."
23. "Not for anyone else's sake... For no one but myself."
24. Shizuku gazed at me.
25. It somehow started to feel embarrassing.
26. "Ahaha, well, whatever. It doesn't matter, does it..."
27. "Anyway, you know. That."
28. "More importantly, we've got to hurry back! The Natsume family is going to be mad and skip dinner on us!"
29. "Ah, that might be true..."
30. "So then."
31. "Let's go home."
32. Shizuku answered happily.
33. A clear autumn night sky.
34. As though the town of Yumihari itself had been transposed onto the heavens.
35. Lights twinkling above and below.
36. "The light of the crossings of cause and effect..."
37. There's a line like that in one of my father's poems, too.
38. "Across all of the illusory spring-hued sky\n only, recklessly, the alternating lamps of causality\n glow brightly, brightly, brightly."
39. Honestly, I don't understand what it means.
40. But when I look at the lights of the town, somehow I feel I do.
41. In each of those window-lights, scattered like a starry sky, there must be someone's life.
42. The light of the crossings of cause and effect.
43. "The stars, twinkling, twinkling..."
44. "Yeah, they are..."
45. "The two of us, walking home down a starlit road..."
46. "It's fine if a miracle like that happens sometimes..."
47. "It's no miracle... This is inevitable."
48. "Twinkling, twinkling..."
49. Shizuku laughed, arm linked with mine. The two of us walked down the sloping road.
50. In the sky, the stars glittered, twinkling, twinkling.

=== lines=133 stop_reason=end_turn in=4550 out=2885 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. 　I came to school alone today.
2. 　Apparently Rina had something to take care of and had left for school early in the morning, or so I was told...
3. "But why isn't she here yet...?"
4. 　I wait in the classroom.
5. 　Nothing but background noise -- the voice I want to hear isn't there.
6. 　The chime rings.
7. 　Class begins.
8. 　There's no way Rina would be late.
9. 　Not unless there was some reason...
10. 　A reason?
11. 　I bolt out of the classroom.
12. 　I pass a teacher in the hallway.
13. "H-hey, Kawachino. Class is starting."
14. "I'm leaving early!"
15. "L-leaving early? H-hey!"
16. 　The teacher's voice fades behind me.
17. 　I run.
18. 　I have no idea where she'd be.
19. 　But I have a really bad feeling.
20. 　A really, really bad feeling and nothing else.
