95. [Naoya] "Even if you'd married into the Nakamura family, I can't imagine you had that much authority back then."
96. [Headmaster] "After graduating, I became a Nakamura, and by my twenties I was already head of a year. So I was able to bring him in as a part-time art instructor."
97. [Naoya] "Yumihari is a prestigious school. Even if Kusanagi Ken'ichirou would later become a world-renowned artist, at the time he was a nobody. Getting a teaching post at Yumihari isn't easy."
98. [Headmaster] "Yes. Without my recommendation,\nhe'd have had trouble even landing the part-time job."
