1. 　They were paintings Kei had done.\nToritani checked those canvases, one by one.
2. 　Making her way across the sea of countless canvases, Toritani finally reached the far end\nand sank to the floor where she stood.
3. 　Beyond the moon-object, Kei was curled up asleep.
4. 　In the hand of Kei, breathing peacefully in his sleep, a brush was clutched.\nBeside him, a palette and paints lay scattered.
5. 　Toritani picked up the canvas that had been lying nearest to Kei.
6. 　It was a picture of a bird, born from an egg, about to take flight.\nThe bird looked something like a magpie.
7. 　Painted only partway through, the brush had stopped there.
8. 　Every canvas was the same.
9. 　The paintings -- were all unfinished.
10. 　Toritani, careful not to smudge the picture, hugged one of the canvases to her chest.
11. 　There were no tears in her eyes.
12. [Makoto] "This is my very best."
13. [Makoto] "For the sake of two geniuses, I gave my very best.\nWishing that the two of them would go even further, I gave birth to the moon."
14. [Makoto] "But --"
15. 　Toritani's fingers, gripping the canvas, tightened.
16. [Makoto] "It didn't reach. It didn't reach, but..."
17. [Makoto] "This is enough."
18. 　Her lips trembled, and her back curled inward.
19. 　No sob escaped her.
20. 　The paintings were all unfinished, and\nKei could not see beyond the place where he now stood.
21. 　The best I can do, for the sake of two geniuses.\nThe hand Toritani had stretched out did not reach her own wish.
22. 　Even so, Toritani would surely never cry.
23. 　The words she had told herself -- 'This is enough' -- were the whole of Toritani.
24. 　That much, at least, I could understand.

=== lines=141 stop_reason=end_turn in=6475 out=4997 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. Toritani went on to sit the entrance exam for a national university's fine arts department, and passed with flying colors.
2. With skill like hers, and academics that left nothing to be desired, it was only the natural result.
3. As for me, I couldn't quite make it into the same department, but I did get into another faculty at the same university.
4. Once we started school, we talked about staying in the dorms for a while to save up money,\nand eventually moving in together.
5. Toritani had plenty of savings from her pottery sales and the like,\nbut she said school fees, living expenses, exam costs, entrance fees, and the move\nhad drained a considerable amount.
6. Our relationship is progressing along very smoothly.
7. In my head I still sometimes slip into calling her "Toritani" out of habit,\nbut when it's just the two of us, we've grown fairly natural about calling each other by our given names.
8. During exam prep, when I scored well on the tests in our two-person study sessions,\nor got good results on a practice exam, I'd demand a reward from Toritani.
9. At first, she balked out of embarrassment,\nbut before long she learned to use those rewards as the carrot part of carrot-and-stick.
10. Toritani's carrot-and-stick was masterful, and I -- turned into the very horse chasing the carrot --\ntore through the final stretch of exam prep.
11. When I got my acceptance, the two of us hugged and celebrated.\nThe reward I asked for that day, however, has yet to actually materialize.
12. Even though the two of us have done things far more extreme, and far more lewd,\nfor some reason, that one thing was the only thing Toritani couldn't clear.
13. It was as if, after mastering even a backflip in tumbling,\nshe still couldn't do the forward roll she'd stumbled on at the very beginning.
14. Impossible! It's impossible! -- how many times has she cried that at me?\nA teary-eyed Toritani is adorable, so even her failing was its own kind of fun.
15. There were plenty of little squabbles, but nothing truly sad ever happened.
16. Even those little squabbles, seen from the outside,\nwere apparently nothing more than lovers' quarrels...
17. [Naoya] "...Shall we head back?"
18. [Makoto] "Today I really think I can do it."
19. A little after graduation... one particular day, the moment I walked into Chimera,\nToritani greeted me with a straight face and that opening line.
20. It was that stretch of afternoon when, for whatever reason, the shop empties out entirely.\nSince no one was around, she must have judged it safe to say aloud.
21. She kept her face as serious as she could, her tone casual,\nbut the corners of her eyes were faintly red.
22. [Naoya] "Got it. I'll be expecting great things today."
23. [Makoto] "Yes. Please do."
24. Chimera closed, and Toritani wrapped up the cleaning and the register.\nEver since exams ended, I'd been helping with the after-hours cleaning too.
25. [Makoto] "Sorry to keep you waiting. Here, your wages."
26. Toritani, back from the kitchen, set a bowl of beef rice down in front of me.
27. [Naoya] "Mm... delicious."
28. Taking my pay as beef bowls that doubled as a late-night meal, rather than as cash,\nhad turned out to be the right call.
29. [Makoto] "Hey, Naoya -- our part-time work at Chimera is almost over, isn't it?"
30. [Naoya] "Hm? Yeah, that's right."
31. [Makoto] "You know the maid uniform I wear for work? One would wear out too quickly,\nso I've been rotating between two of them..."
32. [Makoto] "Since I'm quitting, I decided to buy this one off them.\nIt's worn out here and there, and it'd probably just get thrown out once I leave."
33. [Naoya] "Ohhh, in other words, we can do it with you in a maid uniform."
34. [Makoto] "Ugh... there you go being blunt again...\nWell, yeah, to put it plainly, that's the idea."
35. [Naoya] "Wait, seriously?"
36. [Makoto] "You think I'd joke about something like this? Of course, if you don't want to--"
37. I clatter to my feet from the chair.
38. [Naoya] "No, I want to! Please let me! By any means necessary!!"
39. [Makoto] "H-hey, your face is kind of scary...?"
40. [Naoya] "Ah, sorry. I got a little too eager, in more than one sense."
41. [Makoto] "You really are too eager, in more than one sense... your reflexes are frighteningly quick..."
42. [Naoya] "Where's the fool who wouldn't react when his girlfriend says\nshe'll have sex with him in a maid uniform?"
43. [Makoto] "I don't think you'd be a fool for not reacting either... but well..."
