36. "You charge ahead. Powerfully, believing in your own expression, you charge ahead. That's what an artist is."
37. "But I really didn't think you were unaware of my illness......"
38. "I'd been sure that painting was a message telling me, 'Don't run from your illness'......"
39. "Well, that's not wrong, is it?"
40. "I didn't know whether you were sick, but this kid sure does paint gloomy paintings. Yuck. I want to make it a brighter painting. That's what I was thinking."
41. "So I painted one overflowing with life, for all I was worth."
42. "Gloomy paintings aren't bad in themselves, but they don't suit you as you are now.\nThat's why I made it this kind of painting."
43. "Not bad, right?"
44. Once again Hikawa-san looked up at the painting on the dome.
45. It was a cherry tree soaring into the sky like a cypress.
46. A magic all in white.
47. What had, until only recently, been a black flame had, with only its mode of expression changed, become a soft pale crimson reaching for heaven.
48. The petals fluttering down through the dome
49. were like stars on the celestial sphere.
50. "I'm heading home soon. You two should go home too.\nYou're frail, right?"
51. "Especially that kid over there. You keep swinging knives around and one of these days you'll cause a fatal assault and get hauled off by the cops."
52. "Shut up! Just go home!\nI was an idiot for thinking, even for a moment, that you were doing this for Hikawa-san's sake!"
53. "Don't dump your expectations on me on your own and then blame me!"
54. "Shut up, die!"
55. "Die, die, enough already. What are you, some 'die-die gang'?!"
56. "Never come back here again!"
57. "Yeah, same to you.\nQuit being two brats out alone this late at night."
58. Kusanagi Naoya.\nThe Sakura Artist left the dome.
59. Leaving behind a masterpiece that, in a few hours, would be gone.
60. "Yumi, so you knew...... about my illness......"
61. "Sorry, I saw the name of the medicine......"
62. "I see. I'm sorry -- I didn't explain it properly......"
63. "It's okay."
64. "I'm having surgery at the end of summer......"
65. "I was just scared of it, that's all......"
66. "So I was doing my best to prepare myself to accept death."
67. "Because I thought that if I could feel it was okay to die, the surgery wouldn't be scary either......"
68. "But I was wrong."
69. "I'll have the surgery, cure my illness, and sketch even under the sunlight.\nAfter being shown a painting like that......"
70. "I want to live......"
71. "I think that's the right thing."
72. The thing that had been stirring inside my heart no longer stirred.
73. The stench of death was gone.
74. The shadow of death no longer whispered to her.
75. From her, that moonlike beauty was gone......
76. The end of the story she once told me --\nwhat had it been, again?
77. Why did the scorpion become a bright red flame?
78. Why did the nighthawk become a pale blue flame?
79. Because they had committed the original sin of devouring others, they burned and became stars.
80. Then what about me?
81. Why did I come to love Hikawa-san?
82. Was the choice of loving an ordinary member of the opposite sex not available to me?
83. But for me, the option of loving any other kind of human being was never there from the start, and out of the crowd of pretty girls, I came to love the frailest, the weakest, the loveliest -- Hikawa-san.
84. This is the punishment for my sin.
85. That is why I stand here.
86. But the scorpion burned bright red and became a beautiful star.
87. And the nighthawk too became a beautiful star shining blue.
88. I cannot even become a star.
89. Like a maggot that will never hatch.
90. But even so......
91. (This laughing Hikawa-san is nice too......)
92. That was all I was thinking, quite simply.
93. The painting of the shining forest of cherry blossoms.
94. And the smile she showed within it.
95. It was not the "Hikawa-san" I had known.
96. The Hikawa-san who shone blue like the moon is gone.
97. In her place is a Hikawa-san who shines within the cherry-blossom forest.
98. Spring snow.
99. Wrapped in the pale crimson snow, her smile shines.
100. Even if I do not shine, so long as she does, that is enough for me......
101. So I say it.
102. "Do your best. Rina!"
103. The one who falls in love loses.
104. And even so, I love her.
105. Quite simply, I love her with all my heart.
106. So this is not a punishment.
107. Because I get to be together with her......
108. --the unfinished graffiti--
109. Afterward, I looked into the Sakura Artist.
110. Beyond his major works, I looked into the graffiti he was said to have scattered around town.
111. For some reason, none of the graffiti were finished; every one of them had been abandoned partway through.
112. Why was it, then, that the Sakura Artist had finished only that single mural?
113. It was a question that snagged at me, if only a little,\nbut before I could arrive at any answer, all of the graffiti had been erased.
114. That day too, as always,
115. I was alone in the back garden blowing bubbles with chewing gum,
116. when one of them said,
117. "About the Hikawa-stripping plan --"
118. "Not doing it."
119. "Or rather, I'm not gonna let you do it!"
120. I threw myself at the boy, fists first.
121. I don't know why.
122. Honestly, I was probably just in a foul mood.
123. As we swung at each other, the others joined in, and it became a brawl.
124. Angry shouts split my ears.
125. I don't know if I was hitting or being hit,
126. probably both,
127. but my whole body burned, and I stopped knowing what was what.
128. My whole body grew hotter and hotter.
129. If I kept getting hotter like this, maybe I could become a flame and become a star.
