80. "Deliberately, huh...... That's rather offensive to hear."
81. "Is it? But painting that one was quite painful for you, wasn't it?"
82. "Why do you think that?"
83. "Senpai, after 'Sakura Day Rhapsody,' at some point, something went wrong with your dominant hand, didn't it?"
84. "I've seen 'Sakura Day Rhapsody' many, many times since then, so I can tell."
85. "Senpai, you didn't lay down your brush -- something happened to your dominant hand.\nI don't know the reason.\nAll I know is that after that, you were never able to paint the same paintings again."
86. "Back then, when you kept calling it graffiti and scattered those half-finished paintings all over the place -- that was because you'd come to feel keenly that your hand was ruined, wasn't it?"
87. "No matter how much you painted, no matter how much you painted, nothing worked out.\nSo you couldn't even complete a piece, and you just scattered paintings around aimlessly, didn't you?"
88. "I may not look it, but I hate you, senpai, so I've done a fair amount of research on your works. There was a time when I went hunting all over for the graffiti you painted back then."
89. "Everything I found was unfinished."
90. "And every single one of them, though conscious of 'Sakura Day Rhapsody,' was something entirely different."
91. "What came through to me was the impatience of being conscious of your own past painting, yet ending up with something completely different."
92. "There aren't many answers to this.\nBy that time, Kusanagi-senpai, you could no longer paint the same kind of picture as 'Sakura Day Rhapsody.'"
93. "For someone who doesn't paint to be able to point that out to me -- how far I've fallen......"
94. "Even so, during that collaboration -- the collaboration with Rina -- your brushwork was close to that of your prime."
95. "Which makes me think the opposite. If it had been the Kusanagi Naoya who completed 'Sakura Day Rhapsody,' overwhelming Rina's painting would have taken a single night, easily."
96. "That's how overwhelming the talent called Kusanagi Naoya must have been."
97. "And yet, that Kusanagi Naoya, back then, went there for several days, advancing the work bit by bit."
98. "Not only that -- as if to transform it all at the final touch, up until the day before, everything was plain, drab underlayer work."
99. "It was unnatural."
100. "Wasn't it that, painting with a hand that couldn't paint, forcing yourself through it, the work became days of going back and back again?"
101. "Wasn't that why that collaboration stretched over so many days?"
102. "Kawachino, you're a little frightening."
103. "That sort of thing, even if you notice, you don't say.\nBecause the person is hiding it."
104. "You're right. If you'd hidden it properly, I wouldn't have said anything either."
105. "I am hiding it, aren't I?"
106. "Then why, in that state, did you continue the collaboration with Rina?"
107. "Why did you do something that would give it away?"
108. "The spirit of service...... is that it?"
109. "After your mother's death, have you, like Nakahara Chuuya, been doing all these unnecessary things in a spirit of service?"
110. "Unnecessary? No, that's wrong.\nBecause with that painting, Rina really was saved......"
111. "The painting you finished by overworking a hand that no longer served you.\nBy that painting, Rina was saved......"
112. "A painting that shortened the life of your own right hand.\nAnd because of it, the shadow of death faded from Rina......"
113. "Why -- the collaboration with Rina...... why did you go so far......"
114. "And afterward, when you enrolled at Yumihari Academy, your dominant hand had changed, hadn't it? Which means your right arm hardly works at all, doesn't it?"
115. "No, it's not that bad. The arm is basically fine.\nIt's just that a few of my fingers have no feeling......"
116. "I can hold chopsticks. I can hold a pencil.\nI just can't paint the way I used to......"
117. "But back then, you tried to paint the way you used to.\nThat must have been serious abuse of it."
118. "Yeah, that's true. It really was rough......\nHikawa had this ridiculously incredible talent, and it felt like I could be swallowed up by it at any moment......"
119. "'What a gloomy painting. I don't like this. I want to make it brighter......'\nI'm sure I said things like that at the time, and that much is true."
120. "But it's also true that I could sense the scent of 'death' from that painting......"
121. "So you had noticed Rina's illness after all?"
122. "Paintings are an interesting thing. There's something you can sense beyond skill or lack of it."
123. "I didn't know what illness Hikawa had, but I could tell from her painting that she was trying to accept death."
124. "That's why I wanted to wipe that scent of death off her......"
125. "Even though back then you played dumb......"
126. "Well, sure. But I didn't know what illness it was, so it wasn't total feigning."
127. "The fact that not much time had passed since my mother's death was part of it too......"
128. "That distinctive scent of death -- I just couldn't leave it alone."
129. "The scent particular to a person who has accepted death......"
130. "I wanted to remove the shadow of death from her......"
131. "Was that because it was Rina?"
132. "Who knows?"
133. "Are you going to play dumb? Or was it a whimsical spirit of service? Would anyone have done?"
134. "That's for you to imagine as you please."
135. "Was anyone fine, or was it because it was Rina!\nFor me, this is a matter of importance."
136. "Yeah, it's an important matter."
137. "Which is why I can't answer it here."
138. "But this much I can say."

=== lines=70 stop_reason=end_turn in=4205 out=2058 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. [Naoya] "You're right. Back then, I was pretty much in despair over my own right hand."
2. [Naoya] "I'd resigned myself to the fact that my right hand was never coming back......"
3. [Naoya] "That's why, that night, when I stopped by that park, it was to erase graffiti......"
4. [Naoya] "And that's when I ran into her......"
5. [Naoya] "A park of cypresses in the dark...... a girl clad in pure white......"
6. [Naoya] "She was single-mindedly painting up a symbol of death......"
7. [Naoya] "I watched her doing it for several days."
8. [Yumi] "Peeping? What awful taste."
9. [Naoya] "So I saw the moment you met Hikawa, too."
10. [Yumi] "Wh-what?! What is that?!"
11. [Naoya] "No, only the moment you met, honestly.\nI don't have such awful taste as to peep on the time between the two of you.\nI left the scene right then......"
12. [Naoya] "But I did think, ah, this one too has been drawn in by the scent of that strange girl......"
13. [Yumi] "The scent of a strange girl......"
14. [Naoya] "A girl with a small body, going on painting an enormous symbol of death in a place like that."
15. [Naoya] "It was alluring enough to swallow you whole......"
16. [Yumi] "But you -- you erased that allure!"
17. [Naoya] "Yeah, that's right. Exactly so."
18. [Naoya] "I meant to wipe away the seduction of death."
19. [Naoya] "The more seductive it was, the more I wanted to erase it......"
20. [Naoya] "So I thought it wouldn't be so bad to offer up the last thing my right hand could do to her."
21. [Yumi] "The last......?"
22. [Naoya] "Yeah, that was the last."
23. [Naoya] "My right arm has completely lost the power to create paintings now."
24. [Naoya] "So, in a sense, it may have been a kind of miracle.\nThat I managed to finish a painting that could wipe the shadow of death away from Hikawa......"
25. [Yumi] "Then that was Kusanagi Naoya's last work."
26. [Naoya] "Yeah, Kusanagi Naoya's last work."
27. [Yumi] "To offer up your last work...... on something bound to vanish in a typhoon like that."
28. [Yumi] "You really are a hateful man...... Kusanagi Naoya."
29. [Yumi] "At the very least, if it had been from a spirit of service...... how much that would have saved me."
30. [Naoya] "If that were the case, I'd be on par with Christ."
31. [Yumi] "Get yourself nailed to a cross...... someone like you."
32. [Naoya] "Give me a break. I'm no good with pain."
33. [Yumi] "Liar!"
34. [Yumi] "There's no one as numb to pain as you......"
35. [Yumi] "You endure it far too much......"
36. [Naoya] "That's not true......"
37. [Yumi] "Rina is beautiful."
38. [Yumi] "Like the moon......"
39. [Yumi] "Ephemeral...... and gentle...... shining down on everyone."
40. [Naoya] "Yeah, that's the kind of smile she has......"
41. [Yumi] "To think I'd agree with you, damn Kusanagi......"
42. [Yumi] "I was sure a guy like you thought of Rina as nothing more than some eccentric underclassman!"
43. [Naoya] "In actual fact, that's exactly how she is when she's with me."
44. [Naoya] "I saw her in that park too, you know.\nAfter that, there's no way I could think of her like that......"
45. [Naoya] "You've been the same, haven't you, all this time."
46. [Naoya] "You've been chasing after the figure of that girl you saw in the park."
47. [Yumi] "You're right. Half correct, indeed."
48. [Yumi] "But I love the Rina who came after that too."
49. [Naoya] "Yeah, I know......"
50. [Yumi] "Even the bright smile you gave to Rina -- I love that too."
51. [Naoya] "I see, well, thanks for that."
52. [Naoya] "Makes it worth having forced myself to finish that painting."
53. [Yumi] "How candid of you."
54. [Naoya] "Naturally. A creator's glad when someone understands the hardship of creation."
55. [Yumi] "Being talked to as if I were someone who understands you -- that's genuinely unpleasant."
56. [Naoya] "But for a creator, someone who understands is a thing of irreplaceable value."
57. [Yumi] "Me, an understander of you? It really does make me want to vomit."
58. [Naoya] "But it's probably the truth."
59. [Yumi] "Which is exactly why it makes me want to vomit all the more."
60. [NARRATION] Kusanagi-senpai turns on his heel.
61. [Yumi] "You're leaving?"
62. [Naoya] "Yeah. About time I checked on Rin."
63. [Yumi] "Coming to check on me, teaching Rin-senpai to paint -- you really do have it rough......"
64. [NARRATION] Senpai raises one arm in silent farewell.
65. [NARRATION] And then there is no one left on the rooftop.
66. [Yumi] "Kusanagi Naoya......"
67. [NARRATION] If only that man had been nothing but an airheaded, eccentric fool -- how good that would have been.
68. [NARRATION] If only that man had been merely a man of talent, one who was simply good at painting -- how good that would have been.
69. [NARRATION] If only that man had been the kind Rina happened to fall for, someone who had appeared purely by chance -- how good that would have been.
70. [NARRATION] But the truth is otherwise.

=== lines=135 stop_reason=end_turn in=5032 out=3704 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. A few minutes after parting with Rina.
2. I realized I was surrounded.
3. Little by little, a crowd was closing in around me.
4. What a pain... How did this many people even show up...
5. Encircled, I was herded off into a deserted back alley.
6. That's a pretty sizable group...
7. [Yumi] "So then, what business could you possibly have, dragging me into a place like this?"
8. [Schoolgirl A] "Hey, what exactly are you to Kusanagi-senpai?"
9. [Yumi] "Like I said, his girlfrie--!"
10. [Schoolgirl A] "Don't screw with us. The guy himself denied it, didn't he?"
11. Slapping me across the cheek right off the bat -- pretty scrappy bunch, huh...
12. [Schoolgirl B] "You did something to my shoe locker, didn't you? That hurt like hell, you know."
13. [Yumi] "Well, that's what you get for touching someone else's shoe locker without permis--"
14. Gwuff!
15. [Schoolgirl A] "You get the situation? You get what's about to happen to you, running your mouth like that?"
16. This time she kicked me in the stomach.
17. Ah, yeah, I know this.
18. This is the kind that gradually escalates into violence...
19. [Yumi] "The situation? The situation, huh..."
20. [Schoolgirl A] "You know, you're supposed to be one of those trash characters who just keeps her head down at school -- so why are you strutting around all cocky the moment summer break's over? Honestly, it's seriously annoying."
21. Well, well... So this is what I get for enrolling at Yumihari Academy and playing nice.
22. [Schoolgirl B] "What? Did something happen over break? Some kind of summer-break debut?"
23. [Schoolgirl A] "Gyah!?"
24. Without hesitation, I drove a punch into her face.
25. In a fight between girls, you don't normally throw a straight punch at the face.
26. Girl fights are all noise -- nothing but big, wide, swinging attacks.
27. So you start with the strikes that actually work, prioritized first.
28. Usually when women gang up, it starts with open-handed slaps, then gradually escalates until you get beaten to a pulp.
29. Then the nagging lecture starts up again, and another slap flies.
30. They repeat it over and over. That's the pattern unique to a female lynching.
31. So you do what women don't do.
32. Not that men throw straight punches to the face all that often either.
33. You can't pull something like this off without a lot of experience in the field.
34. [Yumi] "Hah!"
35. Left hook.
36. Compared to a right straight, the left is weaker, so I threw my whole body weight into it.
37. Say what you like, the power of a punch is basically determined by body weight.
38. When someone small like me throws a punch, I have to load as much of my full body weight into it as possible.
39. My sudden counterattack had everyone on the scene frozen in stunned silence.
40. And it had to be that way.
41. In sheer numbers, the enemy was overwhelmingly at the advantage.
42. Rabble or not, if they all swarmed and hit at once, there'd be no way to fight back.
43. So the only option was to strike first and win.
44. [Yumi] "Tyah!"
45. Finally I drove in a kick.
46. The girl went flying.
47. [Schoolgirl C] "Huh? Huh? Huuuh?"
48. They were swallowed by the moment.
49. A crowd swallowed by the moment is weak.
50. That's when I smiled.
51. [Yumi] "Just because I keep quiet, did you think I was weak?"
52. [Yumi] "Well, too bad. I'm not weak at all."
53. I answered with a smirk.
54. In truth, I had no such composure to spare.
55. The hand I'd hit her with hurt more than I'd expected.
56. Did I punch wrong? No, my body's probably just not what it used to be.
57. The left with my weight behind it must have put a serious load on me.
58. My body isn't built for hitting people anymore, I guess.
59. Still, if it could just end with this...
60. [Schoolgirl D] "The hell are you getting all full of yourself for?"
61. A uniform from a different school...
62. If I recall, it looked like the uniform of one of the bottom-tier schools.
63. The kind of place idiots go.
64. Actually, no -- it was the school the teacher first recommended to me.
65. [Yumi] "Pfft, so bottom-tier trash are Kusanagi Naoya fan-club members now?"
66. She hit me with quite a bit of force.
67. I threw up an arm to block on reflex, but my arm hurt.
68. What kind of muscle does she have?
69. [Schoolgirl D] "Sorry for being bottom-tier, huh!"
70. As she came at me with a continuous barrage, I countered with a kick.
71. Legs are longer than arms.
72. Simple logic, and my counter landed cleanly.
73. But the bottom-tier girl didn't go down.\nTruly bottom-tier. Are women gorillas or something?
74. [Schoolgirl D] "Wh-why you, making a fool of me..."
75. [Yumi] "As if I'd lick a face that filthy... Gross."
76. I checked the situation again.
77. Most of the crowd was still frozen, but from that exchange, a few of gorilla-girl's friends were quietly moving to encircle me.
78. I slowly backed away to match them.\nLetting a blind spot open would be bad.
79. Honestly, as I am now, if a few of them jumped me from behind, I'd get crushed easily.
80. Sadly, I'm neither tall nor -- though I'd like to boast about it -- especially heavy.
81. Nor do I have any particular strength to speak of.
82. All I've got is plenty of experience with real fights back when I was a brat...
83. And that experience is telling me:
84. Yumi-chan is in serious trouble!
85. That said, I hadn't just wandered into being surrounded without a plan.
86. Now then, how to get out of this...
87. [Schoolgirl] "Hey, hey, isn't punching each other, like, kind of barbaric? Can we not?"
88. From within the crowd of girls, one raised her hand and called out.
89. [Yumi] "Haah? Weren't you the ones who threw the first punch?"
90. [Schoolgirl] "I wouldn't know. It was that girl who hit her, right? Nothing to do with me."
91. [Schoolgirl D] "Shut up, would you. I won't feel right until I beat the crap out of this one."
92. [Schoolgirl] "That's fine. But, uh, I took a photo of the scene just now, so if it gets out to your schools, that'd be pretty bad for both of you, wouldn't it?"
93. [Schoolgirl D] "Y-you! Wh-whose side are you on!?"
94. [Schoolgirl] "Nobody's, really. I've already attached the email address, so all that's left is to hit send."
95. [Schoolgirl D] "S-stop it, please, if I get suspended again..."
96. [Schoolgirl] "Then how about we drop the barbaric brawling?"
97. Yet another uniform.\nI've no idea what school she's from.
98. Still, I had to admit her throwing water on the situation was a real help.
99. [Yumi] "What is it? Are you bottom-tier too?"
100. [Schoolgirl] "M-my deviation score isn't low enough to be called bottom-tier.\nWell, a little below Yumihari Academy, sure."
101. [Yumi] "Anything below a school even I could get into is bottom-tier."
102. [Schoolgirl] "Bold words, Kawachino Yumi-san."
103. [Yumi] "And?"
104. [Schoolgirl] "My name's Nagayama Kana. Nice to meet you."
105. [Yumi] "Not that we'll ever meet again."
106. [Kana] "Don't say such sad things. Besides, I'm your senior. I'd like a little respect, thanks."
107. [Yumi] "I'll pay it if there's need. Where's the need?"
108. [Kana] "Who knows? More importantly, Yumi-chan, would you really be okay with this photo getting sent to your school?"
109. [Yumi] "Any way you slice it, a photo that clearly just shows a bunch of people surrounding one person doesn't scare me in the slightest."
110. [Kana] "Really? Depending how you look at it, it could pass as a big group brawl, no?"
111. [Yumi] "Either way, a suspension over a fight isn't remotely frightening."
112. [Yumi] "More to the point, what's your goal here? Do you want to pry me away from Kusanagi Naoya?"
113. [Kana] "Yeah, probably -- everyone but me."
114. [Schoolgirl D] "You're not with us!?"
115. [Kana] "I was just curious about this person called Kawachino Yumi."
116. [Kana] "You seem like you'd know things about Kusanagi Naoya that I don't."
117. [Yumi] "Haah? What's that about? Don't tell me you're a Kusanagi stalker?"
118. [Kana] "Yeah, maybe."
119. [Yumi] "In that case, I definitely can't tell you anything."
120. [Kana] "Why, why? I just saved you, didn't I?"
121. [Yumi] "I didn't need saving."
122. [Kana] "Oh? Doesn't look that way to me. You were pretty outmatched, weren't you?"
123. [Yumi] "Not at all!"
124. [Kana] "Come on, apparently you were quite the wild one in the old days, but lately you haven't been doing that sort of thing, have you?"
125. What's with this girl?
126. She knows about me?
127. [Kana] "Those upperclassmen you bullied, Yumi-chan? They happen to be in my year, you know."
128. [Kana] "When I asked those girls about you, they begged me to kill you.\nSo I thought, wow, Yumi-chan must be pretty scary, and that's why I gathered this many people."
129. I thought this was awfully extreme for fans... So this stalker girl was the one stirring them up...
130. [Yumi] "Then why not just kill me and be done with it..."
131. [Kana] "Ah, don't get the wrong idea. I'm not friends with those girls or anything, so I've got no obligation to actually follow through on what they asked."
132. [Schoolgirl D] "No, we're killing this one."
133. [Kana] "Just let me talk to her a little, would you?"
134. The girl called Nagayama drew closer to me.
135. And whispered into my ear.

