25. "Yes, rape is an extremely serious crime. But *that* is casually permitted."
26. "That being what?"
27. "If forcibly taking someone's body is a terribly evil thing,\nthen isn't forcibly taking someone's heart also evil?"
28. "No, that's not really evil, is it?"
29. "No, that's not true at all.\nA person who's had their heart forcibly stolen might, perhaps, suffer just as much as a person who's had their body forcibly taken......"
30. "And all the more so if both heart and body are taken,\nand if it happens to be a love that could never come true......"
31. "That's why I think the thing to guard against most, more than perverts, is love."
32. "Love?"
33. "Yes. Especially pure love -- and even more so, pure-love-style universal love."
34. "Universal love is the evil a maiden ought to guard against most."
35. "By that logic, Christ and Buddha are super-perverts......"
36. "Well, I don't really know much about great historical figures."
37. "But I do think it's only natural that people are on their guard against you, senpai."
38. "I see. I don't really know why, but I've got it -- I'm being watched out for."
39. "If you understand that......"
40. "Ah, class is about to end. I have to hurry back, or they'll realize I wasn't sitting out P.E."
41. Hikawa makes to hurry down the stairs.
42. I call out to her as she goes.
43. "So you -- you don't like me, is that it?"
44. "What kind of stupid thing are you saying?!\nI love you, senpai!"
45. "I see...... that's a relief."
46. "It's not a relief! Bleeeh!"
47. is what she told me.

=== lines=128 stop_reason=end_turn in=4551 out=3001 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. "Mmm, well then, I guess it's about time to wrap up for today."
2. "What? Is it that time already?"
3. "Yes. Would you take a look?"
4. "Yeah, not bad. Well, this is about as good as it gets."
5. "Is that so. I'm glad."
6. "Then shall we get ready to head home?"
7. "Right. Bag, bag~"
8. Rin went to fetch the bag she'd left by the window.
9. And then she just stood there, frozen.
10. It seemed she was looking down at something outside.
11. "Hm? It's nothing."
12. "Ah, that's right. I've got something to do today."
13. "Yeah, I have some errands, and I need to wash the oil painting supplies too, so could you head home ahead of me?"
