39. "With you, Senpai?"
40. "Yeah. Would you rather not?"
41. "There's no way I'd not want to. What are you saying..."
42. "No, Yumi's always around, so I figured maybe you wouldn't want to be alone together with me."
43. "What are you talking about, it's a reward for me."
44. "A reward for what?"
45. "Well, I wonder what for. Then shall we walk together for once? Our directions are pretty different, though?"
46. "Well, partway, at least."
47. I started to head toward the main gate.
48. And then--
49. "You'd better not go through the main gate."
50. "Right now the main gate's swarming with girls waiting for you, Kusanagi-senpai."
51. "What are you talking about. That couldn't possibly be true."
52. "It's really true. I just came through the main gate a moment ago..."
53. "It's not just a normal crowd?"
54. "Then want to try it? Want to walk home right through the middle of that swarm of trendy girls?"
55. "...No, I'll pass."
56. "Let's leave through the back gate. There was nobody over there."
57. "That's the opposite direction from the station, though."
58. "Yes, it'll be a detour, but what do you want to do?"
59. "For now, I'll do as you say, Hikawa..."
60. We left the school building through the back exit.
61. According to Hikawa, up until a few dozen minutes ago there had been girls waiting here too, apparently for me.\nI could hardly believe it, but... well, better safe than sorry.
62. "So we ended up out here again."
63. "Yes, from here we'll have to walk even further in the opposite direction from the station. Is that all right?"
64. "No problem. Either way, if we walked toward Yume-no-Ukisaka we'd be in full view from the main gate."
65. "Are you sure this is okay?"
66. "Going home with someone like me."
67. "What's that supposed to mean."
68. "Right now you could have your pick of girls, Kusanagi-senpai."
69. "So is it really all right to waste your time with someone like me?"
70. "That's a strange way to put it. And what do you mean 'pick of girls' anyway?\nThere aren't any such girls."
71. "What are you saying, are you ignoring the existence of those girls at the main gate?"
72. "Yeah, I'm ignoring them."
73. "I don't have the social skills to just suddenly get friendly with strangers of the opposite sex like that."
74. "In that case, what about Rin-senpai or..."
75. "Yeah, I've been teaching her painting lately. We do walk home together often."
76. "Why weren't you together today?"
77. "Who knows. I wonder why."
78. "Earlier, just by chance... I met eyes with Rin-senpai."
79. "Huh? Earlier? You two didn't meet, did you?"
80. "No, we didn't. I was walking across the schoolyard looking up at the art room. Wondering if anyone was there..."
81. "And there was a figure that looked like Rin-senpai..."
82. "What. If it just looked like her, you didn't actually meet eyes with her, did you?"
83. "I wonder. Can't you usually tell about those things?"
84. "I don't know... now that you mention it, I do kind of feel like I could, maybe..."
85. "Since you were with Rin-senpai today too, I thought you'd be walking home together as well."
86. "Ah, no, I don't mean anything by it, but..."
87. "I'm teaching Rin painting. That's all it is."
88. "That's all... is it."
89. Hikawa looked away.
90. "What, you seem dissatisfied."
91. "I'm not dissatisfied or anything."
92. "Senpai... how much do you remember?"
93. "About when we met at the cypress park."
94. "What. Is this some jab because I'd forgotten how that whole 'little sister' arrangement of yours started?"
95. "It's not a jab or anything, since you actually had forgotten."
96. "Yeah, sorry about that. I did forget.\nOr rather, I never imagined you'd been carrying that around all this time."
97. "That's a harsh way to put it. To me it's a precious memory."
98. "Maybe it was..."
99. "You're indifferent, aren't you."
100. "Indifferent? No, that's not it."
101. "Back then, I had my hands full, in my own way."
102. "Your hands full?"
103. "I remember that night well. No, there's no way I could forget it."
104. "But it was a struggle in its own way, back then.\nBecause you were unfortunately just too good at painting."
105. "'Unfortunately too good,' that's a strange way to put it. Hehe."
106. "This isn't a laughing matter. It really was tough."
107. "You didn't look like it was."
108. "I was putting on a front. I always wanted to look cool."
109. "That hasn't changed even now, has it."
110. "Really? I don't think I'm living my life putting on such a bluff these days..."
111. "If you're seriously saying that, then you have zero objectivity."
112. "Senpai, listen. I'm in love with you, you know."
113. "Well, I've got some confidence that I'm reasonably liked by you.\nIncidentally, I've got some confidence that I'm reasonably disliked by Kawachino too."
114. "Ah, as I thought, you really have no objectivity, Senpai. You don't understand anything."
115. "What. Was I wrong? So do you not like me as much as I thought?"
116. "What do you mean 'idiot,' I can't know what other people are feeling."
117. "Still, if you didn't like me much, I'd honestly find that sad."
118. "Really? It seems like it wouldn't matter to you either way how I felt about you, Senpai."
119. "If that's what you think, then this 'objectivity' of yours isn't much either."
120. "What's that supposed to mean..."
121. "But hey, why'd you go and say 'little sister'?"
122. "Because you said 'apprentice' was no good."
123. "No, even so, jumping straight to 'little sister' is a huge leap."
124. "Who knows. Honestly, I don't know."
125. "At the time, that just felt right."
126. "But being a little sister is nice, isn't it.\nBecause even if you're not a lover, you can still be by their side..."
127. "A friend can be by your side too, can't they."
128. "No, a friend won't do."

=== lines=68 stop_reason=end_turn in=3721 out=1806 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
