33. "K-Kusanagi-san..."
34. "Besides, if we're talking faint infatuation, it wasn't just back then."
35. "In fact, since I was a mama's boy, I might have felt it toward my own mother too."
36. "And that night..."
37. The cypress forest.
38. The girl beneath a white umbrella.
39. Her smile was like the moon.
40. Like the moon that reflects the sun's light, transforming its fierce blaze into a soft, gentle glow.
41. That blue flame kept painting death.
42. I was watching her, in that form.
43. "Wh-what is it, so suddenly. Staring at me like that..."
44. "Ah, sorry. I was thinking about something..."
45. "That kind of expression... is too unfair, you know... the timing, too..."
46. "That kind of face is a foul.\nK-Kusanagi-san, you're really way too unfair in all sorts of ways..."
47. "What. 'Unfair'..."
48. "Unfair is unfair... it's sneaky. Honestly..."
49. "That night. The ZYPRESSEN night.\nYou turned the cypresses into cherry blossoms in an instant, Senpai."
50. "You turned something black into something white, in a single instant."
