61. [Naoya] "Because you're crazy good at painting......"
62. [Rina] "That's not a reason!"
63. [Rina] "That's right."
64. [Naoya] "Well then, shall I teach you from now on?"
65. [NARRATION] I paused once, then spoke slowly.
66. [Naoya] "Probably, I can't teach you the way you're hoping for."
67. [Rina] "The way I'm hoping for?"
68. [Naoya] "You already know, don't you?"
69. [Naoya] "Why I said I couldn't teach you......"
70. [NARRATION] Hikawa's flushed face cooled a little.
71. [NARRATION] But her eyes still looked moist, as before.
72. [Rina] "Senpai, your paintings had changed."
73. [Rina] "From 'Sakura Day Rhapsody,' said to be your last work, up through partway into the piece we made together, your style had changed quite a bit."
74. [Rina] "Like your dominant hand wouldn't listen to you...... that sort of wrongness."
75. [Naoya] "But we did finish our collaboration, didn't we?"
76. [Rina] "Yes, that's why, just on that final night, it felt like your brushwork had returned -- it was a strange feeling."
77. [Naoya] "Ah...... maybe so."
78. [Rina] "Why was it that only on that last day, your brushwork returned?"
79. [Naoya] "It wasn't that it returned only on the last day -- I did it with the last of my strength......\nAfter that, I really couldn't paint anymore."
80. [Naoya] "So I can't paint anymore. It's not that I won't, I can't.\nFrom that point on, I gave up on leaving works behind as Kusanagi Naoya."
81. [Rina] "That work was your last?"
82. [Naoya] "Yeah, my last."
83. [Naoya] "Just as you pointed out. For a certain reason, I ruined my dominant hand. And I could no longer paint the way I used to."
84. [Naoya] "Except for that night......"
85. [Rina] "S-senpai, the reason you don't paint...... th-that's an absolute secret, isn't it?"
86. [Naoya] "It's an absolute secret."
87. [Rina] "Then why are you telling me so easily?"
88. [Naoya] "You said it. That things get through from a painting -- and if that's so, I figured hiding it was pointless."
89. [Rina] "Even so, to say it with your own mouth......"
90. [Naoya] "Well, you might not really get this, but."
91. [Naoya] "Having you call me sneaky, or unfair, all the time --\nit's kind of painful, you know."
92. [Naoya] "Believe it or not, I devoted my last brushstrokes to you."
93. [Rina] "Th-thank you very much......"
94. [Rina] "No, words like that aren't enough, I think......"
95. [Rina] "Or rather, why would you use your last brushstrokes for someone like me......\nI don't even know what to say in response......"
96. [Naoya] "It's fine. I didn't do it because I wanted gratitude......"
97. [Rina] "Helping someone out?"
98. [Naoya] "See, having it all written off as universal kindness like that, it's a bit galling too."
99. [Naoya] "Sometimes it isn't that......"
100. [Naoya] "Even I've got some ulterior motives, you know."
101. [Naoya] "Not for someone else. There are times when I do something because it's for this person......"
102. [Naoya] "I devoted my last painting to you. No one else."
103. [Naoya] "Exactly what that means -- I used my last right hand for you."
104. [Naoya] "But I don't regret it. If anything, I think it was fitting as a last."
105. [Naoya] "That's how much fun that last night was......\nFor me......"
106. [Rina] "S-senpai, you really are unfair!"
107. [Naoya] "What is......"
108. [Rina] "That, that's unfair!"
109. [Rina] "That kind of...... pained smile...... it's too unfair."
110. [Naoya] "No matter what I do, I turn out unfair, huh......"
111. [NARRATION] Hikawa fell silent just like that.
112. [Naoya] "Anyway, I'll teach you painting anytime. Just say the word."
113. [Rina] "I probably won't ask anymore......"
114. [Naoya] "I see. That's fine too."
115. [Rina] "Can I ask one last thing......"
116. [Rina] "That painting...... the one that vanished the night of the typhoon.\nHardly anyone got to see it."
117. [Rina] "And on a work like that, you used up the last of your strength, didn't you."
118. [Naoya] "Yeah, that's right. That's how it ended up."
119. [Rina] "Why was that?"
120. [Naoya] "Because I wanted to erase the scent of death from you."
121. [Rina] "Wh-why...... was it me......"
122. [Naoya] "I suppose I was captivated......"
123. [Rina] "Captivated?"
124. [Naoya] "Yeah, by your paintings, and by you......"
125. [Rina] "I see...... But the me from back then is no longer here......"
126. [Rina] "The me who was enchanted by death is no longer here."
127. [Naoya] "Yeah, I know."
128. [Naoya] "After all, I'm the one who turned you into a girl of my own liking."
129. [Naoya] "To accept death, to enjoy it, and then to gaze at life."
130. [Naoya] "The you of now, like that -- I like you."
131. [Naoya] "I love the Rina of now."
132. [Rina] "W-why would you say something like that?!"
133. [Naoya] "Who knows. But probably, the time when I have to properly settle things with my own heart is coming, not too far off."
134. [Naoya] "And depending on that answer, well, maybe I might die, or something......"
135. [Rina] "Die? Why?"
136. [Naoya] "No, just as an example.\nBut either way, the time when I have to face it properly will come."
137. [Naoya] "It's just that, over the course of my life, I plan to produce only one answer."

=== lines=18 stop_reason=end_turn in=1866 out=438 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. [Rina] "Over your whole life? One answer?"
2. [Naoya] "Yeah, I get why you all tease me for being some philanthropist.\nBut that's not it."
3. [Naoya] "I'm human too."
4. [Naoya] "I'm not living solely on some spirit of service."
5. Hikawa began to cry right there on the spot.
6. [Rina] "Coward! Senpai, you're the worst kind of coward!"
7. [Rina] "Because Senpai, with that absolute power of yours, you grip my heart tight......"
8. [Rina] "That's why I have to run away from you, Senpai."
9. [Rina] "Otherwise......"
10. [Naoya] "That's fine too.\nI'll just make my decision......"
11. [Naoya] "You should make yours."
12. [Naoya] "Koi can hold up one-way, but ren'ai can't stand on one side alone."
13. [Naoya] "Even so, love doesn't disappear."
14. [Rina] "Kusanagi-san......"
15. [Rina] "Kusanagi-san, you idiot!"
16. Hikawa yelled at me at the top of her lungs.
17. I understood well enough what those words meant.
18. And to that, too, I would have to produce an answer before long.

=== lines=127 stop_reason=end_turn in=5121 out=3378 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. I'm staring up at the sky.
2. The scenery barely registers in my eyes......
3. "Rina-chan, mind if I sit next to you for a bit?"
4. "Ah...... Rin-senpai."
5. While I was spacing out, Rin-senpai had come to stand right in front of me.\nI hadn't noticed at all.
6. "There we go."
7. And then she sat down right beside me.
8. "Nice autumn sky, isn't it......"
9. "The weather's been so nice lately, it's really been putting me in a good mood......"
10. "Hah...... is that so."
11. "You don't look like you're in a very good mood, though, Rina-chan."
12. "Huh? No, it's not really like that......"
13. "It very much is like that. Every time I've seen you since yesterday, you've been spacing out."
14. "...... Ahaha, is that so."
15. "Rina-chan, did you turn Nao-kun down?"
16. "Huh? W-why do you ask?\nDid senpai say something?"
17. "There's no way Nao-kun would say something like that.\nAnyway, watching the two of you lately, it's obvious."
18. "Just from watching us lately......?"
19. "Yeah. I don't know the reason, though......"
20. "It's not that I turned him down or anything like that......"
21. "Then you're going out?"
22. "W-we're not going out."
23. "Oh. Then, Rina-chan, is it that you don't really like Nao-kun that much?"
24. "W-why, would you ask...... that."
25. "Nao-kun confessed to you, right?"
26. "It wasn't really a confession, exactly......"
27. "Either way, you didn't give him a good answer."
28. "You don't really like Nao-kun, do you?"
29. "Which is it? That much I'd like to know."
30. "Oh my, giving me the silent treatment?"
31. "I think I might just confess to him myself."
32. "Confess?"
33. "I've been in love with Nao-kun for the longest time, you know.\nSo much that I transferred to this school just for him."
34. "So, if there's a chance for me too, then I want to go out with Nao-kun."
35. "I-if it's Rin-senpai...... th-the two of you would make a lovely pair......"
36. "You think so? But Nao-kun is really popular, you know."
37. "If it comes to that...... Rin-senpai is too......\nT-the two of you together...... no one would complain."
38. "Really? No one would complain?"
39. "All right!"
40. Rin-senpai stood up.
41. "Nao-kun must be lonely with his broken heart, and right now, I feel like even I could make him mine! That's it, I'll confess!"
42. "If someone's kind to him, the way he is now, he'll fall head over heels."
43. "Well then, that's how it is."
44. Rin-senpai started to walk away.
45. "R-Rin-senpai......"
46. "What is it?"
47. "N-nothing......"
48. "Really? Your face doesn't look like it's nothing."
49. "S-senpai, did you come all the way up to the roof just to say that?"
50. "'Just to say that' -- how rude.\nWhether or not Rina-chan turned Nao-kun down is quite an important matter, you know?"
51. "If Rina-chan turned Nao-kun down, that means there might be a chance for me too, right? That's incredibly important."
52. "...... K-Kusanagi-senpai probably isn't like that......"
53. "Hm? Not like that -- meaning not like what, exactly?"
54. "He's not the kind of person who would go out with someone else just because his heart is broken!"
55. "Yes, yes, that might be true.\nIn that case, I'll save the confession for later, and just be kind to him for now, how's that?"
56. "Taking my time, slowly...... that way I can win Nao-kun over too."
57. "Even so......"
58. "Even so? Nao-kun won't go out with anyone?\nIs that what you want to say, Rina-chan?"
59. "If that's what you want to say, then you're cruel, Rina-chan.\nYou pushed him away knowing that Nao-kun wouldn't go out with anyone just from a broken heart......"
60. "And yet you won't answer whether you like or dislike Nao-kun."
61. "Even if you push him away a little, Nao-kun is so straightforward that he wouldn't waver.\nHe'd come back to you, properly.\nIsn't that what you're thinking, Rina-chan?"
62. "And what does that make me?"
63. "That's not it......"
64. "Then what is it?"
65. "Are you worried about things with Yumi-chan?"
66. "Ah, no, no, I don't actually know what happened between the two of you.\nBut Yumi-chan likes Rina-chan as more than just a friend, that much is certain, right?"
67. "I don't know the details, but I was wondering if maybe your refusing Nao-kun has something to do with that......"
68. "But if Rina-chan is putting Nao-kun on hold for such a trivial reason, then I'll make Nao-kun mine by any means necessary."
69. "That's why I came back here......"
70. "R-Rin-senpai, did you come back to Yumihari to go out with Kusanagi-senpai?"
71. "No, that's not it."
72. "I've been thinking about a certain phrase for a long time......"
73. "A certain phrase?"
74. "I've heard it before."
75. "Nakahara Chuuya's 'Spring Day Rhapsody.'"
76. "When we were kids, when Nao-kun's mother passed away, Nao-kun murmured it under his breath......"
77. "Back then, not understanding the true meaning of that poem, I got angry."
78. "Asking him why he'd say something so sad."
79. "I was such a fool...... I wasn't thinking about Nao-kun's feelings at all."
80. "But if someone told me you have to kill yourself when the one you love dies, I wouldn't want that...... especially if it were someone I loved......"
81. "Yes, but this poem has more to it."
82. "Nakahara Chuuya lost his beloved son at a young age.\nIn 'Songs of Bygone Days,' 'Spring Day Rhapsody' especially expresses those feelings in the most straightforward way."
83. "The one you love has died.\nA poem that makes you feel that emotion painfully."
84. "You know, I've been thinking all this time about why Nao-kun spoke those words back then."
85. "And to reach an answer, an answer I could accept in my own way, I came back to Yumihari."
86. "That's the reason I returned to this town......"
87. "Kusanagi-senpai's final work. 'Sakura Day Rhapsody,' right."
88. "Yes, I think that title was given with that in mind."
89. "You see. I think he probably can't love another person just for himself......"
90. "Senpai can't love people?"
91. "The person Kusanagi Naoya is, I think, is someone possessed of a spirit of service, no matter how far you go......"
92. "That's why...... Nao-kun sticks his nose into everything......"
93. "It's been a few months since I came back to Yumihari. Actually, I've been looking into a lot of things."
94. "And I've learned all sorts of things."
95. "Around the time Nao-kun and Rina-chan first met, it seems Nao-kun was leaving studies in various places."
96. "The general story is that he laid down his brush after 'Sakura Day Rhapsody,' but after that, he painted an incredible number of studies."
97. "On canvas, on drawing paper, even on walls......"
98. "But almost all of the paintings from that period were destroyed by his own hand."
99. "As though he were hiding them......"
100. "He was painting on all sorts of things besides walls?"
101. "Yes. By chance, I met someone who had known Kusanagi Ken'ichirou-san for a long time. That person had a few of Nao-kun's works that had escaped being destroyed."
102. "What were those works like?"
103. "Unfinished...... and scribbled over on top."
104. "I don't know why.\nHe could no longer paint with the same brushwork as 'Sakura Day Rhapsody.'"
105. "That much is certain......"
106. "But for some reason, that fact and the word 'service' that Nakahara Chuuya spoke of fit together strangely within me......"
107. "Ah, this person is trying, all this time, to distract himself from the sorrow of his mother's death through the form of service......"
108. "I can't help but think that......"
109. "If that's the case, then that person's love, no matter how far it goes, is nothing but service......"
110. "If that's true, it's a lonely story."
111. "Yes, that's why Nao-kun needs someone to love him."
112. "He probably lost his own love along with his beloved mother...... which is exactly why he needs someone to love him."
113. "So if Rina-chan won't love Nao-kun, then I will love him."
114. "That's what I think."
115. "If Rina-chan won't love him, then I'll love him for you.\nOtherwise, he'll never be freed from that spirit of service......"
116. "I -- I!"
117. "You?"
118. "I -- I think that's wrong."
119. "S-senpai, you can love someone properly too!"
120. "I don't think you're going to stay caught up in your mother's death forever, senpai."
121. "You can love people, properly!"
122. "...... Why do you think that?"
123. "I don't know, but senpai's brushwork is too full of love to be summed up by a word like 'service.'"
124. "For senpai to say she can't love people -- that's just Rin-senpai deciding it on her own!"
125. "I can't believe that!"
126. "Is that so? Isn't that just Rina-chan deciding it on her own?"
127. "Maybe so, but,\nstill, I think Rin-senpai is wrong!"

=== lines=69 stop_reason=end_turn in=3859 out=1573 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. "Good eyes......"
2. "Those eyes just now were good, Rina-chan."
3. "Eyes?"
4. "Rina-chan, you're such a good girl, you never let your true feelings show, do you."
5. "But just now, you showed clear revulsion toward me."
6. "R-revulsion... th-there's no way I'd... toward Rin-senpai..."
7. "Lies, lies. It's too late to say that now.\nThose eyes just now were revulsion aimed at me."
8. "But that's the right response."
9. "You mustn't accept what I just said."
10. "It's true that Kusanagi-kun has that possibility......"
11. "But at the very least, the person who loves him has to believe in his love."
12. "Kusanagi-kun has to be freed from that spirit of service by now......"
13. "Overcoming his mother's death......, and then meeting his father's death......,\nhe has to overcome it......"
14. "That's why Kusanagi-kun can properly love someone."
15. "I think Kusanagi-kun has found, properly, the person he loves."
16. "Rin-senpai......"
17. "Rina-chan, you love Kusanagi-kun, don't you?"
18. "No going silent on me!"
19. "Yes, honesty is a virtue.\nIf you'd given me another half-hearted answer here, I was ready to throw you."
20. "Then I'd have liked to say something half-hearted and get thrown by you, senpai......"
21. "No way. Then I'd have to fight Yumi-chan, right?\nI love Yumi-chan."
22. "Ahaha...... you love Yumi......"
23. "By the way, I hated the Rina-chan from a moment ago."
24. "But the Rina-chan of right now, I don't dislike."
