=== lines=138 stop_reason=end_turn in=5974 out=3368 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. "Yes, you got it right away."
2. "Well, I've heard that people in Kansai don't put sugar in tamagoyaki -- though I hear they do add mirin."
3. "Mirin makes it sweet. I like tamagoyaki with just salt."
4. "Kawachino, do you dislike sweet things?"
5. "No, I prefer other dishes on the sweeter side."
6. "That's right, with sukiyaki and such, Yumi tries to dump in a ton of sugar."
7. "Sugar makes it better."
8. "So, this teriyaki chicken I made today is pretty sweet."
9. "Yaay."
10. "I see, so this teriyaki was seasoned the way Kawachino likes."
11. "Yes. So if you have any complaints, you don't have to eat my tamagoyaki."
12. "I've got no complaints. My mother didn't put sugar in her tamagoyaki either."
13. "Really? Was she from Kansai too?"
14. "No, I don't know. Family circumstances are a bit unusual -- I don't even know where my mother was born."
15. "So this tamagoyaki tastes nostalgic to me."
16. "I'm bad at making tamagoyaki, so I couldn't do it this well."
17. "Th-thanks...... You praise people so directly, don't you."
18. "Well, it's delicious."
19. "But if you have a tamagoyaki pan, pretty much anyone can make it, you know."
20. "That's what people who can make it always say."
21. "Isn't that exactly what you do, senpai?"
22. Even something as simple as a home-cooked meal carries the taste of each family.
23. Eating a bento made by someone else like this was quite enjoyable.
24. "But I'm glad. I was pretty nervous, you know."
25. "You're such a good cook, so I was scared you'd be picky about the flavor."
