27. "It's the same with everything. The people who don't do it are the ones who talk big like critics.\nThose who actually do it don't throw words around lightly, and they know how to properly enjoy what others have made."
28. Chatting about nothing in particular, we made our way through lunch.
29. Though I probably shouldn't say it -- food someone else makes for you really does taste good.
30. It was a deeply satisfying time for me.
31. "Let's draw pictures!"
32. "Pictures?"
33. "Yes, like this, on the ground."
34. Hikawa started scratching a drawing into the ground with a stick.
35. "What is it? You planning to draw the Nazca Lines?"
36. "That might be nice too. But this way, senpai, you don't have to worry about your hand, right?"
37. I picked up a stick too, and started drawing on the ground.
38. For starters, I tried drawing a dog.
39. "Wow, amazing, a single line -- what incredible drawing skill."
40. "Big drawings tend to get the proportions off...... well, there are various techniques."
41. "Draw a wolf!"
42. "Yes, a wolf."
43. "Hmm, I'm not really sure but I'll give it a try."
