1. There's nothing more unpleasant than being called out to by some annoying guy at a time like this.
2. "Hey, what are you doing out here alone?"
3. I ignore the man beside me.
4. "Same as ever, Kawachino. Never one for pleasantries."
5. Why does this guy know my name?
6. "Who are you? No, never mind, I don't care. You're unpleasant, so please get lost."
7. "Don't be like that."
8. That was when I looked at the man's face for the first time.
9. Running jersey, drenched in sweat. He must be out on a run.
10. "You're in the middle of a run, right? I don't know what you're training for, but please just mind your own business. It's unpleasant having you take an interest in me."
11. "Ah, training, huh. Yeah, sure."
12. Laughing, the man sat down beside me.
13. "Huh? What is with you?"
14. "I've been hearing about you from the old crowd from that class -- same as ever, aren't you.\nYour getup's toned down a lot, though..."
15. "That class... crowd?"
16. "Yeah, we all still keep in touch now and then. Everyone gripes about how Kawachino's no fun to hang out with."
17. There's something familiar about his face...
18. "Okazawa?!"
19. "Yeah, Okazawa. Who else would it be?"
20. "No, I mean, your whole vibe's really changed..."
21. "It's been four years since then. Of course I've changed."
22. "So? What's up with you, Kawachino? Getting all sentimental at sunset in a place like this?"
23. "Ah, no, I wasn't getting sentimental or anything."
24. "That's how it looked to me."
25. "You're imagining things. I'm just normal..."
26. "I don't really see the normal you sitting somewhere like this staring at the sea, though."
27. "There can be that kind of normal too..."
28. "Heartbreak... is it?"
29. "...What's that supposed to mean?"
30. "But I got it right, didn't I?"
31. Okazawa said it a little gently.
32. "Aah, geez, who says that to someone the first time they see them in ages?"
33. "Hikawa?"
34. I don't answer.
35. "Hikawa was cute, after all. Word is she's a real beauty now too.\nWhen people talk about the cute first-year at Yumihari, it's usually her."
36. "It's a given that Rina is cute."
37. "That's a matter of opinion."
38. "But if Kawachino got her heart broken, then that means I'm finally at the starting line too, right?"
39. "Just what I said."
40. "What are you getting the wrong idea about... whether I got my heart broken or not has nothing to do with you."
41. "I'm a lesbian. Getting my heart broken doesn't change who I'm attracted to."
42. "Ahaha, what are you talking about? I loved you, Kawachino -- of anyone, I know that best."
43. Being laughed at so openly, I got a little embarrassed.
44. "Th-then, what starting line are you talking about?"
45. "I always wondered what kind of face you'd make when you got your heart broken..."
46. "To me, you were unbelievably strong, unshakeable..."
47. "That's a misunderstanding. I'm not that strong."
48. "No, to me, you were absolute..."
49. "So unless I got to see even the face of your heartbreak, you'd stay someone I could never reach."
50. "You still can't reach me. I'm a lesbian."
51. "That's not what I mean."
52. "I mean, I can finally talk to you naturally like this."
53. "Talk to me naturally?"
54. "Was it that you couldn't talk to me naturally before?"
55. "Yeah, I couldn't. I was always nervous around you."
56. "Ever since we were kids..."
57. That's just you overestimating me...
58. I'm not strong, or anything of the sort...
59. And I'm really, really lonely.
60. "Well, guess I should get going."
61. "What club are you in?"
62. "Basketball."
63. "I'm still a first-year so I can't make the starting lineup, but I'm working hard in my own way."
64. "Cheer up, Kawachino."
65. "I'm fine."
66. "You don't look it. Hikawa isn't the only cute girl around."
67. "No, Rina's cuteness is off the charts."
68. "Even so, someday you'll find someone you like."
69. "What about you? You got shot down spectacularly by me, didn't you?"
70. "Me? For the time being, club is enough."
71. "I don't feel like chasing after girls right now."
72. "Right now, basketball's all I need."
73. "I see. Look at you, living your best life. Go die."
74. "How is a guy with no girlfriend, throwing himself into club activities, 'living his best life'?!"
75. "But you look happy."
76. "Well, sure. Each day's a healthy one."
77. "I see. That's good, then."
78. "But someday --"
79. "Someday, when I get a cute girlfriend too, Kawachino, give me your blessing, okay?"
80. "Yeah, leave it to me. In exchange, land a girl cute enough to make me jealous."
81. "Same goes for you, Kawachino."
82. "Well, thanks."
83. "See you, then. Kawachino."
84. "Yeah, drop me a text once in a while."
85. "You're the one who never writes back."
86. "I won't. Never write back."
87. "But still, it makes me happy to get a message."
88. "That's our boss for you. Selfish as ever."
89. "It's not so much selfish -- I'm just lonely."
90. "Ahaha, I knew that."
91. "Right, I'm heading off."
92. Just like that, Okazawa started running again.
93. His figure grew smaller and smaller.
94. And then I was alone.
95. A sea without waves.
96. A sea you couldn't call beautiful even out of politeness.
97. And yet, it seemed the kind of sea you'd never tire of watching...
98. Even so, I looked at the sea only for a little while,
99. and then slowly began to walk.
100. The world has taken on the full look of autumn.
101. Even so, the ZYPRESSEN must be as black as ever.
102. "ZYPRESSEN in a single row against the autumn sky"
103. "drinking in the ether darkly"
104. "and from their dark ranks even the dream-floating sea shines out"
105. "the waves of heat-haze and the white polarized light"
106. "the true words are lost"
107. "the clouds are torn and fly across the sky"
108. "Ah, along the floor of the shining October sea
109. gnashing my teeth, blazing, I come and go"
110. "I am such an asura"
111. "ZYPRESSEN, ever blacker"
112. "the sparks of the clouds pour down"
113. Evening is drawing near.
114. The tall goldenrods begin to stir.
115. A blood-red glare of a setting sun.
116. My eyes, gazing at it, are red as well.
117. The wind is sharp, cold, and -- pleasant.

=== lines=81 stop_reason=end_turn in=3592 out=2210 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. "How's he doing?"
2. "Naoya, I mean. Naoya."
3. "Ah, Naoya, huh...... He seemed to have a lot on his mind."
4. "I'll bet......"
5. "Why did you leave the whole inheritance to him?"
6. "Well, there's a lot to it. All sorts of things."
7. "Come to think of it, who was that girl you brought along, Kusanagi-san?"
8. "Hmm, well now......"
9. "Not that it's really my place to say anything. Still, roping Naoya into the Natsume family's affairs at his age -- isn't that a bit cruel?"
10. "That can't be helped. Naoya is a Kusanagi. And being a Kusanagi means being fated to get caught up in serious business."
11. "What kind of family is that......"
12. "What kind, indeed -- you know full well, don't you?"
13. "I only know a little. Kusanagi-san, you were the Madonna every boy at Yumihari Academy pined after. And you eloped with Mizuna-san."
14. "Elopement, huh...... Well, I suppose that's how it looked from the outside......"
15. "Even without looking from the outside, that was an elopement, wasn't it?"
16. "Does it count as one, I wonder......"
17. "I learned a bit more about the circumstances afterward. Ai-chan from the Natsume family was assigned to Yumihari, after all."
18. "Right, that's true, Ai is a teacher now...... at Yumihari......"
19. "Well, no wonder I've gotten old...... That tiny little girl is a teacher now, of all things...... Though her height's still tiny as ever."
20. "Say that in front of Ai-sensei and she'll kill you. She's touchy about her height."
21. "There's nothing to be touchy about. Ai was born with such good looks. And being small is a reward, for guys who're into that sort of thing."
22. "That is a huge taboo in front of Ai-sensei."
23. "Is that so. Well, I was always making Ai angry anyway......"
24. "Really? But surely not recently, right?"
25. "No, no, I got yelled at pretty badly very recently."
26. "Did you now. What did you do?"
27. "No, the opposite. She got mad because I didn't do anything."
28. "Because you didn't do anything?"
29. "'Why didn't you come back until your illness had gotten this bad?' -- something like that. She really tore into me."
30. "Well, of course...... Honestly, I thought the same thing."
31. "But you don't get mad at me."
32. "Well, of course not. You're a proper adult, Kusanagi-san."
33. "Yeah, 'What kind of proper adult does something like that!' -- that's how she yelled at me......"
34. "She's always been a fiercely stubborn girl. Seeing her cry her eyes out like that stings a bit."
35. "Then couldn't you have just gone to the hospital? You've been in poor health for quite a while, haven't you?"
36. "Even so, I want to decide the length of my own life myself."
37. "And? Did it end up matching your calculations, this lifespan you set for yourself?"
38. "I wonder...... Just barely made it in time, maybe? Strange thing, really."
39. "Just barely made it in time?"
40. "If that's my terminus, then it's a remarkably well-crafted story."
41. "Because I had my epitaph carved into me while I was still alive......"
42. "Whew...... Honestly, you're a sinful man, Kusanagi-san."
43. "When I asked the same question last time, you said, 'I miscalculated a little.'"
44. "I see. Well then, has Naoya safely settled everything?"
45. "Who knows. I don't know that. And besides, there's no telling what he'll ultimately do with the inheritance."
46. "I see. Well, I don't know the details, but you seem to be in high spirits, Kusanagi-san."
47. "That I am. Fairly so."
48. "Honestly, what a selfish man."
49. "That's right. I'm the most selfish there is. So I've lived my life as selfishly as could be."
50. "It's been a pretty thrilling, interesting life."
51. "Thrilling and interesting...... huh. Well, I suppose it has been."
52. "Tonight, my last supper. Care to sit and listen?"
53. "Last supper, you say...... there's neither food nor drink."
54. "There's drink. And for a side dish, my old stories."
55. "Old stories as a side dish, huh."
56. "Yeah, it's a somewhat hefty side dish, mind you. Stay and listen."
57. "When you tell me to listen, Kusanagi-san, there's no way I can refuse."
58. "I won't force you, you know?"
59. "Even without forcing me, I can't refuse. So then, will you serve up this dish of yours?"
60. "I feel a bit of loneliness at the thought of your dying, too. Maybe your story can fill the hunger in my heart, a little."
61. "I see, that's good to hear. Do you remember? Back when I was a teacher at Yumihari Academy......"
62. "Yes, I remember. That's right about when I was a student there."
63. "Right, you were in the art club."
64. "You often dropped by the club too, Kusanagi-san."
65. "I had nowhere else to go......"
66. "That aside, even back then...... Mizuna was lovely."
67. "No arguments there. She was famous for her beauty."
68. "Right, right. Well, if she hadn't been born with such beauty, she probably wouldn't have had such an unhappy fate......"
69. "...... Is that a story I should be hearing?"
70. "Yeah, in fact, please listen. It's too heavy for me to keep locked up in my chest alone......"
71. "Then wouldn't Naoya be the one to tell?"
72. "As for Naoya, someone else will tell him everything......"
73. "Someone else?"
74. "Yeah, that girl knows the story of me and Mizuna better than anyone...... Someday, the day will come when she tells Naoya everything......"
75. "So I want you to be the one to listen......"
76. "In order to drink the finest liquor tonight......"
77. "Liquor, is it......"
78. "Yeah, the fine wine called happiness......"
79. "Happiness......"
80. "I don't have much time left. My junior in life. That's precisely why I want you to hear my story."
81. "A story for the drinking of happiness......"

