50. [Mizuna] "Eh? Sensei? Eh? Ehhh? Th-that means......"
51. [Kotoko] "The Natsume clan is a stubborn bunch. Fall for someone, and they'll stake their lives on it.\nWell, this one's still unreliable, but when it counts, he comes through. He is my grandson, after all."
52. [Mizuna] "Eh? Ehhh? G-grandson? Eh? Your grandson?\nAre you Sensei's grandmother?"
53. [Ken'ichirou] "Yeah, she never married so our surnames differ, but Natsume Kotoko is my grandmother."
54. [Mizuna] "Eh? Ehhh? I-is that so!? I-I'm so sorry for my rudeness!\nU-um, my name is Nakamura Mizuna--!"
55. [Kotoko] "What are you getting all formal about now? What a funny girl. You didn't shrink at all when you knew I was the boss of the Natsume yakuza."
56. [Kotoko] "Or is that it? The fact that I'm his blood relative matters more to you -- meaning you really have fallen for him too?"
57. [Mizuna] "Th-that's,\nno, in my heart, I won't deny it.\nB-but, I......"
58. [Kotoko] "Oi! Straighten up!"
59. [NARRATION] She barked at the fidgeting Mizuna.
60. [NARRATION] With Mizuna standing at attention, Granny Natsume slowly circled around her.\nAs though sizing her up......
61. [Kotoko] "I see, I see......"
62. [Kotoko] "Young lady, you've got good eyes."
63. [Kotoko] "Steady eyes. Composed eyes.\nYou must have been through some rough things......"
64. [Kotoko] "But you're not broken. Not one bit.\nYou're trying to fight against that fate.\nGood. That's how it should be."
65. [Kotoko] "A woman isn't only there to have things taken from her."
66. [Kotoko] "In my younger days, I too was always being taken from...... but well, it pays to live a long life. Nowadays, mine's a life of nothing but taking."
67. [Ken'ichirou] "That's abnormal......"
68. [Kotoko] "Ahn? It's fine. Those who take do it prepared to be taken from.\nSuch folk can grapple in the same ring."
69. [Kotoko] "But someone from a different ring taking is a foul.\nJust like those men did."
70. [Mizuna] "Thank you.\nUntil now I've just let things happen to me, so it felt so good."
71. [Kotoko] "Glad to hear it. But this doesn't end here."
72. [Ken'ichirou] "This old woman talks a big game about honor and duty, but she doesn't move for free. Money's what makes yakuza move."
73. [Kotoko] "That's exactly right. My grandson lost the use of his arm. I'll be collecting a full billion yen."
74. [Mizuna] "So you really are his grandmother."
75. [Kotoko] "Yeah, well, times being what they were, some of my children died, and there's plenty I haven't seen in years."
76. [Kotoko] "This Kusanagi Ken'ichirou is one of the few grandchildren I can actually meet face to face.\nOne way or another, an old yakuza hag doesn't have many grandkids willing to keep in touch."
77. [Ken'ichirou] "The hell are you talking about? If it hadn't been a profit for you, you wouldn't have even heard me out. It's always about the money with you!"
78. [Kotoko] "Damn right. For us yakuza, profit is everything. Any talk that isn't profit isn't worth even a second of my time."
79. [Ken'ichirou] "Really, everything this old woman says is nonsense......"
80. [Kotoko] "Chirping away like a noisy brat. Yasu, give him a bit of a working over."
81. [Ken'ichirou] "W-wait!"
82. [Mizuna] "P-please wait!"
83. [Kotoko] "It's fine. This is one way of welcoming him back."
84. [NARRATION] After that, Yasu drove me to the hospital.
85. [NARRATION] A back-alley doctor, though......
86. [NARRATION] Well, the doctor was skilled.\nA man who only ever treats folk hovering on the edge of life and death......
87. [NARRATION] He operated on me right away.
88. [NARRATION] Said my arm might be left with some lasting damage.
89. [NARRATION] Well, I'd left the injury untended for tens of hours, so it couldn't be helped.
90. [Mizuna] "Your face is still swollen......"
91. [Ken'ichirou] "Yeah, I left it alone after they hit me......"
92. [Mizuna] "You're always so reckless......"
93. [Ken'ichirou] "Well, this time I'll admit I'm feeling it."
94. [Mizuna] "But, thank you.\nEven just a little bit, we got back at them, so I'm satisfied......"
95. [Ken'ichirou] "You shouldn't be satisfied with that."
96. [Ken'ichirou] "I'll save you, Mizuna. No matter what."
97. [Mizuna] "Why would you go so far for someone like me?"
98. [Ken'ichirou] "Ahaha, come to think of it, I haven't confessed yet, have I."
99. [Ken'ichirou] "But Granny Natsume beat me to saying it......\nThat old woman says too damn much."
100. [Mizuna] "Granny Natsume is a good person......"
101. [Ken'ichirou] "That's not true. The Natsume people only move by weighing gains and losses."
102. [Ken'ichirou] "In that sense, I'm the same."
103. [Mizuna] "Gains and losses? Really?"
104. [Ken'ichirou] "I wouldn't have come to this mansion in the first place without some ulterior motive."
105. [Ken'ichirou] "When I started coming to this mansion, an old lover of mine told me we'd become enemies from then on."
106. [Mizuna] "A lover? Your girlfriend?"
107. [Ken'ichirou] "Back in the day. I was such a mess she got fed up with me.\nAnd then she went and married someone else."
108. [Ken'ichirou] "Yeah, that's how it goes."
109. [Ken'ichirou] "And on top of that, Saki's husband is that very Nakamura Shouichi.\nSeriously, what a joke. A total case of getting cuckolded."
110. [Mizuna] "Cuckolded?"
111. [Ken'ichirou] "Ah, nothing you need to worry about."
112. [Ken'ichirou] "But I came here even after being told the woman I once loved would oppose me.\nA man like that isn't doing this out of goodwill or brotherly love, is he?"
113. [Ken'ichirou] "Mizuna. Ever since we first met, I've loved you."
114. [Mizuna] "Eh? First met? Ehhh? I acted horribly toward you, didn't I?"
115. [Ken'ichirou] "You had this manner that pushed people away, and yet you were so considerate.\nThe moment I met you, I thought -- this girl must have something going on."
116. [Mizuna] "The moment we met? Really?"
117. [Ken'ichirou] "Yeah, don't underestimate an artist's eye.\nWe're drawn in by a person's distinctive expression......"
118. [Mizuna] "I don't deserve to be loved by you, Kusanagi-san."
119. [Ken'ichirou] "Why do you think that?"
120. [Mizuna] "B-because...... I've, I've been defiled by those men......"
121. [Ken'ichirou] "Defiled? How?"
122. [Mizuna] "My body -- by those men!"
123. [Mizuna] "My body......"
124. [Ken'ichirou] "That doesn't matter. Don't worry about it."
125. [Ken'ichirou] "It isn't something for you to torment yourself over.\nOf course, I'll make them pay the price for it."
126. [Mizuna] "But, but, I--"
127. [Ken'ichirou] "All right. All right. Then do this for me.\nJust while you're with me, for my sake, forget about it."
128. [Mizuna] "For your sake, Kusanagi-san?"
129. [Ken'ichirou] "Also, stop with the Kusanagi-san. Call me Ken'ichirou-san."
130. [Mizuna] "Eh? Ah? U-um...... Ken'ichirou...... san."
131. [Ken'ichirou] "Good, good. What a cute one you are."
132. [Mizuna] "W-waah--"
133. [NARRATION] I pulled Mizuna into my arms.
134. [NARRATION] At first she was flustered, but then Mizuna held me back too.
135. [Mizuna] "......You're warm."
136. [Mizuna] "So people are warm......"
137. [Ken'ichirou] "We're mammals, so yeah, people are warm."
138. [Mizuna] "The warmth of a person is such a comforting thing......"
139. [Ken'ichirou] "You know the phrase 'human skin'? What word suits it after?"
140. [Mizuna] "I wonder? Is it 'yearn for,' after all?"
141. [Ken'ichirou] "That's right. Human skin's the kind of thing that feels good enough to make you yearn for it."
142. [Mizuna] "Why is that...... I should be feeling something like this for the first time......"
143. [Ken'ichirou] "Does it feel nostalgic?"
144. [Mizuna] "Yes, why is the warmth of holding another person so comforting, so nostalgic......?"

