24. [Ai] "Well, it was someone I loved dearly. I suppose that's why I enjoyed it."
25. [Naoya] "Come to think of it, was that bike a hand-me-down?"
26. [Ai] "Yeah, it's a hand-me-down.\nIf you put it that way, I suppose this counts as part of Kusanagi Ken'ichirou's legacy too."
27. [Naoya] "What? That was Dad's bike?"
28. [Ai] "You didn't know? Ken'ichirou-san has ridden this since I was a child."
29. [Ai] "You've never seen it?"
30. [Naoya] "The dad I knew didn't ride a motorcycle, I'm pretty sure."
31. [Ai] "Now that you mention it, this bike is noisy, so he may have refrained from riding it after you were born."
32. [Naoya] "Him? For my sake? Would he show that kind of consideration?"
33. [Ai] "No, for Mizuna-san. Mizuna-neesama.\nHe used to ride up to the Natsume estate on this bike, but Mizuna-neesama detested it."
34. [NARRATION] Well, considering it makes this much noise......
35. [Ai] "And, one way or another, it is dangerous. That was probably part of it too."
36. [Naoya] "Come to think of it, in New York I have a vague memory of him riding a moped -- was that the reason?"
37. [Ai] "A moped...... Naoya, you really have no interest in motorcycles, do you......"
38. [Naoya] "No, I'm pretty sure it was a moped...... Wasn't it?"
39. [Ai] "That's not the issue...... Well, it doesn't really matter......"
40. [Ai] "At this rate, you may have seen this bike any number of times too.\nJust that you don't remember, Naoya......"
41. [Naoya] "Is that so? Now that you mention it, I feel like maybe......"
42. [NARRATION] Dad's motorcycle, huh......
43. [NARRATION] Once she said it, it did start to feel that way -- strange how that goes.
44. [Ai] "More importantly, let's get going."
45. [Naoya] "How?"
46. [Ai] "On foot, of course.\nI'll push the bike along."
47. [Naoya] "Huh? You're pushing that bike?\nThe supermarket's a fair distance."
48. [Ai] "Heheh, I don't train my body for show, so don't worry."
49. [Ai] "This isn't the first time I've pushed it home. This bike breaks down mid-ride now and then. When it does, I push it home every time."
50. [Naoya] "You're riding a hell of a bike."
51. [Ai] "It's an old bike, that's all. It's a vehicle you enjoy all of that as part of the deal."
52. [Naoya] "I... can't relate......"
53. [NARRATION] We set off toward the supermarket.
54. [Naoya] "Say, Ai, did you love my dad?"
55. [Ai] "Hm? That's out of the blue. What made you think so?"
56. [Naoya] "Ah, well, you said 'someone I loved dearly.'"
57. [Ai] "Oh, that.\nWell...... yes, I loved him dearly."
58. [Ai] "But by that measure, I also loved Grandmother Natsume dearly, and I love you dearly too."
59. [Naoya] "I see...... in that sense.\nAh, I thought you meant it in a romantic sense."
60. [Ai] "A romantic sense, huh...... I see. The words 'love dearly' do carry that meaning too."
61. [Ai] "That said, by the time I met him Ken'ichirou belonged to Mizuna-neesama...... There wasn't even room for that kind of feeling to enter, I think."
62. [Naoya] "So? If he hadn't been together with my mother, you're saying you might have felt that way?"
63. [Ai] "Heheh, what? Are you pressing me?"
64. [Naoya] "N-no...... it's not that......"
65. [Ai] "I really don't know. Maybe I would have, maybe I wouldn't......"
66. [Ai] "Either way, Ken'ichirou is gone......\nWhatever I felt, it's all in the past now."
67. [Naoya] "Well, that's true......"
68. [Ai] "Ken'ichirou-san had a strange charm about him.\nI'm sure he had no shortage of women interested......"
69. [Naoya] "Actually, no woman has a bad word to say about him......"
70. [Ai] "There you go again. Well, Ken'ichirou-san's way of life was dashing, but more than that, he was devoted. No woman speaks ill of a man like that."
71. [Naoya] "Devoted, huh...... True, I've heard the story of his romance with my mother many times."
72. [Ai] "Mm, Ken'ichirou-san never so much as glanced at another woman.\nEven after Mizuna-neesama died......"
73. [Ai] "Devoted, but every bit as stubborn. Ken'ichirou and Grandmother Kotoko both......"
74. [Ai] "It's thanks to that we were saved, though......"
75. [Naoya] "Those two, yeah. They're a little off. Their stubbornness is beyond belief."
76. [Ai] "Doesn't the same go for you, Naoya?"
77. [Naoya] "Me? No way. I live by flexibility."
78. [Ai] "Flexibility, huh......"
79. [Naoya] "What. What's with that weird little smirk......"
80. [Ai] "It seems the Nakamura family had unreleased paintings of Ken'ichirou's."
81. [Naoya] "Yeah, apparently......"
82. [Ai] "'Apparently'......"
83. [NARRATION] Ai studied my expression.
84. [NARRATION] I kept my face as calm as I could.
85. [NARRATION] Seeing that, Ai laughed.
86. [Ai] "No, it's nothing.\nNothing at all......"
87. [Ai] "But Naoya, too many things are lining up......\nEach member of the Natsume family has their own inner conflict about how to face that fact."
88. [Ai] "Even Shizuku working as an entertainer while still a student must be for that reason......"
89. [Naoya] "Huh? Is there some meaning to it?"
90. [Ai] "Who knows. What I can say is, she wouldn't do work like that for her own sake."
91. [Ai] "She's a girl with no attachment to money and no need for approval.\nFor her to enter the entertainment world, there must be some reason......"
92. [NARRATION] Some reason, huh......
93. [Ai] "More than that, the one it must weigh on most is Kei."
94. [Naoya] "Kei?"
95. [Ai] "His expression changed the moment he saw the six pieces of The Seven Aspects of the Sakura......\nI've lived with Kei all this time, but I've never seen him like that."
96. [Naoya] "Kei did......"
97. [Ai] "He acts vague, but when it comes to art he's remarkably sharp......\nHe must have felt something when he saw those works."
98. [Naoya] "I wonder what he felt......"
99. [Ai] "Ken'ichirou-san's return to Japan, and his battle with illness. Shizuku's return to the Natsume house.\nAnd above all, the unreleased works said to have been in the Nakamura family's collection......"
100. [Naoya] "You sound like you think all those events are connected somehow."
101. [Ai] "That's right. But what I think, I'll keep to myself."
102. [Ai] "Whether Kei can keep it to himself, though......"
103. [Ai] "Kei is a Natsume too. He looks carefree, but he's suffered a great deal.\nSo even when he feels something, he'll never say it aloud."
104. [Ai] "He'll show it through action."
105. [Naoya] "......Action, huh."
106. [Ai] "The Moore Exhibition is coming up soon, isn't it?"
107. [Ai] "For your sake, Kei will make his finest work."
108. [Naoya] "For my sake?"
109. [Naoya] "But I'm not entering the Moore Exhibition."
110. [Ai] "In that case, what will Kei do......"
111. [Naoya] "Won't he just paint it through without worrying about me?"
112. [Ai] "You think so? He might finish it,\nbut if it's him, I think he'll wait."
113. [Naoya] "Wait? For who?"
114. [Ai] "Until you come."
115. [Naoya] "For me to come?"
116. [Ai] "Just a feeling, but I think so.\nIn that sense, you can take your time to think it over......"
117. [Ai] "Because he'll wait for you, forever......"
118. [Naoya] "Wait forever......"
119. [Naoya] "It's just like......"
120. [Naoya] "The prince said to the little swallow,\n'You must go to the south now.'"
121. [Ai] "What's that? Is that The Happy Prince?"
122. [Naoya] "Yeah, good catch."
123. [Ai] "I'm a Japanese literature teacher. I can manage that much."
124. [Ai] "But if that's it, then what came next was this, wasn't it?"
125. [Ai] "Still the swallow said,\n'I will stay by your side, forever.'"
126. [Naoya] "If I were the prince, I'd force it to fly south."
127. [Naoya] "I wouldn't let a swallow with wings freeze to death......"
128. [Ai] "I imagine so. But just as stubbornly, Kei will stay by your side. Just like the swallow in The Happy Prince."
129. [Naoya] "Wilde's works are essentially homosexual.\nSo it's kind of gross. I won't allow that."
130. [Ai] "Really? What a shame. If it were you and Kei, I'd have blessed the union."
131. [Naoya] "Pff! Wh-what the hell!?"
132. [Naoya] "Wow...... that was pretty abrupt. You startled me......"
133. [Ai] "But you know, Kei really does love you, Naoya......"
134. [Naoya] "I'll pass, thank you."
135. [Ai] "I see. Well then, no need to worry about the two of you announcing a marriage.\nWhat a relief. What a relief."
136. [Naoya] "Of course not!"
137. [Ai] "In any case, the Moore Exhibition is soon, right?\nThen I'd like to make the two of you something nutritious, for once......"
138. [Naoya] "Something nutritious, huh.\nHmm, what would be good, I wonder."

=== lines=144 stop_reason=end_turn in=7030 out=4577 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. [Ai] "Fried rice, maybe?"
2. [Naoya] "Fried rice!? Th-that's not quite right, is it?"
3. [Ai] "Mm, that's true too......but whenever Ken'ichirou-san shut himself away to work, it was almost always fried rice. He said it was an all-purpose meal, since you could get vegetables and meat in it."
4. [Naoya] "What kind of half-baked nonsense...... That man had a hopelessly narrow repertoire in the first place......"
5. [Ai] "Is that so? Ken'ichirou-san couldn't cook?"
6. [Naoya] "Yeah, he was the classic Showa-era man. Couldn't do a single chore around the house."
7. [Ai] "Is that so...... Ken'ichirou-san said it with such confidence that I more or less took him at his word......"
8. [Naoya] "That idiot's like that, isn't he. What is it with that groundless self-assurance......"
9. [Naoya] "Sure, fried rice is convenient when you're working, but it's oily. And heavily salted. It's hardly nutritious."
10. [Ai] "Yes, exactly. Ken'ichirou told me that fried rice should be made not by stir-frying in oil, but with the mindset of deep-frying it."
11. [NARRATION] Told her, was it.
12. [NARRATION] I see. Ai apparently can't cook anything else, but I feel I've figured out why she's abnormally good at fried rice alone......
13. [NARRATION] Fried rice is a peculiar dish.
14. [NARRATION] Unthinkable levels of heat and oil compared to other dishes.
15. [NARRATION] Even I still can't get it quite right.
16. [Naoya] "Well, that said, Kei's working too, so fried rice might go over well."
17. [Ai] "Really? Then let's go with fried rice."
18. [Naoya] "Sure. In that case, I'll make the sauce, and you make the fried rice, Ai."
19. [Ai] "Sauce?"
20. [Naoya] "Ankake fried rice. That way we can get some vegetables in too, and it's easy to eat."
21. [Ai] "I see. As expected of you, Naoya."
22. [Naoya] "Of course. I'm a cut above my old man."
23. [Ai] "Bringing up Ken'ichirou-san even here.\nHonestly, the two of you are forever bristling at each other......"
24. [Naoya] "It's in the blood, isn't it? Neither of us could stand losing."
25. [Ai] "True. You father and son are both sore losers, and truly stubborn."
26. [Naoya] "I'll take that as a compliment."
27. [NARRATION] At the supermarket, we picked up not just today's ingredients but enough for the next few days.
28. [NARRATION] Groceries for several days for the Natsume household ended up being quite a load.
29. [Ai] "Right then, I'll take these home......"
30. [Naoya] "Huh? On the bike?"
31. [Ai] "Because it's the bike. The oversized bag I always carry converts into a side bag for the motorcycle. So it's fine even packed full."
32. [Naoya] "Is that so...... I did think it was awfully big for a shoulder bag......"
33. [Ai] "So feel free to say the word whenever you're going shopping. I can even prep a bigger side bag."
34. [Naoya] "No, no, we don't buy that much. It wouldn't fit in the fridge."
35. [Ai] "Well, I'll head back first."
36. [Naoya] "Yeah, see you shortly."
37. [NARRATION] Small-framed Ai threw her whole body into the kick-start and got the engine running.
38. [Naoya] "That's an awfully troublesome way to start an engine."
39. [Ai] "I'm light, so it might look that way, but old bikes are all like this."
40. [Naoya] "I see. Still, that engine's as loud as ever."
41. [Ai] "Yeah, this sound reminds me of all sorts of things. That's why I still love it."
42. [Naoya] "All sorts of things, huh......"
43. [Ai] "Well, I'll head back first."
44. [NARRATION] And with that, Ai was out of sight.
45. [Naoya] "Shopping with Ai. That's a rare occurrence......"
46. [NARRATION] All things considered, it was rather refreshing and fun......
47. [NARRATION] I ladled a scallion-and-ginger ankake sauce over the fried rice Ai had made.
48. [NARRATION] Scallions and ginger rank among the top three most nutritious of all ingredients.
49. [NARRATION] I'd also blended in garlic as a hidden touch, so all three of the great health-boosters were in there.
50. [Naoya] "Right, I'll take this over to Kei."
51. [NARRATION] When he's absorbed in a painting, he's not the type to come even if you call him for a meal.\nQuicker to bring it to him.
52. [NARRATION] My old man was the same way in that regard.
53. [Naoya] "Oi, Kei."
54. [NARRATION] I called out from in front of the storehouse.
55. [NARRATION] No answer.
56. [Naoya] "I'm coming in. All right?"
57. [NARRATION] I raised my voice and opened the storehouse door.
58. [Naoya] "Kei? Are you asleep?"
59. [NARRATION] No reaction from Kei at all.
60. [Naoya] "You are asleep......? Sheesh, at least sleep in your own room......"
61. [NARRATION] As I approached him--
62. [Kei] "Whoa! Y-you scared me!!"
63. [Naoya] "Y-you scared me. Why the sudden shout?"
64. [Kei] "I was listening to music."
65. [Naoya] "You were listening to music......?"
66. [Kei] "Yeah, listening to music to boost concentration is important, you know."
67. [NARRATION] The headphones tossed aside were blasting a suitably noisy song.
68. [Naoya] "You listen to something that loud to concentrate?"
69. [Kei] "I do."
70. [Naoya] "Personally, I'd recommend classical."
71. [Kei] "No good. That doesn't boost concentration, it just makes me sleepy."
72. [Naoya] "You wouldn't fall asleep to Beethoven's 'Fate.'"
73. [Kei] "How did that one go again?"
74. [Naoya] "Da-da-da-daaan! That one."
75. [Kei] "Ah, that. I dunno. Pieces like that go quiet partway through, don't they."
76. [Naoya] "Well, it's true it does get comparatively quiet from the second movement on......"
77. [Kei] "See, that kind of music doesn't suit me after all."
78. [Naoya] "What is it you're always listening to?"
79. [Kei] "What? Interested? But you'd know it, wouldn't you, Naoya?\nLike Mods."
80. [Naoya] "What's that? Something like a mop?"
81. [Kei] "No. Mods."
82. [Kei] "The culture around riding super cool bikes like Vespas and Lambrettas, the ones I ride."
83. [Naoya] "Is that so? What's the connection between bikes and music?"
84. [Kei] "It's a long story to explain...... well, if you're that curious about Mod culture, Naoya, I'll fill you in."
85. [Naoya] "No, no need, not interested."
86. [Kei] "Why not? Mods are cool!"
87. [Naoya] "Bikes and music, right? It's like Yokohama Gin*ae and biker gangs. Or that Ki*idan and delinquents kind of relationship."
88. [Kei] "No, that's different. I don't really know either of those, but they're definitely different."
89. [Naoya] "Why would you declare they're different when you don't know either?\nSame thing! This debate's over."
90. [Kei] "Ugh. Naoya, don't you have any taste in music?"
91. [Naoya] "Nothing in particular. I can't play any instruments."
92. [Kei] "I can't play any either."
93. [Kei] "Then how about punk? The Jam are cool. Mod Revival!"
94. [Naoya] "What kind of name is that, sounds like actual jam."
95. [Kei] "No, not like jam. It's Jam."
96. [Naoya] "You only listen to stuff with weird names, huh."
97. [Kei] "They're not weird! You're just too disinterested in the music scene, Naoya!"
98. [Naoya] "The music scene, huh. Yeah, I really am not interested......"
99. [NARRATION] Come to think of it, in that garage in New York, my old man used to blast the same sort of music......
100. [NARRATION] Do artists just love their volume cranked up......?
101. [Naoya] "Do you artists all like that ear-splitting stuff? Velvet......something-or-other."
102. [Kei] "The Velvet Underground. Oh, not bad taste."
103. [Naoya] "No, I haven't really listened to them."
104. [Naoya] "The Velvet Underground--wasn't Andy Warhol, the pop art guy, the one who backed them? So I just know the name."
105. [Naoya] "The jacket's famous too. That banana one Andy Warhol designed."
106. [Kei] "Yeah. Rock jackets often use artists' work. Sonic Youth used one of Gerhard Richter's candles."
107. [Naoya] "I know Gerhard Richter. Artist from the former East Germany. Famous for fetching the highest auction price of any living painter, too. But I don't know Sonic whatever."
108. [Kei] "Ugh...... you really have zero interest in rock."
109. [Naoya] "None...... my father loved noisy music, so I probably ended up preferring the quiet stuff in reaction."
110. [Kei] "What kind of music did Ken'ichirou-san listen to? Was it Mods stuff after all?"
111. [Naoya] "Like I said, I don't know these Mods you're going on about. Probably he was just playing whatever similar-looking albums were lying around."
112. [Kei] "Ah, similar-looking jackets. Then yeah, maybe that's what he was listening to."
113. [Kei] "A garage atelier in Chelsea, New York......\nA place like that would suit that kind of music."
114. [NARRATION] Well, the atmosphere does fit exactly, I suppose.
115. [Naoya] "What, you? Weren't you the one saying Ken'ichirou was no big deal? So you do care after all."
116. [Kei] "W-well, of course. He's that incredible a person. Of course I look up to him."
117. [Naoya] "Huh? You look up to that guy?"
118. [Kei] "B-but you know. You and I are going to be incredible artists ourselves someday.\nSo we can't lose, can we?"
119. [Naoya] "No, I'm thinking of becoming a civil servant in the future."
120. [Kei] "A c-civil servant!?"
121. [Naoya] "I want a stable career."
122. [Kei] "Wh-what. J-just now, for a second, you looked really lame, Naoya."
123. [Naoya] "What kind of eyes have you been looking at me with all this time. I've been like this from the start."
124. [Kei] "No, no way. Naoya, you're definitely going to be an incredible artist someday! I'm certain of it."
125. [Naoya] "Even if you're certain......"
126. [NARRATION] Truthfully, as I am now, I can't even touch Kei's heels......
127. [Naoya] "Anyway, whatever, just eat. It'll get cold."
128. [Kei] "Ah, right. I'll dig in."
129. [NARRATION] Kei shoveled the fried rice in.
130. [Kei] "Delicious. Delicious. Man, Naoya, you really are good at cooking. If only the Natsumes had a little of that talent......"
131. [Naoya] "What are you talking about. Ai's the one who made that fried rice."
132. [Kei] "Oh, come on, you're not fooling me. There's no way sis could make something like this."
133. [NARRATION] ......No, she did.
134. [NARRATION] What, does Kei not know that Ai is bizarrely good at fried rice, and only fried rice?
135. [Naoya] "Believe it or don't, that's up to you, but Ai can cook properly."
136. [Kei] "I don't believe it. When I first came to this house she made me fried rice, but it was practically soot......"
137. [NARRATION] Ah, I see. So Ai didn't become good at it right away after my old man taught her, either.
138. [NARRATION] Years after being taught, it was still soot when she first served Kei. Then, over an even longer stretch of time, she gradually got better......
139. [NARRATION] If that's the case, then that flavor makes sense......
140. [Kei] "Come to think of it......\nUmm......"
141. [Naoya] "Umm? What are you on about?"
142. [Kei] "Ah, no...... never mind."
143. [Naoya] "What is it. Hesitating like that isn't like you."
144. [Kei] "I have my moments."

=== lines=144 stop_reason=end_turn in=7147 out=4733 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. [Naoya] "Really? I haven't really noticed......"
2. [Kei] "How do I put it...... I didn't realize it until I saw the painting......"
3. [Naoya] "Until you saw the painting?"
4. [Kei] "Yeah, honestly, I was scared the whole time, deep down, for the longest time...... That's why I was always saying prickly things to you."
5. [Kei] "Somewhere along the way...... it started to seem like you were living while shielding your right hand, Naoya."
6. [NARRATION] Reflexively, I hid my right hand.
7. [Naoya] "Shielding...... wh-why would I do that?"
8. [Kei] "No. There's no particular reason. And anyway, it's fine now. I saw that painting and I was convinced."
9. [Naoya] "What painting?"
10. [Kei] "That you really are amazing after all, Naoya. So from now on I'm going to paint like my life depends on it."
11. [Kei] "It's a bit much to say this, but...... honestly, I don't really care about the Moore Exhibition."
12. [Kei] "Sorry to Makoto, but I have no interest in winning the Moore Exhibition or anything like that."
13. [Naoya] "Interest or no interest, there's no way anyone could win that thing. It'd be like a student taking the Nobel Prize or the Fields Medal."
14. [Kei] "You think? I didn't get that impression."
15. [Kei] "Not after being shown something like that......"
16. [Kei] "For me, so long as it gives you a pretext to paint, Naoya, anything is fine."
17. [NARRATION] I couldn't say anything.
18. [NARRATION] I understand full well what Kei is trying to say.
19. [NARRATION] Probably, Kei is speaking after having seen the six-part Seven Aspects of the Sakura.
20. [NARRATION] But that thing is nothing but a forgery.
21. [NARRATION] It is not my own work.
22. [NARRATION] And the very method by which it was made is entirely counterfeit.
23. [NARRATION] I merely assembled that painting through an artificial contraption.
24. [Kei] "What are you making that solemn face for?"
25. [Kei] "Don't take it so heavily. I mean, this is just what I think on my own, and I know deep down I can't force it on you."
26. [Kei] "Even so. I'll wait as long as it takes. So it doesn't have to be now."
27. [Kei] "I want to paint with you, Naoya. That alone is enough for me."
28. [Kei] "No matter how long it takes."
29. [Kei] "But hey, we're geniuses, right? So if the two of us really push each other, we'll probably end up world-class artists. Can't really help it, huh. Ahahahaha."
30. [Naoya] "It's not that sweet."
31. [Kei] "No way, if it's you and me, we can do it."
32. [Naoya] "I watched my old man my whole life. Even he was a struggling artist forever. His talent was the real thing. Even so, the world doesn't grant recognition that easily."
33. [Naoya] "The artist Kusanagi Ken'ichirou faced the greatest turning point of his life -- the death of his beloved wife -- and completed 'The Reclining Sakura.'"
34. [Naoya] "A despair beyond imagining is what made him bring forth that god-touched work."
35. [Naoya] "For him, the most precious thing in his life, the thing he had to protect at any cost, was Kusanagi Mizuna. Kusanagi Ken'ichirou became an artist only for her sake."
36. [Naoya] "And yet, ironically, when the very object of that purpose was lost and only the art -- which had been nothing but the means -- remained, only then did he become a world-class artist."
37. [Naoya] "Art is a cruel thing."
38. [Naoya] "Dreams devour people. And the devoured dreams ripen into the fruit called art."
39. [Naoya] "The ripened fruit falls to the earth and nourishes people."
40. [Naoya] "Without knowing what sort of fruit it even is, people praise only its sweetness."
41. [Naoya] "That is what the Moore Exhibition you're all aiming at really is."
42. [Kei] "Yeah, I get it. That it's not that simple......"
43. [Naoya] "So even if we compete against each other, it's not something we can easily do anything about."
44. [Kei] "Maybe it's not simple, but the possibility isn't zero, is it?"
45. [Naoya] "Well, the possibility, sure......"
46. [Kei] "Then we can do it!"
47. [Naoya] "We can do it...... huh."
48. [NARRATION] I let out a bitter smile.
49. [NARRATION] "Ah, or rather, if it's you, maybe......"
50. [NARRATION] "There's no such possibility for me, though......"
51. [NARRATION] I wanted to say that, but the words wouldn't come.
52. [Kei] "Maybe it's true that Ken'ichirou-san only reached the summit of the world after he lost Mizuna-san, someone irreplaceable to him."
53. [Kei] "But if it's the two of us, we'll manage somehow."
54. [Naoya] "Heh, you're the only one who says such stupid things......"
55. [Kei] "It may be stupid. But to accomplish something as absurd as reaching the summit of the world, you can't afford to stay clever."
56. [Naoya] "I see. Every now and then you say something that sounds the part."
57. [Naoya] "It's true, to accomplish something absurd, one probably has to become an idiot......"
58. [NARRATION] The artist called Kei possesses a rare and extraordinary talent.
59. [NARRATION] Indeed, that talent might well hold its own on the world art scene.
60. [NARRATION] Perhaps one day he'll receive an award said to sit at the very summit of the world.
61. [NARRATION] Even so, it won't be with me.
62. [NARRATION] Unlike Kei, I have lost my wings.
63. [NARRATION] I can't soar freely across the canvas with a brush the way he can.
64. [NARRATION] I know that painfully well.
65. [Naoya] "Little swallow, little swallow. The cold, cold winter is coming soon. So you must fly south......"
66. [Naoya] "It's nothing."
67. [Kei] "What? What? Are you inviting me on a graduation trip to some tropical island? Even though the Natsume household is this broke -- so that means you're counting on the Moore prize money, right!"
68. [Naoya] "Hahahahaha! If I were going to a tropical island, there's no way I'd take a loudmouth like you! If I go, you're absolutely off the list."
69. [Kei] "Why! Why do you have to say such awful things! Naoya!"
70. [Naoya] "It's business as usual. Don't mind it."
71. [Kei] "You could try being nice to me once in a while, you know?"
72. [Naoya] "Nope."
73. [Kei] "Tch."
74. [Naoya] "But, the world, huh...... That kind of stupid dream isn't so bad either."
75. [Naoya] "At the very least, when my old man was just a part-time instructor, no one back then imagined he'd become a world-class artist."
76. [Naoya] "Naturally, the man himself was fully intending to become one."
77. [Kei] "Yeah, sounds like the kind of person Kusanagi Ken'ichirou was."
78. [Naoya] "So I don't dislike it when you say stupid things like that."
79. [Kei] "Yeah, I know. That that's the kind of guy you are, Naoya."
80. [NARRATION] Kei laughed heartily.
81. [Kei] "Even wandering off course can become fuel for moving forward."
82. [Kei] "No, I mean, the very force that drives you forward can also send you flying backward."
83. [NARRATION] Saying that, Kei handed me a single album.
84. [Kei] "A song I recommend. The track 'Sunflower' is cool."
85. [Naoya] "Sunflower, huh......"
86. [Naoya] "Well, I don't really like noisy songs, but I'll borrow it for now."
87. [Kei] "Yeah, definitely give it a listen. It's my favorite song. It's the 'Modfather.'"
88. [Naoya] "Oh, is that so......"
89. [Kei] "That's a weak reaction."
90. [Naoya] "Come on, hurry up and finish. I'm taking the dishes when you're done."
91. [Kei] "Eating in a rush is bad for your health, you know!"
92. [Naoya] "Yes, yes, understood, so no more chatter."
93. [Kei] "It's not chatter......"
94. [NARRATION] Kei polished off the rest of the fried rice.
95. [Naoya] "Oh!?"
96. [Ai] "How was Kei doing?"
97. [Naoya] "Comparatively lively."
98. [Ai] "I see. I hope he doesn't push himself too hard. He's the type who loses all sense of proportion once he throws himself into something."
99. [Naoya] "Maybe so. Once he gets absorbed in one thing, he loses sight of everything else."
100. [Ai] "Come to think of it, Ken'ichirou-san was like that too."
101. [Naoya] "The old man, huh......"
102. [Ai] "Before he moved to the Sakuragahara apartment, whenever he came back to Japan he'd always paint in that atelier."
103. [Ai] "I often carried the meals Mizuna-neesama made."
104. [Naoya] "I knew my old man painted in that atelier, but back then Ai was the one bringing the meals...... somehow that's funny."
105. [Ai] "You were in this house too, you know. Though you'd only just been born."
106. [Naoya] "No, I remember. I lived in this house until I was four. Granny Natsume was still alive back then."
107. [Ai] "You remember? Those days were lively and fun. You were here, and Mizuna-neesama, and Grandma Kotoko, and Ken'ichirou would come home now and then."
108. [Naoya] "It's true, it was lively back then."
109. [Ai] "So when you came back to this house again, I was really, truly happy."
110. [Naoya] "I see. Well, it just happened to work out that way, after the boating accident......"
111. [Ai] "Ugh...... about what Kei did, I really am sorry."
112. [Naoya] "I'm joking. Don't worry about it. Without that kind of pretext, I probably wouldn't have come back here."
113. [Ai] "Pretext?"
114. [Naoya] "Yeah, that's right. A pretext. This house is too full of memories...... I think it's too comfortable, and I had the feeling that once I moved back, I wouldn't be able to return to that apartment anymore......"
115. [Naoya] "So I hesitated a little."
116. [Ai] "That apartment is a precious place too. It's the place for you and Mizuna-neesama...... no, Mizuna-san."
117. [Ai] "But when I invited you to come to this house, the thought of us living together again made me happy somehow."
118. [Naoya] "Yeah, and I'm not a kid anymore. Cradling my head like that."
119. [Ai] "Ah, that was...... how do I put it...... it just happened."
120. [Naoya] "I'm not a kid anymore, so don't do that kind of thing. The feeling of your chest was really, uh, tangible."
121. [Ai] "T-tangible!? What do you mean by that!"
122. [Naoya] "You probably don't realize it, Ai, but you've grown too, you know? When I was a kid, your chest was completely flat."
123. [Ai] "D-don't call it completely flat! Th-there's a little something."
124. [Naoya] "Right. There is now. That's what I meant by tangible."
125. [Ai] "Huh? M-my chest? R-really?"
126. [Naoya] "That's right. I could subtly feel it, and it made me happy."
127. [Ai] "H-happy!?"
128. [Naoya] "That kind of thing -- I'm a young man too, you know. Be careful."
129. [Ai] "Q-quit saying weird things...... Normally you don't get happy about your sister's chest. When you say happy, you mean it in the sibling-skinship sense, right?"
130. [Naoya] "If we were blood-related, that might apply, but since we're not blood-related, it doesn't."
131. [Naoya] "No matter how much you were like an older sister to me long ago, you and I aren't related by blood."
132. [Naoya] "In that case, that distinctive feel of your chest -- it could well stir lust in me."
133. [Ai] "Th-there you go again...... there's no way you'd feel lust for someone like me, Naoya."
134. [NARRATION] Without a word, I stepped closer to Ai.
135. [NARRATION] Sensing the unsettling movement, Ai stepped back.
136. [NARRATION] But I closed the distance at once.
137. [Ai] "Huh? N-Naoya...... um......"
138. [NARRATION] Ai was cornered against the wall.
139. [NARRATION] I did that thing they call a kabe-don, pinning Ai between my arms.
140. [Ai] "Uh, um...... N-Naoya......"
141. [Ai] "Huh? Um...... what exactly is going on here?"
142. [Naoya] "You're cute, Ai. I'm just pressing my advantage."
143. [Ai] "Huh!? I-I'm cute!? No, no, please stop with the jokes."
144. [Naoya] "Want to test whether it's a joke or not?"

=== lines=79 stop_reason=end_turn in=3983 out=1768 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. "T-test!?"
2. "Ai, close your eyes......"
3. "Huh? Huh? Huuuh? Huh!?"
4. "I'll say it again. Close your eyes."
5. "Close your eyes......"
6. "U-um, you know. I'm a teacher, and you're a student, aren't you?"
7. "Yeah, that's right. But close your eyes."
8. "No, that's exactly why it's no good."
9. "Understood. But close your eyes."
