1. The days pass by.
2. Their pace has been steadily accelerating since I was a child.
3. They say that twenty is the halfway point of life, or something like that.
4. If that's true, then in a few more years, my life will be at its halfway mark, too, I suppose.
5. I had a conversation like that with my father while he was still alive.
6. The way time moves changes depending on your environment.\nThere's no such thing as time that flows the same for everyone.
7. That's why the world has this thing called a "clock" -- so that everyone can share the same time. That's what he said.
