115. See, that's why I hate it.\nWhat is it with these people.
116. Over 70, over 80 -- to me it sounds like the age of an old man...\nAn utterly alien world...
117. "You lot who can study abnormally well, are you supernatural or something?"
118. "Nothing like that. It's because we've been studying properly since childhood."
119. That's what I hate -- capable people say things like that with a straight face.
120. For the time being, I resolved to glue myself to my desk again today and study.
121. Looking at the clock, it was past one.
122. "About time I got to sleep."
123. No matter how hard I push myself, I want at least five hours of sleep.
124. Any less than that and efficiency really does drop.
125. "Sheesh, I haven't spent this long stuck on one thing since I was a kid drawing pictures..."
126. "Though even so, this is a lot easier than back then..."
127. In that period, I was pouring an insane amount of time into painting.\nDay after day, sketching, sketching, sketching.
128. Looking from outside, sure, I might have seemed like a prodigy, but there aren't many people that age spending that much time on painting.
129. And it was the genuine article, trained by my father, no less.\nOf course I'd end up painting things you wouldn't believe a kid had done.
130. "Come to think of it, that guy I met in the library today said something..."
131. "'As we suspected, guys like you are different from the ground up,' huh..."
132. I denied it in the moment, but where painting in particular is concerned, he was right.
133. I had lived through an abnormal childhood.
134. Idly, I looked out at the garden.
135. "The atelier lights are still on..."
136. Or rather, I've never actually seen them off.
137. "Kei must be working really hard..."
