100. "Ai, what exactly do you think a confession is?"
101. "Huh? It's when someone you like says they like you... right?"
102. "That means it's when the person you like says they like you, doesn't it?"
103. "Yes, that's right. Didn't you say the same thing, Naoya?"
104. "That's what I mean! That! It's the bad influence of that old woman of the Natsume house, isn't it! A confession counts even when it comes from someone you don't like!"
105. "Huh? I-is that so?"
106. "That old woman takes single-mindedness as her creed, and brainwashes the whole clan that way... honestly..."
107. "So even when someone just says they 'like' you, that counts?"
108. "But if that's the case, something's a bit off."
109. "By that logic, about a third of the times someone has told me they like me have been women..."
110. "Well... yeah... that sort of thing does happen, I guess..."
111. As good as she is at martial arts, of course she'd be popular with girls too...
112. "The premise is wrong to begin with, but I'll say this just in case.\nYou're beautiful, and you've surely been popular before, and even I catch myself seeing you as a woman more than enough."
113. "Oh come on now, that can't be true."
114. "Everyone in the Natsume family has well-arranged features. Didn't you tell me that with Kei included, the three of you were called the beautiful three sisters of the neighborhood?"
115. "No, that was just flattery."
116. "If you're going to say something that idiotic, I really am going to live inside your skirt."
117. "U-um, listen... it's true that I was in the wrong, but... this really isn't good..."
118. "You're the one who did it twice."
119. "Th-that's true, but... but I get embarrassed too, you know..."
120. Ai turned bright red and averted her eyes.
121. I've known Ai since way back.
122. So I know full well how beautiful she is.
123. I set things back to how they were.
124. "Th-thank goodness... I really did think you were going to stay inside forever."
125. "Of course not. That was just a little mischief..."
126. "But I'll say it again -- remember this.\nYou're plenty cute, Ai, and there's a strong chance I'll become aware of you as a member of the opposite sex."
127. "So try to be careful that doesn't happen."
128. "Yeah -- there's no telling when my reason might just fly out the window."
129. "What happens when your reason flies out the window?"
130. "I'd probably jump you."
131. "In that case, I'll fight you off properly."
132. "Please do -- even if I say something crazy."
133. "Something crazy?"
134. "No, how do I put it... some careless thing said in the heat of the moment, like 'I love you'..."
135. "Would you really say something so important carelessly, Naoya?"
136. "That's what I'm saying! Fight me off! If I blurt out something like that, it's just raving nonsense!"
137. "I see, raving nonsense... understood. I'll take it to heart."
138. "But if that did happen, it would be my first confession..."
139. "What is that supposed to mean?"

=== lines=137 stop_reason=end_turn in=6912 out=4713 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. [Ai] "Ah, no, it's nothing. Ahahaha..."
2. [NARRATION] Late at night, after I had finished studying.
3. [NARRATION] I stood alone in the atelier.
4. [NARRATION] I fitted that brush into the spring holder and faced the canvas.
5. [NARRATION] But the brush wouldn't move at all.
6. [NARRATION] In that state, I stood rooted to the spot for hours on end.
7. [NARRATION] In the end, unable to lay down a single stroke,\nI set the brush down where I stood.
8. [???] "Did you truly paint it with that method?"
9. [NARRATION] I turned toward the voice, and there stood Nagayama.
10. [Naoya] "Since when? Have you been there?"
11. [Kana] "I went to school, went home once, ate dinner, took a bath, thought about various things, and then came back."
12. [Naoya] "Didn't you go home this morning, fed up with my mediocrity?"
13. [Kana] "Yeah, well, that's part of it, I guess... Even if you paint with that method, Kusanagi-kun, you can't produce anything worthwhile."
14. [Naoya] "What is it? Did you come all this way just to snipe at me?\nWhat an annoying woman."
15. [Kana] "I thought that afterwards, Kusanagi-kun would probably paint again by himself... so I came."
16. [Naoya] "And if I did?"
17. [Kana] "I thought that when you paint alone, you paint in earnest."
18. [Naoya] "So this morning wasn't serious..."
19. [Kana] "Yeah, that could only be seen as performance.\nAs an insistence that you can't paint..."
20. [Naoya] "I see. But if I were the kind of person who'd go that far to insist I can't paint, I wouldn't paint alone either, would I?"
21. [Kana] "That's not true. I think the current Kusanagi-kun, if left alone, would paint seriously."
22. [Naoya] "Why do you think that?"
23. [Kana] "Because Kusanagi-kun has fallen to the level of an ordinary person..."
24. [Naoya] "Fallen to the level of an ordinary person, huh...\nIt's a fact, but hearing it spelled out again is pretty infuriating."
25. [Kana] "Nagayama Kana is an artist. Well, an amateur, but with that sort of thing, whoever says it first wins."
26. [Kana] "Nagayama Kana has been painting ever since she was a child. It's been a life like an insect's, on and on, but only when I was painting -- only inside that -- was I able to shine."
27. [Kana] "Until I met you."
28. [Naoya] "You were saying the same sort of thing yesterday..."
29. [Kana] "Ordinary people are different from geniuses."
30. [Kana] "Geniuses paint freely, as if they had received a revelation from heaven.\nWhen something they want to paint appears, they give it form."
31. [Kana] "But ordinary people are different."
32. [Kana] "Ordinary people are desperate to hide the fact that they are ordinary, so they work hard not to fail, not to slip up."
33. [Kana] "When I told you, Kusanagi-kun, that you could just paint with the spring holder, you had the eyes of an ordinary person through and through."
34. [Kana] "Really junk eyes. Those are eyes I know well."
35. [Kana] "On the contrary, when you did that sketch in the croquis book to flaunt your own junkiness -- that had far more of the majesty of a genius..."
36. [Naoya] "Are you trying to say your eye for the real thing isn't just for show?"
37. [Kana] "Who knows. In this case, I think it's just because I understand the species called 'ordinary person' painfully well."
38. [Kana] "To be honest, even I'm confused..."
39. [Naoya] "Confused?"
40. [Kana] "A genius like you has fallen to the level of an ordinary person.\nIf I can confirm that, I can move forward..."
41. [Kana] "I won't have to keep cowering at the shadow of you -- that absolute being who stole my world away..."
42. [Kana] "But just as much as that... I also feel a sense of loss."
43. [Kana] "I don't know what this sense of loss is...\nAll I know is that I hate whoever it was that took that right hand away..."
44. [Kana] "I hate whoever trampled on that magnificent talent..."
45. [Kana] "I want to find that person and ruin their life."
46. [Kana] "I even have feelings like that in me."
47. [Naoya] "If you ever did that, I'd kill you."
48. [Kana] "I'm sure you would... That's the kind of person you are."
49. [Kana] "Your talent lives in such a precarious place.\nIt's terribly fragile..."
50. [Kana] "That's why you lost such an irreplaceable talent so easily..."
51. [Kana] "You -- your very existence -- disturbs my heart even further...\nAnd I want to forget about you and go far, far ahead..."
52. [Naoya] "Then forget about me and go far ahead.\nBesides, the shadow of me you're imagining is nothing more than something you built up on your own..."
53. [Naoya] "As long as you can convince yourself, my shadow should vanish in an instant..."
54. [Kana] "Do you really think it's that simple... idiot..."
55. [Kana] "No, you're right, Kusanagi-kun. I'll forget about you."
56. [Kana] "The artist called Kusanagi-kun is dead. That's all there is to it."
57. [Kana] "There's inner conflict, of course... but that outcome is the more desirable one for me."
58. [Kana] "You're giving up, aren't you?"
59. [Naoya] "That's what you'd prefer, isn't it?"
60. [Kana] "Yes. I'd be glad if you just sank away as you are."
61. [Kana] "But, as a senior ordinary person, let me give you some advice."
62. [Kana] "Ordinary people have their own way of doing things."
63. [Naoya] "Their own way of doing things?"
64. [Kana] "Talent betrays the ordinary,\nbut technique does not."
65. [Kana] "A system of technique earned through effort -- that is the ordinary person's weapon.\nEven an ordinary person's blade can sometimes reach a genius's throat."
66. [Kana] "A person of talent possesses techniques that can bewilder a genius.\nBecause a person of talent is, at heart, an ordinary person."
67. [Kana] "The act of painting -- an almost infinite repetition of it.\nThat is the only way an ordinary person can surpass a genius."
68. [Kana] "Though, right now, Kusanagi-kun, you are neither."
69. [Kana] "You've abandoned painting altogether... so you're neither a genius, nor a person of talent, nor an ordinary person.\nBut isn't that fine?"
70. [Kana] "For me, I'm happy if even one talent greater than my own disappears from the world..."
71. [NARRATION] I grabbed Nagayama's hand.
72. [Kana] "Um... I have no interest in you as you are now, so I'd rather you didn't casually touch me..."
73. [Kana] "Why are you silent?\nAre you angry, perhaps?\nOr are you sad, and want me to comfort you?"
74. [Kana] "Either way, could you try someone else?\nYou're a celebrity now, Kusanagi-kun -- there must be any number of girls willing to do that sort of thing."
75. [Naoya] "Help me."
76. [Naoya] "You barged in this far.\nSo see my struggle through to the end with me!"
77. [Kana] "I-I don't understand. Why do I have to keep company with your struggle? A-and besides, as I said, I want you to disappear just as you are..."
78. [Naoya] "Hah!? You're the one who came clinging to me in the first place! And now, because you've lost interest, you're just going to disappear? Like hell that flies!"
79. [Kana] "Ugh... K-Kusanagi-kun, were you always this kind of person?"
80. [Naoya] "You're right about everything."
81. [Naoya] "I've probably been running away.\nMy right hand is nothing more than a pretext."
82. [Naoya] "Or maybe I've been clinging to the past, back when I could paint.\nJust dragging along the glory of that time, pretending to have chosen 'not painting' as an option."
83. [Naoya] "What you said is correct."
84. [Kana] "I-is that so. Well then, please just accept it and sink away as you are."
85. [Naoya] "But listen, Nagayama, there's one enormous thing you've got wrong."
86. [Kana] "Got wrong?"
87. [Naoya] "I hate to lose. Once I've been made to face where I am now, I can't just leave things this way."
88. [Kana] "Don't say that. Just go 'plop' and sink already.\nHonestly, I much prefer the Kusanagi-kun who doesn't paint."
89. [Naoya] "Because it's convenient for you."
90. [Kana] "Of course. Though when I say 'prefer,' I don't mean romantically."
91. [Naoya] "Well, that suits me fine. Same here."
92. [Kana] "U-um, listen. If you're asking someone for their cooperation, shouldn't you at least offer a little flattery?"
93. [Naoya] "What, would you be happier if I said you were a romantic prospect?"
94. [Kana] "It's not that... but how do I put it... you're a little off, Kusanagi-kun."
95. [Naoya] "There's a certain genius."
96. [Kana] "A certain genius?"
97. [Naoya] "Yeah. That's probably the only talent Kusanagi Ken'ichirou ever acknowledged.\nWithout a doubt, his disciple."
98. [Kana] "Kusanagi Ken'ichirou's disciple? Such a person exists?"
99. [Naoya] "Yeah. I'll introduce you."
100. [Kana] "Kusanagi Ken'ichirou's disciple..."
101. [Naoya] "Tomorrow, midnight,\ncome to Yumihari Academy."
102. [Kana] "Th-that's rather sudden, isn't it?"
103. [Naoya] "I'm going to face off with that genius."
104. [Kana] "Face off!? Huh? Like, a brawl or something?"
105. [Naoya] "Are you an idiot. As if I'd do something that dangerous.\nOf course, a duel with paintings."
106. [Kana] "With paintings? You, as you are now? Against that genius?"
107. [Kana] "Ahahaha, no, you really should stop... I've been watching all along, and Kusanagi-kun, you're completely junk. I don't think you can possibly compete with a genius like that."
108. [Naoya] "If you're watching and you think that, then feel free to call off the match at any time. But make sure you see it through to the end."
109. [Kana] "Is 'I don't go' one of my options?"
110. [Naoya] "Basically, it's a request."
111. [Kana] "But, Nagayama, you've had that uninterested look on your face for a while now, and your eyes are shining."
112. [Kana] "Huh? My eyes?"
113. [Naoya] "Yeah. Ever since you heard 'a talent Kusanagi Ken'ichirou acknowledged,' the color of your eyes changed."
114. [Kana] "Heh, even down and out, you're still Kusanagi Naoya.\nYour powers of observation aren't just for show."
115. [Kana] "A face-off with a genius, huh... that certainly does sound interesting.\nUnderstood. Tomorrow night, correct?"
116. [Kana] "But can you tune yourself up by tomorrow?"
117. [Naoya] "Tune up?"
118. [Kana] "The time to get your painter's instincts back."
119. [Naoya] "I don't need that. You said an ordinary person needs an almost infinite repetition, didn't you?"
120. [Naoya] "As for that, I've done more than you have any right to lecture me about."
121. [Naoya] "I may have broken my brush,\nbut even so, I never stopped practicing the art of painting."
122. [Kana] "So even if you weren't producing works, you kept up your practice without fail..."
123. [Naoya] "Yeah, so I don't need any tune-up.\nAs long as I can find Sui, that's enough."
124. [Kana] "Find, you say... Is she someone hard to find?"
125. [Naoya] "Yeah, she's extraordinarily elusive."
126. [Kana] "I see... sounds exactly like a talent with a story behind it."
127. [Kana] "Understood. I'll go along with it."
128. [Kana] "Because if I see you lose miserably, the shadow that has possessed me might just disappear."
129. [Naoya] "As if I'd lose so easily."
130. [Kana] "Heh, what am I even trying to do."
131. [Kana] "You disappearing ought to be my wish...\nAnd yet, helping you..."
132. [Kana] "How idiotic..."
133. [Naoya] "Of course it's idiotic.\nIf you were smart, you couldn't be an artist."
134. [Kana] "Heh... hehehehe... maybe, maybe that's true..."
135. [Kana] "I see, if you were smart, you couldn't be an artist... maybe so."
136. [Kana] "I'll look forward to tomorrow."
137. [NARRATION] With that, Nagayama left the atelier.

=== lines=136 stop_reason=end_turn in=4830 out=3075 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. I kept painting until morning.
2. I just kept painting.
3. That guy told me:
4. "You have the eyes of an ordinary man."
5. Strangely, those words became my salvation.
6. "The ordinary man has an ordinary man's way of doing things."
7. "Nagayama was right about that."
8. Early in the morning, without having slept, I headed to school.
9. And there, alone on the rooftop, I gazed at the sky.
10. A painting showdown with Sui, huh......
11. Now that I've said it......, will I even be able to find him?
12. Even supposing I do find him......, \nis a showdown with him something that could actually come about?
13. If he really is the genius my old man made him out to be, there's a strong chance I'll finish without being able to do anything at all.
14. "Then again, the story was that it might be Rin......"
15. Well, the details don't matter.
16. As long as Sui is the real thing, that alone is enough.
17. To reach Kei, my opponent has to be at least that caliber.
18. "That guy...... he's going to undergo an absolutely staggering evolution......"
19. "He'll reach heights no one else can touch......"
20. "Hyah!?"
21. Something cold against my cheek.
22. I sprang up.
23. "W-who's there!?"
24. "You're up early......"
25. "Here, catch. Cold coffee."
26. Ai tossed the canned coffee lightly toward me.
27. I caught it.
28. "Ah, thanks."
29. "Figured you'd want some caffeine, no?"
30. "The light in your atelier was on all night, it seemed......"
31. "You were up too, Ai?"
32. "It was on my mind a little......\nSo, Naoya -- have you decided to paint again?"
33. Ai looked up at the sky.
34. "Everyone loves to paint, don't they."
35. "Kei, Naoya...... and Ken'ichirou too......"
36. "Long ago, Ken'ichirou painted all sorts of things for me."
37. "And I loved it -- loved it more than I could bear."
38. "Things that exist in this world, things that don't...... he'd paint all kinds of things for me......"
39. "Whenever I said thank you, Ken'ichirou would always say the same thing back."
40. "A painting is born again through the one who sees it.\nIf no one sees it, it might as well not exist......"
41. "So, thank you for looking at it -- that's what he'd say."
42. "I imagine Ken'ichirou painted plenty of paintings no one ever saw......"
43. "Just like you do, Naoya."
44. "Paintings aren't only the ones that meet the public eye.\nActually, the ones that never do probably outnumber them."
45. "Sketches, studies...... an endless-seeming trial and error to bring forth a finer work."
46. "Those have no audience."
47. "That's precisely why my old man understood so well how important an audience is."
48. "From the bottom of his heart, he must have been thinking 'thank you' to you, Ai."
49. "Paintings that no one is shown, huh......"
50. "Kei, you see......\nHe's the way he is, but he's who I look up to."
51. "That guy just keeps painting, like a man possessed."
52. "Inside his head there's nothing but painting.\nYou could say he lacks even common sense...... that's a bit of a problem, though."
53. "Painting isn't something you get better at just by putting in the volume."
54. "A hundred sketches an ordinary man dashes off easily can't come close to a single sketch a genius wrings out of himself in anguish."
55. "A painting without anguish is nothing but pleasure.\nThat sort of thing belongs to the realm of hobby......"
56. "He looks like a carefree guy, but from his paintings you can feel anguish."
57. "There's a kind of terrible force in his paintings -- like he's shaving off his own life to express something."
58. "Sketches born of that kind of anguish. Their seemingly infinite repetition......"
59. "He's a man who was practically born to paint."
60. "He's staking his life on it."
61. "And isn't that the same for you, Naoya?"
62. "I've been putting on this air like I don't paint, but\ninept as I am, I've been drawing sketches like a man obsessed."
63. "So no one would see me...... I never let a day of practice slip."
64. With this left hand......
65. Because the last of my right hand's strength I used up back then......
66. "Even so, I don't catch up."
67. "Even when I think I've moved beyond him, I can always see his back ahead of me.\nHe's always one step ahead."
68. "Kei said the very same thing, you know."
69. "That's just him overestimating me."
70. "I wonder. It doesn't look that way to me......"
71. "No, every last one of you overestimates me......"
72. "You're still drawing sketches......\nSo then why do you pretend you've quit painting, Naoya?"
73. "There are various reasons."
74. "But in fact you're still painting."
75. "It's only practice. However far it goes, it stays as studies."
76. "I haven't left behind anything you could call a work."
77. "So the fact that I've quit painting -- that's the truth."
78. "That part is no lie."
79. "But I'm going to bring forth a work now."
80. "One that won't lose even to Kei's...... a painting like that."
81. "I've decided, so I can't back down now......"
82. "I have to......  take up the brush again......"
83. "You're trembling...... Why?"
84. "I'm not trembling...... well, I won't claim I'm not......"
85. "You look excited...... Is there something you're afraid of?"
86. "I-I'm not afraid......"
87. "Always putting on a brave face...... Every one of you Kusanagi people, without exception......"
88. "W-what's this...... you hugged me because I was trembling?"
89. "Yeah. I know you well, Naoya."
90. "Ever since you were a kid, you had a fierce refuse-to-lose streak.\nEven with adults you wouldn't flinch."
91. "But whenever you made that face, you were always trembling, ever so slightly......"
92. "Whenever you were about to challenge something, whenever you were about to face something head-on, you were always trembling."
93. "You carry yourself bravely no matter what, as though you don't know fear."
94. "To most people, that must look like a hero with absolute strength......"
95. "An invincible hero who stands against any hardship......"
96. "But to me, you only ever look like someone still trying to take flight, wounded, with his wings torn off......"
97. "Every time you fight, Naoya, you get hurt......"
98. "Maybe I've had a longing for that kind of thing since I was little."
99. "The super-hero who sweeps in and solves everything."
100. "The hero who overturns any hardship...... that kind of hero."
101. "But it's not that simple."
102. "The only ones allowed that are the heroes inside stories."
103. "Reality is different."
104. "If a mere human keeps acting the hero, of course he loses all sorts of things......"
105. "People aren't built to be omnipotent like that......"
106. "So there's plenty you can only protect by losing something in return......"
107. "Unlike the heroes in stories, the heroes possible in the real world are so terribly fragile -- that's what I think."
108. "Watching my old man made me think so......"
109. "His too was a life of nothing but losing."
110. "Even after he'd lost the most precious thing, he kept on fighting."
111. "So I decided I'd take up his will......"
112. And so The Seven Aspects of the Sakura was born.
113. "Old lady Natsume said this."
114. "In her youth, her life was one of nothing but being taken from......"
115. "So now, she does the taking...... from villains."
116. "Those are words she can only say because hers was a life of being taken from."
117. "If a human is going to mimic what is not human, he needs to pay a price."
118. "Without a price, it can't be done."
119. "That, I know better than anyone......"
120. "So...... of course I tremble......"
121. "It's always like this when I make a decision......"
122. "My legs shake. It feels like I can't take that one step forward."
123. "That's exactly why I always take the step."
124. "Because once I do, the trembling stops......"
125. Ai held me tightly.
126. "Naoya...... isn't it about time you stopped needing to fight?"
127. "You've fought well enough up to now."
128. "Even losing all sorts of things, you kept fighting all the same, didn't you."
129. "You tremble because you're afraid......"
130. "Once in a while, listen to that feeling......\nYou don't have to shoulder everything. You don't have to answer to every single thing."
131. "Yeah, I tremble partly out of fear......"
132. "But you know, people tremble when they're excited, too."
133. "Fear and excitement are blended together."
134. "So it's not just me pushing myself......"
135. Ai wore a sad expression, then said quietly:
136. "I see...... yeah, that's true."

=== lines=140 stop_reason=end_turn in=5960 out=3401 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. "I figured that would be your answer......"
2. "Even so, I'll say it as many times as it takes. It's all right to fold your wings and rest whenever you like.\nThat's what I'm here for......"
3. "What do you mean...... 'what you're here for'......"
4. "I was entrusted with you -- by Ken'ichirou, by grandmother Kotoko......"
5. "So lean on me as much as you like......\nI'd be happier that way, too."
6. "Still, to think you saw me that way, Ai......"
7. "Was I really trembling......?\nWell, I suppose you're right about that......"
8. "I've watched you all this time. I know you better than you know yourself."
9. "That's going too far."
10. "Yeah, that was overstating it......\nStill, at heart, that's how well I mean to know you......"
11. "But hey, Ai."
12. "If you understand me so well, then --\nlike I told you before, quit hugging me like this......"
13. "Yeah, you're right. But I can't just leave you alone while you're trembling."
14. "If you're trembling all by yourself, I'll hold you and make that trembling stop......"
15. "Damn it...... when you say things like that, it's hard to shoot back with a dirty joke......"
16. "You don't need to shoot back with something like that. You're an idiot in the strangest ways."
17. "No, if I don't at least crack a dirty joke......"
