113. [Sui] "The one who makes Kei-san's brilliance shine even brighter is you, and the one who makes your paintings shine even brighter is Kei-san."
114. [Sui] "So just paint with peace of mind."
115. [Naoya] "Thanks......"
116. [Sui] "The contest is over."
117. [Sui] "It was fun."
118. [Naoya] "Yeah. Well, honestly, for me the feeling of pain was greater."
119. [Sui] "It was the same for Sui. That's what creation is."
120. [Naoya] "Well then -- let's clean up the pool before we get chewed out!"
121. [Kana] "W-wait, are you really going to erase a painting like this?"
122. [Kana] "N-no, you can't. A wonderful work like this......"
123. [Naoya] "Can't be helped. It's painted with watercolor. Either way, it wasn't going to last long."
124. [Kana] "B-but......"
125. [Sui] "Come, come, we're going to wash it all away in grand style. And the moment of washing it away is beautiful too!"
126. [Kana] "W-wait! At least give me time to take a photo with my phone!"
127. [Naoya] "How you spray the water matters too. Come on, let's savor the beauty of the scattering as well!"
128. [Kana] "Hey, wait, listen to me! Idiot!"
129. [NARRATION] 　With a hose, we washed away the newborn painting.
130. [Kana] "A-a masterpiece like that...... with no record left of it......"
131. [NARRATION] 　We washed away the newborn painting.
132. [NARRATION] 　What a waste, and yet it felt bold and refreshing.
133. [Sui] "This is fun."
134. [Sui] "But from here on, it won't just be fun."
135. [Naoya] "It wasn't just fun up to now, either......"
136. [Sui] "No, I suppose it wasn't......"
137. [NARRATION] 　By the time we'd washed it all away, the first trains had begun to run.

