1. After that, I simply kept painting.
2. Using everything I had, I filled the canvases one after another.
3. Sometimes with my left hand. Sometimes with my left hand assisted by a spring--\nI didn't cling to any one method, and used every means available in pursuit of a finer completion.
4. Many paintings were finished.
5. But none of them satisfied me.
6. What I could do now.
7. The paintings I could paint now.
8. I kept pushing them to the limit.
9. Then, one night.
10. Just like that time before, she came.
11. "You're really at it, aren't you."
12. "Well, yeah..."
13. "What did you come for?"
14. "No particular reason.\nI just figured you'd be painting..."
15. "For the record, what you're doing is trespassing."
16. "Even if you lecture me with common sense, I won't listen..."
17. "Don't get so high and mighty..."
18. "That's just the kind of person I am."
19. "Don't play it off like that... geez."
20. "You've started running again, haven't you... Kusanagi-kun."
21. "Who knows. I'm just painting right now. That's all."
22. "Aren't you submitting to the Moore Exhibition, Nagayama?"
23. "Me? Please, don't be ridiculous."
24. "I know my own ability. I really hate\nthat 'commemorative attempt' kind of thing."
25. "That's a total denial of every art club member Yumihari Academy has ever had."
26. "Yes, I hate that sort of thing. Besides, the Moore Exhibition isn't something students can win in the first place."
27. "I only move when I can win for certain."
28. "And to win, I'll use any means necessary."
29. "So, Kusanagi-kun..."
30. "If you're going to do it, please win for sure,\nand don't disillusion me."
31. "I'd like to hope so."
32. "But there's nothing that's for certain.\nAll I can do is push what I'm capable of to the maximum."
33. "So, Nagayama.\nThank you."
34. Nagayama smiled softly.
35. "I only ever loved my own world of brilliant color."
36. "You appeared, and that world was lost.\nAnd even when you were gone, I couldn't get those colors back."
37. "If I can defeat you at your full revival, then perhaps, once again, I might see my own world."
38. "I still think that way now."
39. "So there's no reason for you to thank me."
40. "Because someday, I will defeat you."
41. "I only lent a hand for that purpose."
42. "Yeah. I hope that splendid world of painting returns to you."
43. "Honestly, that's the kind of thing you say when you don't consider me a threat at all."
44. "What? I just said it from the heart."
45. "I'd like to make you feel a little bit of anxiety too."
46. "I see, maybe so. But then paint an incredible picture, would you."
47. "I'll paint even if you don't tell me to. And in the end, I'll crush you all and stand at the top."
48. "Right. Well, I'm looking forward to it."
49. "Such a flippant reply... Well, it can't be helped. As I am now..."
50. "At my current level, the prep school told me the Arts University is going to be tough."
51. "Well, that place is difficult, after all."
52. "But it starts once I've cleared that."
53. "For someone aiming to be an artist, that's a reasonable goal."
54. "That's right. Well, that's how it is..."
55. "Well then, I think I'll be heading home..."
56. "Seriously, what did you come here for?"
57. "Ah, that painting--you don't want it?"
58. Nagayama pointed at the pile of canvases I'd scattered about.
59. "Ah, this? Yeah, I don't need it.\nI didn't like it, so I was about to paint it over white and reuse the canvas."
60. "That's it. Might I have a little reward for helping you out?"
61. "Wh-what!? Thirty thousand yen now, at this point!?"
62. "That's true. Thirty thousand yen might be nice too..."
63. "B-but that was only if I couldn't hold my own against Sui, and technically it ended in a draw."
64. "Then let me have that one painting."
65. "Huh? A painting?"
66. "Yes, that landscape with the moon visible over the town... would you give it to me?"
67. "Well, sure, but what are you going to do with a painting of mine?"
68. "No particular reason.\nI just want to receive the moon from you."
69. Nagayama held up my painting.
70. "It's a good painting..."
71. "Really? It's a piece of junk."
72. "Maybe... but it's a good painting..."
73. "What's that supposed to mean..."
74. "Even about paintings... there are things you don't understand."
75. "More than that, if this is junk, then you can paint far, far better pictures."
76. Nagayama Kana laughed.
77. I only realized afterwards that the painting was the scenery visible from the Yumihari Academy pool.
78. On the last day of summer vacation, the view from there had been beautiful, so I'd captured it in a photograph.
79. In the photograph it was a new moon, but somehow I'd changed it to a full moon...
80. A full moon... come to think of it, the night Sui and I had our contest was a full moon too...
81. After that, I just kept painting.
82. A painting greater than any I had ever painted.
83. I kept my brush in hand until the very last moment time allowed.
84. It must have been the same for Kei.
85. He too, I'm sure, painted right up until the final moment.
86. That was what I thought when I completed my last painting.
87. The Moore Open Exhibition deadline day.
88. At long last, I had finished my own work.
89. My comeback piece as Kusanagi Naoya.

