80. [NARRATION] I stepped up onto the stage.\nApplause broke out.
81. [NARRATION] The spotlight fell on the work.
82. [NARRATION] At the same time, my piece was projected onto the display set up on the stage.
83. [NARRATION] In that instant, the venue fell utterly silent.
84. [NARRATION] A soundless stage.
85. [NARRATION] Even the emcee was at a loss for words.
86. [NARRATION] It wasn't a bad reaction.
87. [NARRATION] This kind of silence is what you feel when you've seized people's hearts...
88. [NARRATION] A theater has no need for a single feeling of hesitation.
89. [NARRATION] This is that kind of work.
90. [MC] "Th-this really is a painting of tremendous impact...\nFor a moment I was so taken by it that I... forgot I was the emcee. Ahaha..."
91. [NARRATION] The emcee's laughter finally brought the venue back to its senses.
92. [NARRATION] Laughter could be heard here and there.
93. [NARRATION] Many of the people there must have been feeling the same thing as this emcee.
94. [MC] "Um, so... this is it, isn't it. A swarm of butterflies crossing the sea. My, what an amazing swarm... such extraordinary force."
