136. [Friedman] "But precisely because it is alternative, this land was long kept in isolation from Western art."
137. [Friedman] "That, however, changed six years ago."
138. [Friedman] "Six years since Kusanagi Ken'ichirou-shi received his award."
139. [Friedman] "This land has, once again, rejoined the West."
140. [Friedman] "Arts that had walked separate paths have met once more."
141. [Friedman] "That has since manifested in the form of an increase in Japanese laureates at the Moore."
142. [Friedman] "Truly, right now, art is erasing its borders and about to give rise to a new surge."

=== lines=145 stop_reason=end_turn in=6238 out=3120 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. "And in that lies the intimation of a new generation's rise."
2. "That intimation -- yes, that is precisely Natsume Kei-shi, who has become the youngest recipient in history."
3. "He is the new generation that will bear the art of the days to come."
