51. 　Friedman raised his voice in a way I had never heard from him before.
52. 　That painting was rendered in a fantastical manner.
53. 　The more fantastically it was painted, I thought, the more vividly the real thing that is death would come into relief.
54. 　Countless butterflies crossing the sea.
55. 　Their beating wings are aimed somewhere far away.
56. 　Just where that "somewhere" is, no one knows.
