82. 　So he was unhurt too.
83. 　Just some grazes from when he leapt off, nothing more.
84. 　And so the Kei I saw --
85. 　There was no external injury anywhere,\nit truly looked as though Kei had merely lost his soul.
86. 　And so,\nit seemed as though that soul,\ntoo, would easily come back.
87. 　Not just me.\nEveryone thought so.
88. 　Only the doctor,\nmercilessly, conveyed Kei's death.
