1. 　We griped to each other about our workplaces.
2. 　Yumihari Academy in particular was somewhere Wakata had also worked, so he had the same sort of complaints.
3. 　The conversation flowed easily.
4. "Oh, that reminds me..."
5. 　As if suddenly remembering, Wakata murmured.
6. "That booze I gave you way back, remember?"
7. "Booze? Ah, that domestic single cask, you mean."
8. "Did you drink it?"
9. "Drink the whole thing?"
10. "No, there's still a little left..."
11. "I see, a little left, huh..."
12. "Yeah, just a little..."
13. "Been sipping at it bit by bit?"
14. "No, that's not it. There was one time I went on a real bender with it..."
15. "Ever since, I've had no thought of opening that bottle again."
16. "No thought of opening it, huh...\nI see..."
17. "When exactly is the moment of happiness, I wonder?"
18. "Say you buy some special booze. Something really expensive."
19. "You figure, I'll open this on some special day. Some extra-special day, right?"
20. "Whiskey especially -- it keeps well."
21. "But what counts as a special day?"
22. "Beats me. Like, a wedding, maybe?"
23. "On a day like that, you pop the venue's own champagne, don't you?"
24. "True... uh, some kind of anniversary, then?"
25. "If it's an anniversary that comes around once a year, then the 'specialness' of the bottle is only worth about a year."
26. "Now that you mention it, yeah..."
27. "So what's the ultimate special day? The best day of your life?"
28. "In your case, going from part-time to full-time was one, right?"
29. "On a day like that, y'know, it's got a celebration-drink kind of feel -- you end up drinking out. Usually at a bar."
30. "Ah, yeah... I kind of get that."
31. "For a celebration drink, having something other than cheap malt beverage at a bar feels more the part, and when the day actually comes, that's what you end up doing."
32. 　I see -- if something worth celebrating comes along, you wouldn't quietly open your treasured bottle at home. You'd just go out drinking as usual.
33. "So where is the special moment, really?"
34. "Then isn't it when you're out drinking something that isn't cheap malt beverage?"
35. "That might well be the right answer, but it means the special bottle never gets opened."
36. "I see. That might be true."
37. 　I took the bottle Wakata had given me down from the cupboard.
