135. [Headmaster] "Director Inoue of the hospital is also feverish about contemporary art, so being left out in the cold while things move forward may not sit well with him."
136. [Naoya] "Is that how these things work?"

=== lines=76 stop_reason=end_turn in=4262 out=2285 cache_read=3222 cache_create=0 last_entry_continued=0 ===
1. [Headmaster] "The thing about rich people, you see -- what they treasure most is their pride."
2. [Naoya] "Pride?"
3. [Headmaster] "That's right. The rich actually have less attachment to money than ordinary people. Maybe because they have so much of it that they can't tell whether they've gained or lost."
4. [Headmaster] "Instead, what they hate most is having their pride wounded. Even a small slight against their face, they'll hold onto forever."
5. [Headmaster] "This time too, Director Inoue may not be too pleased inside. 'Why didn't they bring this to me first!' -- that sort of thing."
6. [Naoya] "When will Bourbagi's graffiti be released to the press?"
7. [Headmaster] "We've already received an explanation from Bourbagi, so there's no need to make it a criminal matter. Well, I imagine the owners, Bourbagi, and probably the Moore Foundation's intentions all get tangled up in that part."
8. [Naoya] "Will there be a gap of a few days?"
9. [Headmaster] "Right. It'll be a few days."
10. [NARRATION] I stub out my cigarette.
