8. [Ai] "For now, until you get married, I'll take proper care of you.\nAs a teacher, I'm your senior too."
9. [Ai] "Well then, shall we head home soon?\nBack to our house......"
10. The cherry blossoms were still in bud.
11. The footsteps of spring were drawing nearer, but spring itself was still a little way off.
12. The two of us walked down Yume-no-Ukisaka.
13. From here you could take in the whole town of Yumihari at a glance.
14. The sun was still high.\nBut in a few hours it would set.\n&
15. And when it did, the lights of this town would come on.
16. The night view of Yumihari is beautiful, just like scattered cherry blossoms.
17. Perhaps that is because in each single petal, in each single light,\nthere is the life of a person.
18. A single petal is beautiful too.\nBut still, it is more beautiful when surrounded by countless other petals.
19. The karmic lanterns of people's connections.
20. The karma of countless people kindles the light.
21. Our house, too, is one of those lights.
22. The Natsume residence.
23. Within it lie the feelings of many people, and the pasts of many people.
24. Natsume Kotoko.
25. Kusanagi Ken'ichirou.
26. Kusanagi Mizuna.
27. Natsume Shizuku.
28. Natsume Kei.
29. And\nNatsume Ai.
30. No -- Kusanagi Naoya.\nI, too, am one of them.
31. So many things happened in that house.
32. Memories beyond counting.
33. Good ones\nand bad ones.
34. All of it is packed into that place.
35. That's why -- we're going back there.
36. It's not that I ever stood still.
37. It's not that I ever stopped walking.
38. Here, in this place, I have walked my own life.
39. As I looked up at the sky, thinking such things,\nAi said, "We really have been walking, you know."
40. From here on, let's walk together, the two of us.
41. Slowly, the two of us......
42. A road that stretches on and on, without end.
43. And down that road, we walk slowly.
44. Watching me like that,\n&
45. Ai smiled gently.
46. And at that moment, faintly, I heard the Song of the Sakura.

